{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggyDfbK6ivR1xK38Dmrf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MEHD2nz2g2P2y9VaUvFw61","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/.cache/x8de669-research/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff && head -60 API-INDEX.md && grep -n -i \"outfit\\|hair\\b\\|hair:\\|'long'\\|ponytail\\|skirt\\|swim\\|female\\|feminine\\|bust\\|curv\\|figure\\|hips\\b\" API-INDEX.md | head -60","description":"Read the index header and search for character outfit options"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7314,"cache_read_input_tokens":132301,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7314},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"99d4115e-ac85-4844-bf9c-39009e8f9714","uuid":"7eea60be-b3c3-4177-8e55-f40c889545af","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:50:21.614Z","request_id":"req_011CggyDfLh3Nmpvc4pMJJZU","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01MEHD2nz2g2P2y9VaUvFw61":{"command":"cd /home/micha/.cache/x8de669-research/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff && head -60 API-INDEX.md && grep -n -i \"outfit\\|hair\\b\\|hair:\\|'long'\\|ponytail\\|skirt\\|swim\\|female\\|feminine\\|bust\\|curv\\|figure\\|hips\\b\" API-INDEX.md | head -60","description":"Read the index header and search for character outfit options"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MEHD2nz2g2P2y9VaUvFw61","type":"tool_result","content":"# my-3D2dge API index (v0.85.2)\n\nEvery public name in `engine/my-3d2dge.js` and its modules (`engine/modules/`: a section each, after the core's), one line each: its signature (and default, for a field) and what its doc comment says (a long one's options on lines of their own: `new E.Game({ expand })`). Written by `node tools/api-index.mjs` from the engine itself; `doctrine-check` fails when a public name has no description here. Search it for a name; `API.md` and the agent edition's header are the overviews. † marks a name the agent edition (`my-3d2dge-agent.js`) doesn't have.\n\n## Units and the height rules\n\n| Quantity | Unit |\n| --- | --- |\n| Distances, positions, sizes in the world | world units: one floor tile is 16; x east, y south, z up |\n| Speeds, gravity | world units per second, per second squared |\n| Time, `dt` | seconds (`dt` is one fixed step: 1/120 s of real time times `game.timeScale`) |\n| Angles, `facing`, `dir` | radians: 0 east, π/2 south (a direction may also be a ground vector `[dx, dy]`) |\n| Screen positions | pixels of the game's own low-resolution buffer (`game.screen.W` × `H`) |\n| Colors | `'#rrggbb'` strings |\n\n- A body's `z` is its feet. A cell's top is `map.height(cx, cy)`: 0 on the floor; a wall is solid from 0 up to its `h`.\n- A body stands on the highest top within `z + 2` under its footprint (`E.HEIGHTS.step`, `Body.step`).\n- Eyes are at `z + 30` and a target is seen at `z + 22` (`E.HEIGHTS.eye`, `chest`; a body's own `eye` and `chest` override them).\n- Two things are on the same level when `|dz| <= 8` (`E.HEIGHTS.level`), unless a call says otherwise.\n- Collision, standing, sight (`map.sight`, `map.ray`), reach (`E.targets`, `E.inArc` with `dz`) and navigation (`E.FlowField`) all follow these rules. `E.dist` is 3D; `E.overlap` is flat.\n\n## Examples\n\nEach runs in `tools/contract-test.mjs`.\n\n```js headless\n// a game with no display, in Node or a test: fixed steps, scripted input, its state\nconst E = My3D2dge, game = new E.Game({ headless: true, res: 'snes' });\nconst hero = new E.Body({ x: 40, y: 40, r: 5 });\ngame.start({ update(dt) { hero.vx = game.input.move()[0] * 80; if (game.input.pressed('jump')) hero.jump(210); hero.update(dt); }, draw() {} });\ngame.input.hold('right'); game.input.tap('jump');\ngame.advance(0.25);   // 30 fixed steps of 1/120 s, at once\nif (!(hero.x > 55 && hero.z > 20)) throw new Error('the hero should run right and be in the air');\ngame.dispose();\n```\n\n```js heights\n// a guard on a roof, a hero in the street: sight, reach and a climb read heights the same way\nconst E = My3D2dge, map = new E.TileMap({ rows: ['#######', '#.....#', '#..RR.#', '#######'], legend: { '#': 1, R: 2 }, types: { 1: { h: 80 }, 2: { h: 40 } } });\nconst guard = { x: 56, y: 40, z: 40, facing: Math.PI }, hero = { x: 36, y: 40, z: 0, r: 5 };\nif (!map.sight(guard, hero)) throw new Error('eyes on a roof see down into the street');\nif (E.targets(guard, [hero], { range: 60 }).length) throw new Error('not on the same level: no melee target');\nconst up = map.ledge(hero, 0);   // east, toward the roof\nif (!up || up.z !== 40) throw new Error('a ledge to climb onto the roof');\n```\n\n## Contents\n\nThe line each section starts on, and the name its classes' instances go by: `E.Attack: slash` lists its members as `slash.start`.\n\n- 108 The engine object (E = My3D2dge)\n- 119 Math\n- 194 Pixel primitives\n- 213 Sprite frames, turns and swaps\n- 219 Views (projections); E.View: view\n- 246 Screen; game.screen\n- 268 Input; E.Input: input\n- 353 Pixel font\n- 364 Lighting; game.lights\n- 383 Particles; E.Particles: game.particles\n100:- 1573 Module road: the pseudo-3D road: segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, roadside scenery, tunnels (engine/modules/road.js); E.Road: road\n141:- `E.ease`: easing curves for u 0..1: linear, outQuad, inQuad, inOut (inOutQuad), outCubic, outBack (it overshoots a little more than Penner's: 1.9), and the rest of Penner's set (sine, quad, cubic, back, elastic and bounce, each in, out and inOut: inSine, outSine, inOutSine, ...), the names every tween library uses (section 1b)\n603:- `new E.Path(points, o = {}) → path` †: new E.Path(points, { closed: false, smooth: null }): points [x, y, z] (z optional) or { x, y, z } (a side view's height is z); closed runs back to the first; smooth: 'catmull' curves through every point (Catmull-Rom); at(d), nearest(x, y, z), draw(r) below\n666:- `new E.Humanoid(o = {}) → rig`: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.3, build, weapon, outfit, hair, hat, sleeves, armor, hood, cape, colors, ... }): a character rig posed from math every step (API.md, \"Characters\", lists the options); update(dt, state) each step, draw(g, ox, oy, view) inside r.actor. hat: 'cap' | 'band' | 'crown' | 'helmet' | 'pointed' (or { style, color }); hood: true (drawn in colors.hair)\n669:- `rig.drawPortrait(g, x, y, size = 40, o = {})` †: a close-up bust for dialog boxes and menus, drawn live from the rig (blinks, hair and hats included): rig.drawPortrait(g, x, y, 40, { zoom: 3, turn: .6, bg: '#1a2050', frame: true }) // inside r.overlay(g => ...) zoom: pixels per world unit (3 = face fills the frame), turn: 0 = facing you, .6 = three-quarter. The bust stays upright while the rig kneels or lies down (upright: false shows the real pose); cape: false hides the cape; tint: '#808080' greys it out (a KO'd party member).\n677:- `rig.update(dt, s = {})`: s: { x, y, z, vx, vy, facing, dash, hurt, attack, air, point } air: true while jumping or falling (legs tuck), point: true to hold the weapon hand forward (aiming a gun) attack: { spec, phase: 'wind' | 'active' | 'recover', u: 0..1 }. spec.kick = true swings the right foot instead of the hand also aim (radians up), crouch, sprint, climb, hang (hangZ: the top it hangs from, above the feet), flip: 0..1 (a roll), pose: 'cheer' | 'cast' | 'guard' | 'kneel' | 'crouch' | 'wave' | 'hips' | 'down' | 'die' | 'block', stance: 'guard' | 'ready', down: 0..1, vz (with climb: the climbing speed), land: k (a heavy landing), expr: 'smile' | 'shout' | 'angry' | 'wince', run: 0..1 (run in place)\n679:- `rig.C`: its colors (skin, hair, cloth, pants, boot, belt, cape, capeIn, metal, hilt, eye, ...), the defaults with o.colors over them; change one and it shows at the next draw\n693:- `rig.o`: its options, with the build's proportions and the defaults filled in (size, build, weapon, outfit, ...; legUpper, torso, headR and the other lengths are at size 1)\n695:- `rig.poseW`: held poses: 'cheer' (item get, victory), 'cast' (both hands forward), 'guard' (fists up), 'kneel', 'crouch', 'wave', 'hips' (hands on hips), and down: 0..1 (knocked flat). stance: 'guard' (fists up while moving) | 'ready' (weapon held forward)\n1094:- `E.SHAPES: barrel, crate, chest, table, chair, stool, bench, bed, bookcase, shelf, pot, jar, sack, cart, ... (25)`: the shapes by id: { about, tags, mats: { slot: material }, parts | make(params), params, foot, lights, flames } (the core library's, the sets' as 'SET:id' from E.addAssets, and your own: E.SHAPES.stool = {...})\n1096:- `E.materialTile(id, o = {})`: a material's pattern as a tile of pixels, for a 3D renderer's texture: E.materialTile(id, { size: 32 (world units square: it repeats every size; a face pattern's whole face), px: 2 (pixels a unit), lid: false (true: as on a face looking up), curved (as on a turned face), band: 2 (the light: 0 dark .. 4 bright) }) -> { w, h, rgba (Uint8ClampedArray, top row first, v up the tile) }; null for an unknown material\n1099:- `E.shapeMesh(id, o = {})`: a shape's triangles, for a 3D renderer (the 3D engine's world.shape): E.shapeMesh(id | entry, { params, mats, seg }) -> { groups: [{ mat, key, lid, curved, face, pos, nrm, uv }], bounds [x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1] } in the entry's own units and frame (z up, its front +y, its own scale applied: place it with the placement's facing, scale and flip). The same parts as r.shape draws; null for an unknown shape\n1101:- `E.shapeMesh() → groups`: each one's mat (the material ready to draw: E.material's), key (its id), lid (true: the faces looking up or down, which some patterns draw their own way), curved (turned or round faces: planks run up them), face (a pattern drawn once per face, the crate's sides and bark's ends: uv runs 0 to 1 across each face), pos, nrm, uv (Float32Arrays: three numbers a corner, three corners a triangle; uv two a corner, world units across the surface)\n1516:- `physics.arc(x, y, r, a0, a1, o = {})`: a curved rail: a chain round (x, y) at radius r from angle a0 to a1 (radians; o.n segments)\n1573:## Module road: the pseudo-3D road: segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, roadside scenery, tunnels (engine/modules/road.js)\n1576:- `road.add(n, o = {})`: n segments more, bending (curve) and climbing (hill: units up, - down), eased in and out; o.tunnel, o.colors\n1578:- `road.curveAt(z)`: how hard the road bends at a distance\n1588:- `road.segs = []`: its segments ({ i, z, y0, y1, curve, tunnel, colors, things })\n1621:- `new E.RPG(o = {}) → rpg`: new E.RPG({ items, monsters, status, curve }): the rules of a role-playing game (the manual above)\n1633:- `rpg.curve`: curve(lv): the experience level lv needs in all (15 x (lv - 1) ^ 2.4 by default)\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174749__x8de669/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"99d4115e-ac85-4844-bf9c-39009e8f9714","uuid":"b9103c9e-e1a3-4c42-8d7a-f541421584c3","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:50:21.636Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# my-3D2dge API index (v0.85.2)\n\nEvery public name in `engine/my-3d2dge.js` and its modules (`engine/modules/`: a section each, after the core's), one line each: its signature (and default, for a field) and what its doc comment says (a long one's options on lines of their own: `new E.Game({ expand })`). Written by `node tools/api-index.mjs` from the engine itself; `doctrine-check` fails when a public name has no description here. Search it for a name; `API.md` and the agent edition's header are the overviews. † marks a name the agent edition (`my-3d2dge-agent.js`) doesn't have.\n\n## Units and the height rules\n\n| Quantity | Unit |\n| --- | --- |\n| Distances, positions, sizes in the world | world units: one floor tile is 16; x east, y south, z up |\n| Speeds, gravity | world units per second, per second squared |\n| Time, `dt` | seconds (`dt` is one fixed step: 1/120 s of real time times `game.timeScale`) |\n| Angles, `facing`, `dir` | radians: 0 east, π/2 south (a direction may also be a ground vector `[dx, dy]`) |\n| Screen positions | pixels of the game's own low-resolution buffer (`game.screen.W` × `H`) |\n| Colors | `'#rrggbb'` strings |\n\n- A body's `z` is its feet. A cell's top is `map.height(cx, cy)`: 0 on the floor; a wall is solid from 0 up to its `h`.\n- A body stands on the highest top within `z + 2` under its footprint (`E.HEIGHTS.step`, `Body.step`).\n- Eyes are at `z + 30` and a target is seen at `z + 22` (`E.HEIGHTS.eye`, `chest`; a body's own `eye` and `chest` override them).\n- Two things are on the same level when `|dz| <= 8` (`E.HEIGHTS.level`), unless a call says otherwise.\n- Collision, standing, sight (`map.sight`, `map.ray`), reach (`E.targets`, `E.inArc` with `dz`) and navigation (`E.FlowField`) all follow these rules. `E.dist` is 3D; `E.overlap` is flat.\n\n## Examples\n\nEach runs in `tools/contract-test.mjs`.\n\n```js headless\n// a game with no display, in Node or a test: fixed steps, scripted input, its state\nconst E = My3D2dge, game = new E.Game({ headless: true, res: 'snes' });\nconst hero = new E.Body({ x: 40, y: 40, r: 5 });\ngame.start({ update(dt) { hero.vx = game.input.move()[0] * 80; if (game.input.pressed('jump')) hero.jump(210); hero.update(dt); }, draw() {} });\ngame.input.hold('right'); game.input.tap('jump');\ngame.advance(0.25);   // 30 fixed steps of 1/120 s, at once\nif (!(hero.x > 55 && hero.z > 20)) throw new Error('the hero should run right and be in the air');\ngame.dispose();\n```\n\n```js heights\n// a guard on a roof, a hero in the street: sight, reach and a climb read heights the same way\nconst E = My3D2dge, map = new E.TileMap({ rows: ['#######', '#.....#', '#..RR.#', '#######'], legend: { '#': 1, R: 2 }, types: { 1: { h: 80 }, 2: { h: 40 } } });\nconst guard = { x: 56, y: 40, z: 40, facing: Math.PI }, hero = { x: 36, y: 40, z: 0, r: 5 };\nif (!map.sight(guard, hero)) throw new Error('eyes on a roof see down into the street');\nif (E.targets(guard, [hero], { range: 60 }).length) throw new Error('not on the same level: no melee target');\nconst up = map.ledge(hero, 0);   // east, toward the roof\nif (!up || up.z !== 40) throw new Error('a ledge to climb onto the roof');\n```\n\n## Contents\n\nThe line each section starts on, and the name its classes' instances go by: `E.Attack: slash` lists its members as `slash.start`.\n\n- 108 The engine object (E = My3D2dge)\n- 119 Math\n- 194 Pixel primitives\n- 213 Sprite frames, turns and swaps\n- 219 Views (projections); E.View: view\n- 246 Screen; game.screen\n- 268 Input; E.Input: input\n- 353 Pixel font\n- 364 Lighting; game.lights\n- 383 Particles; E.Particles: game.particles\n100:- 1573 Module road: the pseudo-3D road: segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, roadside scenery, tunnels (engine/modules/road.js); E.Road: road\n141:- `E.ease`: easing curves for u 0..1: linear, outQuad, inQuad, inOut (inOutQuad), outCubic, outBack (it overshoots a little more than Penner's: 1.9), and the rest of Penner's set (sine, quad, cubic, back, elastic and bounce, each in, out and inOut: inSine, outSine, inOutSine, ...), the names every tween library uses (section 1b)\n603:- `new E.Path(points, o = {}) → path` †: new E.Path(points, { closed: false, smooth: null }): points [x, y, z] (z optional) or { x, y, z } (a side view's height is z); closed runs back to the first; smooth: 'catmull' curves through every point (Catmull-Rom); at(d), nearest(x, y, z), draw(r) below\n666:- `new E.Humanoid(o = {}) → rig`: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.3, build, weapon, outfit, hair, hat, sleeves, armor, hood, cape, colors, ... }): a character rig posed from math every step (API.md, \"Characters\", lists the options); update(dt, state) each step, draw(g, ox, oy, view) inside r.actor. hat: 'cap' | 'band' | 'crown' | 'helmet' | 'pointed' (or { style, color }); hood: true (drawn in colors.hair)\n669:- `rig.drawPortrait(g, x, y, size = 40, o = {})` †: a close-up bust for dialog boxes and menus, drawn live from the rig (blinks, hair and hats included): rig.drawPortrait(g, x, y, 40, { zoom: 3, turn: .6, bg: '#1a2050', frame: true }) // inside r.overlay(g => ...) zoom: pixels per world unit (3 = face fills the frame), turn: 0 = facing you, .6 = three-quarter. The bust stays upright while the rig kneels or lies down (upright: false shows the real pose); cape: false hides the cape; tint: '#808080' greys it out (a KO'd party member).\n677:- `rig.update(dt, s = {})`: s: { x, y, z, vx, vy, facing, dash, hurt, attack, air, point } air: true while jumping or falling (legs tuck), point: true to hold the weapon hand forward (aiming a gun) attack: { spec, phase: 'wind' | 'active' | 'recover', u: 0..1 }. spec.kick = true swings the right foot instead of the hand also aim (radians up), crouch, sprint, climb, hang (hangZ: the top it hangs from, above the feet), flip: 0..1 (a roll), pose: 'cheer' | 'cast' | 'guard' | 'kneel' | 'crouch' | 'wave' | 'hips' | 'down' | 'die' | 'block', stance: 'guard' | 'ready', down: 0..1, vz (with climb: the climbing speed), land: k (a heavy landing), expr: 'smile' | 'shout' | 'angry' | 'wince', run: 0..1 (run in place)\n679:- `rig.C`: its colors (skin, hair, cloth, pants, boot, belt, cape, capeIn, metal, hilt, eye, ...), the defaults with o.colors over them; change one and it shows at the next draw\n693:- `rig.o`: its options, with the build's proportions and the defaults filled in (size, build, weapon, outfit, ...; legUpper, torso, headR and the other lengths are at size 1)\n695:- `rig.poseW`: held poses: 'cheer' (item get, victory), 'cast' (both hands forward), 'guard' (fists up), 'kneel', 'crouch', 'wave', 'hips' (hands on hips), and down: 0..1 (knocked flat). stance: 'guard' (fists up while moving) | 'ready' (weapon held forward)\n1094:- `E.SHAPES: barrel, crate, chest, table, chair, stool, bench, bed, bookcase, shelf, pot, jar, sack, cart, ... (25)`: the shapes by id: { about, tags, mats: { slot: material }, parts | make(params), params, foot, lights, flames } (the core library's, the sets' as 'SET:id' from E.addAssets, and your own: E.SHAPES.stool = {...})\n1096:- `E.materialTile(id, o = {})`: a material's pattern as a tile of pixels, for a 3D renderer's texture: E.materialTile(id, { size: 32 (world units square: it repeats every size; a face pattern's whole face), px: 2 (pixels a unit), lid: false (true: as on a face looking up), curved (as on a turned face), band: 2 (the light: 0 dark .. 4 bright) }) -> { w, h, rgba (Uint8ClampedArray, top row first, v up the tile) }; null for an unknown material\n1099:- `E.shapeMesh(id, o = {})`: a shape's triangles, for a 3D renderer (the 3D engine's world.shape): E.shapeMesh(id | entry, { params, mats, seg }) -> { groups: [{ mat, key, lid, curved, face, pos, nrm, uv }], bounds [x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1] } in the entry's own units and frame (z up, its front +y, its own scale applied: place it with the placement's facing, scale and flip). The same parts as r.shape draws; null for an unknown shape\n1101:- `E.shapeMesh() → groups`: each one's mat (the material ready to draw: E.material's), key (its id), lid (true: the faces looking up or down, which some patterns draw their own way), curved (turned or round faces: planks run up them), face (a pattern drawn once per face, the crate's sides and bark's ends: uv runs 0 to 1 across each face), pos, nrm, uv (Float32Arrays: three numbers a corner, three corners a triangle; uv two a corner, world units across the surface)\n1516:- `physics.arc(x, y, r, a0, a1, o = {})`: a curved rail: a chain round (x, y) at radius r from angle a0 to a1 (radians; o.n segments)\n1573:## Module road: the pseudo-3D road: segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, roadside scenery, tunnels (engine/modules/road.js)\n1576:- `road.add(n, o = {})`: n segments more, bending (curve) and climbing (hill: units up, - down), eased in and out; o.tunnel, o.colors\n1578:- `road.curveAt(z)`: how hard the road bends at a distance\n1588:- `road.segs = []`: its segments ({ i, z, y0, y1, curve, tunnel, colors, things })\n1621:- `new E.RPG(o = {}) → rpg`: new E.RPG({ items, monsters, status, curve }): the rules of a role-playing game (the manual above)\n1633:- `rpg.curve`: curve(lv): the experience level lv needs in all (15 x (lv - 1) ^ 2.4 by default)","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174749__x8de669/work","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01MEHD2nz2g2P2y9VaUvFw61","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
