{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01T7cWKRLX4Cae76HzcchXzs","type":"tool_result","content":"42:if (E.targets(guard, [hero], { range: 60 }).length) throw new Error('not on the same level: no melee target');\n431:- `r.sightCone(obs, o = {})` †: an observer's view on the ground: a dithered fan fov wide (radians) about its facing, out to range, cut short where the map hides a body's chest (map.ray, the height rules), draped over the ground below. o: { range: 120, fov: 1.6, facing, map, eye, color: '#ffe080', alpha: .3, rays }. Call it in draw (it is a decal: under walls and bodies)\n502:- `game.start(hooks)`: Start the loop. Either one scene: game.start({ update(dt), draw(r) }) or several: game.start({ scenes: { title: {...}, play: {...} }, scene: 'title' }) A scene is { enter(data), exit(), update(dt), draw(r), back(), pausable, view, views, input, res, expand, touch, camera } (all optional). start() with nothing resumes a stopped loop. A headless game, or one made with loop: false, runs only by advance().\n565:- `settings.define(sp)`: add a setting: { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', value, min, max, step, options: [[value, label]] or [value], help, group: 'Game', apply(game, value) }. Its saved value is loaded (when it is a valid one) and applied; it shows on the settings screen. Returns its value\n568:- `settings.set(key, v)`: change a setting: checked (a slider kept in range, a choice among its options), saved, applied, onChange told. Returns the value kept (the old one when v is not a valid value)\n1015:- `E.sees(obs, tgt, o = {})`: can observer see target? { seen, d (ground distance), angle (observer -> target), exposure: 0..1 }. The target must be within range and inside the cone fov wide (radians) about the observer's facing; exposure is the share of three points on it (its feet, its chest, its head) that the observer's eyes see past every top of o.map, times the target's own exposure (default 1) and .6 when it crouches (it also shows lower). o: { range: 120, fov: 1.6, facing, map, eye }\n1156:- `E.ui.bar(g, x, y, w, h, frac, color = '#e0463c', o = {})`: a bar (a meter: health, magic, stamina, a boss's): ui.bar(g, x, y, w, h, 0..1, '#e0463c')\n1157:- `E.ui.box(g, x, y, w, h, o = {})`: window frame: ui.box(g, x, y, w, h, { bg, border, shadow, gradient }) bg: one color (drawn as a soft top-to-bottom gradient, like Final Fantasy windows) or [top, bottom] colors. gradient: false for a flat fill.\n1158:- `E.ui.counter(g, x, y, label, value, color = '#ffffff', o = {})`: label + value, e.g. ui.counter(g, 4, 4, 'RUPEES', 12)\n1159:- `E.ui.hearts(g, x, y, hp, max, o = {})`: row of hearts: hp and max in hearts (halves allowed, e.g. 2.5 of 3)\n1163:- `new E.Shell(game, o = {}) → shell`: new E.Shell(game, { theme, screens: { name: spec }, settings: { items, onChange(settings, key) }, store: 'shell-settings', meters: .125, standard: true }): an HTML interface over the game (see the section's header)\n1164:- `new E.Shell({ theme })`: CSS variables (ink, paper, accent, muted, danger, line, font, titleFont)\n1165:- `new E.Shell({ screens })`: specs ui.show(name) starts from (the pause screen follows game.paused; screens: { pause: false } leaves it out)\n1166:- `new E.Shell({ settings })`: settings.items: the game's own settings, { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', min, max, step, options, value } (kept in game.settings, beside the standard ones)\n1167:- `new E.Shell({ store, meters })`: store: where an older version saved them; meters: meters per world unit for distances\n1168:- `new E.Shell({ standard })`: false leaves out the standard menu (the pause screen's Settings, Controls, Full screen and Quit, and the settings' groups)\n1169:- `shell.back()` †: what cancel does: the screen's own back(), or close it (back to the screen under it; closing the pause screen resumes)\n1170:- `shell.dispose()` †: take its elements away and let go of the game (game.dispose() does it)\n1171:- `shell.hide()` †: close every screen (and resume, when the menu paused the game)\n1172:- `shell.hud(st = {})` †: the HUD, from this step's state (call it every step; a piece left out is hidden, and only what changed is redrawn)\n1173:- `shell.hud({ objective })` †: { step: '01 / 04', title, text, at: { x, y, z }, from: hero } (the distance in meters, and above or below)\n1174:- `shell.hud({ status, place, tip })` †: status: 'UNSEEN' or { text, color }; place: 'The Old Harbour'; tip: 'text' or { title, text }\n1175:- `shell.hud({ bars, counts })` †: bars: [{ label, value, max, kind: 'bar' | 'pips', color }] (health, stamina, a meter); counts: [[label, value]]\n1176:- `shell.hud({ prompt })` †: { key: 'E' (or act: 'interact': its key on the player's device), label, hint, progress: 0..1 }\n1177:- `shell.hud({ keys, buttons })` †: keys: [['WASD', 'Move'], ...] (hidden on touch screens); buttons: [[label, fn or action]] (top right: pause and map where there is no Escape key)\n1178:- `shell.hud({ minimap })` †: { map, at (with facing), markers: [{ x, y, kind: 'dot' | 'diamond' | 'ring' | 'cross', color }], onClick(x, y) (the world point clicked), fog (an E.Fog: unseen cells black, seen ones dim), camera: true (the ground the screen shows) }\n1179:- `shell.screen` †: the name of the open screen ('pause', 'settings', 'controls', ...), or null while the game plays\n1180:- `shell.settings` †: the player's settings: game.settings (the standard ones and the game's own, by key)\n1181:- `shell.show(name, spec = {})` †: open a screen: 'title' | 'pause' | 'settings' | 'help' | 'results' | 'map' or a name of your own, from spec over o.screens[name]. A spec: { kicker, title, text (strings or functions), actions: [[label, fn] or { label, fn, act, primary, disabled }], back (fn for cancel) }. From another screen it stacks (back() returns); shown again, it updates (the new spec over the old). 'settings' takes its items\n1182:- `shell.show('title')` †: { name, subtitle, meta: [...], footer }\n1183:- `shell.show('help')` †: { keys: [[key, what]], sections: [[heading, text]] }\n1184:- `shell.show('results')` †: { emblem, stats: [[value, label]], medals: [[label, earned]] }\n1185:- `shell.show('map')` †: { map, at, markers (a list or a function), labels: [[text, x, y]], onPick(x, y) }\n1186:- `shell.toast(title, text = '', seconds = 4)` †: a message that slides in at the top for a few seconds\n1187:- `shell.tutorial(title, text = '', seconds = 15)` †: a tutorial card (bottom left, dismissable) for some seconds; tutorial(null) takes it away\n1188:- `shell.root = null` †: game: the game it is over; o: its options; root: its DOM element (null in a headless game)\n1224:- `arcade.attract(dt)`: the attract mode, each step on the title: 'title', 'demo' (o.idle seconds without input; it lasts o.demo seconds or until endDemo()), 'scores' (o.scores seconds), then 'title' again; any input goes back to 'title'\n1248:- `arcade.mode = 'title'`: 'title' | 'play' | 'over'\n1251:- `arcade.phase = 'title'`: the attract mode's, 'title' | 'demo' | 'scores'\n1458:- `grid.threat(units, o = {})`: what a side can strike on its next turn: units ([{ cx, cy, move, range: [min, max] or n (1), climb, drop }]) each moving within its reach (o.blocked: cells it can't enter) and striking within range of where it stops. { cells: [[cx, cy, n]], count(c), by(c) -> [units] }: a threat map, for an AI's safe cells and a player's warning tint\n1605:- `world.shellMap()`: the explored map for E.Shell's minimap: game.shell.hud({ minimap: world.shellMap() }) (a cell a square, the save and boss rooms marked, the hero's cell)\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174749__x8de669/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"99d4115e-ac85-4844-bf9c-39009e8f9714","uuid":"4a6c40b6-722f-4fc9-a217-e31ced7fa3d8","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:50:43.351Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"42:if (E.targets(guard, [hero], { range: 60 }).length) throw new Error('not on the same level: no melee target');\n431:- `r.sightCone(obs, o = {})` †: an observer's view on the ground: a dithered fan fov wide (radians) about its facing, out to range, cut short where the map hides a body's chest (map.ray, the height rules), draped over the ground below. o: { range: 120, fov: 1.6, facing, map, eye, color: '#ffe080', alpha: .3, rays }. Call it in draw (it is a decal: under walls and bodies)\n502:- `game.start(hooks)`: Start the loop. Either one scene: game.start({ update(dt), draw(r) }) or several: game.start({ scenes: { title: {...}, play: {...} }, scene: 'title' }) A scene is { enter(data), exit(), update(dt), draw(r), back(), pausable, view, views, input, res, expand, touch, camera } (all optional). start() with nothing resumes a stopped loop. A headless game, or one made with loop: false, runs only by advance().\n565:- `settings.define(sp)`: add a setting: { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', value, min, max, step, options: [[value, label]] or [value], help, group: 'Game', apply(game, value) }. Its saved value is loaded (when it is a valid one) and applied; it shows on the settings screen. Returns its value\n568:- `settings.set(key, v)`: change a setting: checked (a slider kept in range, a choice among its options), saved, applied, onChange told. Returns the value kept (the old one when v is not a valid value)\n1015:- `E.sees(obs, tgt, o = {})`: can observer see target? { seen, d (ground distance), angle (observer -> target), exposure: 0..1 }. The target must be within range and inside the cone fov wide (radians) about the observer's facing; exposure is the share of three points on it (its feet, its chest, its head) that the observer's eyes see past every top of o.map, times the target's own exposure (default 1) and .6 when it crouches (it also shows lower). o: { range: 120, fov: 1.6, facing, map, eye }\n1156:- `E.ui.bar(g, x, y, w, h, frac, color = '#e0463c', o = {})`: a bar (a meter: health, magic, stamina, a boss's): ui.bar(g, x, y, w, h, 0..1, '#e0463c')\n1157:- `E.ui.box(g, x, y, w, h, o = {})`: window frame: ui.box(g, x, y, w, h, { bg, border, shadow, gradient }) bg: one color (drawn as a soft top-to-bottom gradient, like Final Fantasy windows) or [top, bottom] colors. gradient: false for a flat fill.\n1158:- `E.ui.counter(g, x, y, label, value, color = '#ffffff', o = {})`: label + value, e.g. ui.counter(g, 4, 4, 'RUPEES', 12)\n1159:- `E.ui.hearts(g, x, y, hp, max, o = {})`: row of hearts: hp and max in hearts (halves allowed, e.g. 2.5 of 3)\n1163:- `new E.Shell(game, o = {}) → shell`: new E.Shell(game, { theme, screens: { name: spec }, settings: { items, onChange(settings, key) }, store: 'shell-settings', meters: .125, standard: true }): an HTML interface over the game (see the section's header)\n1164:- `new E.Shell({ theme })`: CSS variables (ink, paper, accent, muted, danger, line, font, titleFont)\n1165:- `new E.Shell({ screens })`: specs ui.show(name) starts from (the pause screen follows game.paused; screens: { pause: false } leaves it out)\n1166:- `new E.Shell({ settings })`: settings.items: the game's own settings, { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', min, max, step, options, value } (kept in game.settings, beside the standard ones)\n1167:- `new E.Shell({ store, meters })`: store: where an older version saved them; meters: meters per world unit for distances\n1168:- `new E.Shell({ standard })`: false leaves out the standard menu (the pause screen's Settings, Controls, Full screen and Quit, and the settings' groups)\n1169:- `shell.back()` †: what cancel does: the screen's own back(), or close it (back to the screen under it; closing the pause screen resumes)\n1170:- `shell.dispose()` †: take its elements away and let go of the game (game.dispose() does it)\n1171:- `shell.hide()` †: close every screen (and resume, when the menu paused the game)\n1172:- `shell.hud(st = {})` †: the HUD, from this step's state (call it every step