{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NDge8X3LmRDSrgvrqMeVJf","type":"tool_result","content":"1:# Importing ready-made animation\n5:- **QUATERNIUS** (`src/mocap/sets/quaternius.js`): every free clip of [Quaternius' Universal Animation Library 1](https://quaternius.com/packs/universalanimationlibrary.html) and [Library 2](https://quaternius.com/pack\n6:- **MESH2MOTION** (`src/mocap/sets/mesh2motion.js`): the human animations of [Mesh2Motion](https://github.com/Mesh2Motion/mesh2motion-app) (CC0), from three origins:\n13:- **HERO** (`src/mocap/sets/hero.js`): the 15 clips Emberdeep's hero, the Wanderer, has adopted (see [The hero's clips](#the-heros-clips-in-emberdeep)): 8 from QUATERNIUS and 7 from MESH2MOTION, picked with `tools/ani\n24:## Pipeline\n29:libraries (.glb) ──tools/anim-import.mjs──▶ src/mocap/sets/quaternius.js ──tools/anim-set.mjs──▶ src/mocap/sets/hero.js\n31:                                                     └──────────── Mocap.load(set) ◀──────────────────────┘\n33:                                              lib.sample(clip, t) ──▶ Mannequin.draw / Mocap.drive(humanoid)\n50:2. **Pick a set for a game**: `node tools/anim-set.mjs src/mocap/sets/quaternius.js --clips Death01,LayToIdle --name HERO --out src/mocap/sets/hero.js --credit \"...\"` (`npm run mocap:set -- ...`) copies those clips, k\n65:   | QUATERNIUS | 88 | 1,295 | 378 KB | 72 KB | ~190k for all; a typical clip ~2,100 |\n66:   | MESH2MOTION | 177 | 2,798 | 800 KB | 155 KB | ~400k for all |\n67:   | CMU | 60 | 2,376 | 705 KB | 162 KB | ~360k for all |\n68:   | HERO | 15 | 238 | 74 KB | 17 KB | ~34k |\n70:   For comparison, the old raw form (every frame of the first library's 46 clips as base64 Int16) was 591 KB, 232 KB gzipped, and unreadable.\n71:4. **Play**: `const lib = Mocap.load(window.MOCAP.HERO)`. Then:\n73:   - `lib.sample(clip, t)` returns the pose at time t, in-betweening the key poses (loops wrap, one-shots hold their last pose);\n79:   `src/mocap/readable.js` (`MocapReadable`) holds the format itself, shared by the browser and the Node tools.\n82:   - `Mocap.drive(humanoid, lib)` makes a `Humanoid` take `rig.mocap = pose` after it poses itself.\n84:## Adding a library, step by step\n88:**1. Check the license.** The converted set is committed to this public repository and ships inside games, so the source must allow sharing derived data.\n89:- CC0 is ideal.\n154:**9. Test and commit.** Run `npm test`. Commit the set and the catalog, never the source files, and add the source and its license to the table below.\n158:### Importing from CMU, step by step\n170:**Every take in the lab.** `node tools/cmu.mjs library` writes the whole database to `examples/cmu-lib/` for the mocap lab's **CMU library** (`mocap-lab.html?set=library`): one set file a subject, long takes in 10-se\n185:- `\"$sources\"`: one `\"CMU\"` record (label, origin, license, url); the importer copies it for each subject, naming the subject and linking its page.\n210:### Where each clip came from\n214:- **`sources`**: one record per library the set was imported from. It gives the `file` and `rig`, plus a `label`, `origin`, `license` and `url`, written by hand in the catalog's `\"$sources\"`.\n219:     \"license\": \"CC0 1.0\", \"url\": \"https://github.com/Mesh2Motion/mesh2motion-app\" }\n234:The lab shows the origin under each clip's name (\"From Quaternius, via Mesh2Motion (CC0 1.0), made from QUATERNIUS Walk_Loop\"), and the catalog adds the library to each line. `tools/mocap-test.mjs` fails a clip whose\n237:- every 100 clips adds about 450 KB to the lab (85 KB gzipped);\n241:## Retargeting onto a Humanoid\n243:The hero's skeleton is 15 points with fixed bone lengths. The source's skeleton is a real adult's. `Mocap.drive` keeps the hero's build and borrows the clip's directions:\n252:- **Blending:** `rig.mocapW` (0 to 1) fades a clip in and out over the rig's own animation; `rig.mocapMask = 'upper'` plays only the chest, head and arms over the rig's own legs (reaching for loot while walking).\n254:## The readable format (for AI models)\n302:### How the format was chosen\n308:| Captured: every frame, 30 fps | 2,078 | 118 KB | 0 mm | no (binary) |\n309:| 15 fps: every second frame | 1,069 | 76 KB | 360 mm | no |\n310:| Key poses, 10 mm budget | 905 | 78 KB | 10 mm | no |\n311:| Key poses, 40 mm budget | 515 | 51 KB | 40 mm | no |\n312:| **Readable key poses** | **615** | **31 KB** | 214 mm (about 12 mm on average) | **yes** |\n316:## The hero's clips in Emberdeep\n350:1. Add it to the `anim-set.mjs` command above and run it again.\n353:## What the clips assume\n360:## Limits\n368:## Where to get more animation\n374:| Quaternius Universal Animation Library 1, Standard | 45 + T-pose | free | CC0 | GLB | imported (QUATERNIUS) |\n375:| Quaternius Universal Animation Library 2, Standard | 42 | free | CC0 | GLB | imported (QUATERNIUS) |\n376:| [Library 1 Pro](https://quaternius.itch.io/universal-animation-library) | 120+ | $9.99 | CC0 | GLB, FBX | Drop-in: same skeleton as Standard. Import it in place of the Standard file. |\n377:| [Library 2 Source](https://quaternius.itch.io/universal-animation-library-2) (Library 2 has no Pro tier) | 130+ | $14.99 | CC0 | .blend only | `tools/to-glb.py`, then import. Library 1's Source edition ($14.99) is \n378:| [Mesh2Motion](https://github.com/Mesh2Motion/mesh2motion-app) humans (`static/animations/human-*.glb`) | 178: 87 Quaternius clips re-exported, 75 hand-animated (climbs, ledge hang, bow, backflip, dodges, crawl, fly\n385:## Tests\n397:- a clip whose library has no origin or license on record, whose `orig` names a clip that doesn't exist, or whose `take` is not a take and a stretch of seconds;\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174749__x8de669/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"99d4115e-ac85-4844-bf9c-39009e8f9714","uuid":"c4479c87-9eb6-412b-8d58-806c6d91337a","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:02:15.961Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"1:# Importing ready-made animation\n5:- **QUATERNIUS** (`src/mocap/sets/quaternius.js`): every free clip of [Quaternius' Universal Animation Library 1](https://quaternius.com/packs/universalanimationlibrary.html) and [Library 2](https://quaternius.com/pack\n6:- **MESH2MOTION** (`src/mocap/sets/mesh2motion.js`): the human animations of [Mesh2Motion](https://github.com/Mesh2Motion/mesh2motion-app) (CC0), from three origins:\n13:- **HERO** (`src/mocap/sets/hero.js`): the 15 clips Emberdeep's hero, the Wanderer, has adopted (see [The hero's clips](#the-heros-clips-in-emberdeep)): 8 from QUATERNIUS and 7 from MESH2MOTION, picked with `tools/ani\n24:## Pipeline\n29:libraries (.glb) ──tools/anim-import.mjs──▶ src/mocap/sets/quaternius.js ──tools/anim-set.mjs──▶ src/mocap/sets/hero.js\n31:                                                     └──────────── Mocap.load(set) ◀──────────────────────┘\n33:                                              lib.sample(clip, t) ──▶ Mannequin.draw / Mocap.drive(humanoid)\n50:2. **Pick a set for a game**: `node tools/anim-set.mjs src/mocap/sets/quaternius.js --clips Death01,LayToIdle --name HERO --out src/mocap/sets/hero.js --credit \"...\"` (`npm run mocap:set -- ...`) copies those clips, k\n65:   | QUATERNIUS | 88 | 1,295 | 378 KB | 72 KB | ~190k for all; a typical clip ~2,100 |\n66:   | MESH2MOTION | 177 | 2,798 | 800 KB | 155 KB | ~400k for all |\n67:   | CMU | 60 | 2,376 | 705 KB | 162 KB | ~360k for all |\n68:   | HERO | 15 | 238 | 74 KB | 17 KB | ~34k |\n70:   For comparison, the old raw form (every frame of the first library's 46 clips as base64 Int16) was 591 KB, 232 KB gzipped, and unreadable.\n71:4. **Play**: `const lib = Mocap.load(window.MOCAP.HERO)`. Then:\n73:   - `lib.sample(clip, t)` returns the pose at time t, in-betweening the key poses (loops wrap, one-shots hold their last pose);\n79:   `src/mocap/readable.js` (`MocapReadable`) holds the format itself, shared by the browser and the Node tools.\n82:   - `Mocap.drive(humanoid, lib)` makes a `Humanoid` take `rig.mocap = pose` after it poses itself.\n84:## Adding a library, step by step\n88:**1. Check the license.** The converted set is committed to this public repository and ships inside games, so the source must allow sharing derived data.\n89:- CC0 is ideal.\n154:**9. Test and commit.** Run `npm test`. Commit the set and the catalog, never the source files, and add the source and its license to the table below.\n158:### Importing from CMU, step by step\n170:**Every take in the lab.** `node tools/cmu.mjs library` writes the whole database to `examples/cmu-lib/` for the mocap lab's **CMU library** (`mocap-lab.html?set=library`): one set file a subject, long takes in 10-se\n185:- `\"$sources\"`: one `\"CMU\"` record (label, origin, license, url); the importer copies it for each subject, naming the subject and linking its page.\n210:### Where each clip came from\n214:- **`sources`**: one record per library the set was imported from. It gives the `file` and `rig`, plus a `label`, `origin`, `license` and `url`, written by hand in the catalog's `\"$sources\"`.\n219:     \"license\": \"CC0 1.0\", \"url\": \"https://github.com/Mesh2Motion/mesh2motion-app\" }\n234:The lab shows the origin under each clip's name (\"From Quaternius, via Mesh2Motion (CC0 1.0), made from QUATERNIUS Walk_Loop\"), and the catalog adds the library to each line. `tools/mocap-test.mjs` fails a clip whose\n237:- every 100 clips adds about 450 KB to the lab (85 KB gzipped);\n241:## Retargeting onto a Humanoid\n243:The hero's skeleton is 15 points with fixed bone lengths. The source's skeleton is a real adult's. `Mocap.drive` keeps the hero's build and borrows the clip's directions:\n252:- **Blending:** `rig.mocapW` (0 to 1) fades a clip in and out over the rig's own animation; `rig.mocapMask = 'upper'` plays only the chest, head and arms over the rig's own legs (reaching for loot while walking).\n254:## The readable for