{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WZNzrY1K822xSjPt9nuYhz","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Ahead or Alive: Xtreme Beach Volleyball\n2\t\n3\t**Build plan.** It is written for developers (people or AI models) who will build the game from `TASK.md` and this file\n4\talone, without the planner. Where the two differ, `TASK.md` wins.\n5\t\n6\t- **Title:** *Ahead or Alive: Xtreme Beach Volleyball*. On screen the logo reads **AHEAD OR ALIVE** with the strap\n7\t  **XTREME BEACH VOLLEYBALL**. Tagline: *Stay ahead. Stay alive. Stay tanned.*\n8\t- **How the title was picked (as TASK.md asks):** 50 playful riffs on \"Dead or Alive Xtreme Beach Volleyball\" were\n9\t  brainstormed, then one was drawn with a real RNG: Python `secrets.randbelow(50)` (OS entropy) gave index 27, *Ahead or\n10\t  Alive: Xtreme Beach Volleyball*. Don't re-roll it.\n11\t- **Names and paths** (relative to this folder; `DEV/` and `GAME.html` are this plan's shorthand for the first two):\n12\t\n13\t| What | Path |\n14\t| --- | --- |\n15\t| Dev folder (`DEV/`): every source, tool and test | `./AheadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-DeadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174749/` |\n16\t| The deliverable (`GAME.html`): one self-contained file | `./AheadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-DeadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174749.html` |\n17\t| Exit interview, beside the html | `./exit-interview.json` |\n18\t\n19\t---\n20\t\n21\t## 0. The game in one page\n22\t\n23\t**Core loop** (put this sentence at the top of the game's source): *pick where to spend each morning, afternoon and night\n24\tof a five-day island vacation; win 2-on-2 beach volleyball with a partner you befriend through chats and gifts; spend the\n25\tprize money on swimsuits, gifts and casino nights; then beat the island's owner in the Fortuna Cup final.*\n26\t\n27\t**Premise** (original fiction in the source's tone): six of the world's toughest fighters each get a gold-trimmed\n28\tinvitation: *\"You are cordially invited to the AHEAD OR ALIVE Invitational on the private island of Isla Fortuna. Prize:\n29\teverything. — S. Fortuna, Esq.\"* They arrive expecting a brawl. Instead, flamboyant jackpot billionaire **Sonny Fortuna**\n30\tannounces that the \"tournament\" is a five-day beach vacation ending in a volleyball cup, the **Fortuna Cup**, while his\n31\tdeadpan concierge **Pepper Quill** hands out villa keys and sunscreen. Rivals become partners and the casino never closes.\n32\tOn day four you learn that Sonny has bet the island itself on the Cup.\n33\t\n34\t| Mode | What it is | Players |\n35\t| --- | --- | --- |\n36\t| **Vacation** (story) | 5 days × 3 time slots: matches, friendships and gifts, shopping, Pool Hop, casino, postcards; tutorial, semifinal, final, two endings | 1 |\n37\t| **Beach Match** (exhibition) | any fighters, owned outfits, court and time of day; any mix of 1–4 local players and CPUs | 1–4 local |\n38\t| **AI Hub session** | opens straight into a shared-world match on its own card; CPUs fill empty seats | 1–4 online |\n39\t| **Attract** | after 10 s idle on the title or menu: an AI-played broadcast of matches and a feature montage | — |\n40\t\n41\t**Feature checklist.** Everything here ships. There are no stubs; §11 repeats it as the definition of done.\n42\t\n43\t1. 2v2 beach volleyball. One timed **Play** button does the bump, set, spike and serve, with a timing ring on the sand.\n44\t   Also: dive, shot/block, Mine/Yours calls, aiming by stick or mouse, rally scoring, every fault, an AI partner and\n45\t   opponents, partner chemistry, two cameras, a TV-style HUD, Sonny's commentary, a crowd, celebrations and high-fives,\n46\t   and highlight replays.\n47\t2. Vacation calendar: 5 days of Morning, Afternoon and Night; weather; NPC schedules, teams and moods; a summary at the\n48\t   end of each day.\n49\t3. Island map travel and 5 walkable places: Sunset Courts, Lagoon Pool, Fortuna Promenade, Your Villa, and Casino\n50\t   Fortuna (night only). The Dock is used for cutscenes.\n51\t4. Talk, chat, gifts, team-ups and challenges; affinity hearts; likes you discover; partners who break up.\n52\t5. Money in Sonny Dollars (S$); 3 shops; 21 swimsuits, 10 accessories, 25 gifts; a wardrobe with try-on; NPCs wear the\n53\t   swimsuits you give them.\n54\t6. Pool Hop, a rhythm hopping minigame.\n55\t7. Casino: cashier, *Fortuna Sevens* pachislot, blackjack, roulette.\n56\t8. Postcards (photo mode), an album, and a postcard as the title backdrop.\n57\t9. Story: invitation, arrival, a welcome tutorial match against Sonny & Pepper, daily events, semifinal, a final against\n58\t   \"The House\" with special rules, farewell party, two endings, credits slideshow, vacation results, New Vacation+.\n59\t10. Save and load: 3 slots plus autosave; Continue.\n60\t11. Beach Match with 1–4 local players (pads and a split keyboard).\n61\t12. AI Hub shared-world online matches with the game's own card.\n62\t13. Attract mode.\n63\t14. Dev mode from the pause menu: tools, plus live tuning sliders with reset to defaults.\n64\t15. A controller-first 10-foot UI. PlayStation glyphs by default with an Xbox option in Settings; native keyboard and\n65\t    mouse (hover moves focus everywhere); touch-only devices get a gate instead of touch controls.\n66\t16. All audio made in code: 9 music tracks, jingles, about 45 sound effects, and Animalese-style voices per character.\n67\t17. How to Play pages, and an About & Credits screen with the Source Information and the three feedback sections.\n68\t\n69\t---\n70\t\n71\t## 1. Capturing the source\n72\t\n73\t| What the source is known for | How it shows up here |\n74\t| --- | --- |\n75\t| A fighting-game cast on holiday, lured by a flamboyant host under a fake tournament | 6 original fighters, each with a fighting style, personality and tastes, plus Sonny & Pepper. The invitation-ruse premise. Fighting backgrounds shape volleyball stats and celebrations. |\n76\t| Simple, timing-based 2v2 volleyball with an AI partner whose teamwork depends on your relationship | One Play button with a timing ring for every touch. Partner chemistry comes from affinity and changes how well she passes, sets and covers. |\n77\t| A vacation calendar where every activity takes time | 5 days × 3 slots. A location visit or an activity ends the slot. |\n78\t| Gift-giving and friendship as the social game | Loves, likes and dislikes; moods; accept/refuse reactions; team-up requests; break-ups. |\n79\t| Collecting swimsuits and accessories with prize money | 3 shops, 21 suits and 10 accessories with a live try-on. NPCs wear suits you give them. |\n80\t| Casino nights and pool hopping | Casino Fortuna (slots, blackjack, roulette) and Pool Hop. |\n81\t| Glossy tropical paradise, sunsets, a camera to play with | Resort art direction, time-of-day lighting, Postcards photo mode and album. |\n82\t| Campy, upbeat, slightly cheesy writing and a buffoonish host | Sonny's ALL-CAPS PA announcements, Pepper's deadpan, short punchy character lines. |\n83\t| A sunny pop/tropical soundtrack | An original chip-tropical score with steel drum, marimba and pluck instruments. |\n84\t\n85\t**Content line (keep it):** the source is famous for fan service. This game keeps its world, its cast dynamic, its\n86\tfashion collecting and its tone, but stays PG/teen:\n87\t\n88\t- every character is an adult (21+);\n89\t- swimwear is athletic or fashion-forward;\n90\t- the camera never lingers on bodies, and there is no jiggle physics;\n91\t- there are no peeping or \"dress her up for you\" mechanics;\n92\t- photo poses are holiday-snapshot poses;\n93\t- relationships are friendship and rivalry.\n94\t\n95\tThe humor comes from Sonny, the rivalries and vacation mishaps.\n96\t\n97\t---\n98\t\n99\t## 2. Genre, perspective and scope\n100\t\n101\t- **Genre:** sports (arcade 2v2 beach volleyball), plus a light life-sim (vacation calendar, friendship, collecting),\n102\t  plus minigames (rhythm Pool Hop, casino). Matches are the heart of it, about 60% of play time.\n103\t- **Cameras:**\n104\t  - **Matches:** a custom side-on **Broadcast** view, `new E.View('court', 'Broadcast', 0, 32, 1.5, 1)`. The net runs\n105\t    into the screen at the centre, your team is on the left, and the sea is behind the court. `cam.frame` keeps the ball\n106\t    and players in shot like a TV director.\n107\t  - Alternate: **Serve Cam**, `new E.View('servecam', 'Serve Cam', ±90, 46, 1.5, 1)`, behind your team as in the\n108\t    source. Pick the yaw sign that puts your team at the bottom of the screen (check with a screenshot). V or R3 toggles\n109\t    it, and Settings has it too; the attract mode cuts between both. Tune Broadcast pitch 28–36 and scale 1.3–1.5 by\n110\t    screenshot, keeping characters at least 44 px tall at zoom 1.\n111\t  - **Resort places and the Villa:** `threequarter`. **Island map:** `iso`. **Pool Hop:** the Broadcast angle following\n112\t    the hopper.\n113\t  - **Shops, wardrobe, casino tables and album:** full-screen canvas UI over a live world view.\n114\t- **Resolution:** `res: 'ps1'` with `expand: true` (at least 320×240; about 427×240 on 16:9). Every HUD is anchored to\n115\t  `r.W` and `r.H`.\n116\t- **Length:** a whole vacation takes about 45–75 minutes. A Beach Match to 7 takes about 4 minutes.\n117\t- **Hooks for the full game:** days, slots, cast, items, locations, events, text, music and tuning are all data tables.\n118\t  Adding a day, a fighter or a shop is a data edit plus art.\n119\t\n120\t---\n121\t\n122\t## 3. Tech and architecture\n123\t\n124\t### 3.1 Stack\n125\t\n126\t- **Engine:** my-3D2dge **v0.85.2**, the handoff package at\n127\t  `https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/tree/main/dist/handoff`.\n128\t  - Use the full engine `my-3d2dge.js`, which carries every module (story, songs, rhythm, arcade…).\n129\t  - Copy it to `DEV/engine/my-3d2dge.js` and patch it as §3.2 says.\n130\t  - Read `API.md` and `docs/ASSETS.md` whole. Grep `API-INDEX.md` and `AI_GUIDE.md` for: the sports recipe, Shell,\n131\t    Players, Audio, Testing without a browser, Recorded sessions, and \"New animation on the rigs\".\n132\t- **Kit to learn from:** `kits/sports.js` (2v2, `game.allowJoin`, the ball as a Body, `E.arc`, the crowd, radio\n133\t  commentary, the `proof()`/`bot()` pattern). Read it all. The volleyball simulation is new, but reuse its patterns.\n134\t- **Motion clips:** `src/mocap/readable.js`, `src/mocap/mocap.js`, and a small set cut with `tools/anim-set.mjs` from\n135\t  `src/mocap/sets/{quaternius,mesh2motion,cmu}.js`. Raw files are at\n136\t  `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/main/<path>`. The clip list is in §4.26.\n137\t- **AI Hub client:** `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/session.js` (v1.4.0 when this\n138\t  was planned), pasted in **unmodified**. For tests also fetch `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` from the same\n139\t  folder. Read `lib/hub/README.md` whole.\n140\t- **Tooling:** Node ≥ 20 (24 is installed); Playwright **1.63.0** (the handoff pins it) and Chromium for browser checks;"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"99d4115e-ac85-4844-bf9c-39009e8f9714","uuid":"b50eaaab-a5d7-4f99-b561-cc862db7d621","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:35:51.409Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174749__x8de669/work/PLAN.md","content":"# Ahead or Alive: Xtreme Beach Volleyball\n\n**Build plan.** It is written for developers (people or AI models) who will build the game from `TASK.md` and this file\nalone, without the planner. Where the two differ, `TASK.md` wins.\n\n- **Title:** *Ahead or Alive: Xtreme Beach Volleyball*. On screen the logo reads **AHEAD OR ALIVE** with the strap\n  **XTREME BEACH VOLLEYBALL**. Tagline: *Stay ahead. Stay alive. Stay tanned.*\n- **How the title was picked (as TASK.md asks):** 50 playful riffs on \"Dead or Alive Xtreme Beach Volleyball\" were\n  brainstormed, then one was drawn with a real RNG: Python `secrets.randbelow(50)` (OS entropy) gave index 27, *Ahead or\n  Alive: Xtreme Beach Volleyball*. Don't re-roll it.\n- **Names and paths** (relative to this folder; `DEV/` and `GAME.html` are this plan's shorthand for the first two):\n\n| What | Path |\n| --- | --- |\n| Dev folder (`DEV/`): every source, tool and test | `./AheadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-DeadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174749/` |\n| The deliverable (`GAME.html`): one self-contained file | `./AheadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-DeadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174749.html` |\n| Exit interview, beside the html | `./exit-interview.json` |\n\n---\n\n## 0. The game in one page\n\n**Core loop** (put this sentence at the top of the game's source): *pick where to spend each morning, afternoon and night\nof a five-day island vacation; win 2-on-2 beach volleyball with a partner you befriend through chats and gifts; spend the\nprize money on swimsuits, gifts and casino nights; then beat the island's owner in the Fortuna Cup final.*\n\n**Premise** (original fiction in the source's tone): six of the world's toughest fighters each get a gold-trimmed\ninvitation: *\"You are cordially invited to the AHEAD OR ALIVE Invitational on the private island of Isla Fortuna. Prize:\neverything. — S. Fortuna, Esq.\"* They arrive expecting a brawl. Instead, flamboyant jackpot billionaire **Sonny Fortuna**\nannounces that the \"tournament\" is a five-day beach vacation ending in a volleyball cup, the **Fortuna Cup**, while his\ndeadpan concierge **Pepper Quill** hands out villa keys and sunscreen. Rivals become partners and the casino never closes.\nOn day four you learn that Sonny has bet the island itself on the Cup.\n\n| Mode | What it is | Players |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **Vacation** (story) | 5 days × 3 time slots: matches, friendships and gifts, shopping, Pool Hop, casino, postcards; tutorial, semifinal, final, two endings | 1 |\n| **Beach Match** (exhibition) | any fighters, owned outfits, court and time of day; any mix of 1–4 local players and CPUs | 1–4 local |\n| **AI Hub session** | opens straight into a shared-world match on its own card; CPUs fill empty seats | 1–4 online |\n| **Attract** | after 10 s idle on the title or menu: an AI-played broadcast of matches and a feature montage | — |\n\n**Feature checklist.** Everything here ships. There are no stubs; §11 repeats it as the definition of done.\n\n1. 2v2 beach volleyball. One timed **Play** button does the bump, set, spike and serve, with a timing ring on the sand.\n   Also: dive, shot/block, Mine/Yours calls, aiming by stick or mouse, rally scoring, every fault, an AI partner and\n   opponents, partner chemistry, two cameras, a TV-style HUD, Sonny's commentary, a crowd, celebrations and high-fives,\n   and highlight replays.\n2. Vacation calendar: 5 days of Morning, Afternoon and Night; weather; NPC schedules, teams and moods; a summary at the\n   end of each day.\n3. Island map travel and 5 walkable places: Sunset Courts, Lagoon Pool, Fortuna Promenade, Your Villa, and Casino\n   Fortuna (night only). The Dock is used for cutscenes.\n4. Talk, chat, gifts, team-ups and challenges; affinity hearts; likes you discover; partners who break up.\n5. Money in Sonny Dollars (S$); 3 shops; 21 swimsuits, 10 accessories, 25 gifts; a wardrobe with try-on; NPCs wear the\n   swimsuits you give them.\n6. Pool Hop, a rhythm hopping minigame.\n7. Casino: cashier, *Fortuna Sevens* pachislot, blackjack, roulette.\n8. Postcards (photo mode), an album, and a postcard as the title backdrop.\n9. Story: invitation, arrival, a welcome tutorial match against Sonny & Pepper, daily events, semifinal, a final against\n   \"The House\" with special rules, farewell party, two endings, credits slideshow, vacation results, New Vacation+.\n10. Save and load: 3 slots plus autosave; Continue.\n11. Beach Match with 1–4 local players (pads and a split keyboard).\n12. AI Hub shared-world online matches with the game's own card.\n13. Attract mode.\n14. Dev mode from the pause menu: tools, plus live tuning sliders with reset to defaults.\n15. A controller-first 10-foot UI. PlayStation glyphs by default with an Xbox option in Settings; native keyboard and\n    mouse (hover moves focus everywhere); touch-only devices get a gate instead of touch controls.\n16. All audio made in code: 9 music tracks, jingles, about 45 sound effects, and Animalese-style voices per character.\n17. How to Play pages, and an About & Credits screen with the Source Information and the three feedback sections.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Capturing the source\n\n| What the source is known for | How it shows up here |\n| --- | --- |\n| A fighting-game cast on holiday, lured by a flamboyant host under a fake tournament | 6 original fighters, each with a fighting style, personality and tastes, plus Sonny & Pepper. The invitation-ruse premise. Fighting backgrounds shape volleyball stats and celebrations. |\n| Simple, timing-based 2v2 volleyball with an AI partner whose teamwork depends on your relationship | One Play button with a timing ring for every touch. Partner chemistry comes from affinity and changes how well she passes, sets and covers. |\n| A vacation calendar where every activity takes time | 5 days × 3 slots. A location visit or an activity ends the slot. |\n| Gift-giving and friendship as the social game | Loves, likes and dislikes; moods; accept/refuse reactions; team-up requests; break-ups. |\n| Collecting swimsuits and accessories with prize money | 3 shops, 21 suits and 10 accessories with a live try-on. NPCs wear suits you give them. |\n| Casino nights and pool hopping | Casino Fortuna (slots, blackjack, roulette) and Pool Hop. |\n| Glossy tropical paradise, sunsets, a camera to play with | Resort art direction, time-of-day lighting, Postcards photo mode and album. |\n| Campy, upbeat, slightly cheesy writing and a buffoonish host | Sonny's ALL-CAPS PA announcements, Pepper's deadpan, short punchy character lines. |\n| A sunny pop/tropical soundtrack | An original chip-tropical score with steel drum, marimba and pluck instruments. |\n\n**Content line (keep it):** the source is famous for fan service. This game keeps its world, its cast dynamic, its\nfashion collecting and its tone, but stays PG/teen:\n\n- every character is an adult (21+);\n- swimwear is athletic or fashion-forward;\n- the camera never lingers on bodies, and there is no jiggle physics;\n- there are no peeping or \"dress her up for you\" mechanics;\n- photo poses are holiday-snapshot poses;\n- relationships are friendship and rivalry.\n\nThe humor comes from Sonny, the rivalries and vacation mishaps.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Genre, perspective and scope\n\n- **Genre:** sports (arcade 2v2 beach volleyball), plus a light life-sim (vacation calendar, friendship, collecting),\n  plus minigames (rhythm Pool Hop, casino). Matches are the heart of it, about 60% of play time.\n- **Cameras:**\n  - **Matches:** a custom side-on **Broadcast** view, `new E.View('court', 'Broadcast', 0, 32, 1.5, 1)`. The net runs\n    into the screen at the centre, your team is on the left, and the sea is behind the court. `cam.frame` keeps the ball\n    and players in shot like a TV director.\n  - Alternate: **Serve Cam**, `new E.View('servecam', 'Serve Cam', ±90, 46, 1.5, 1)`, behind your team as in the\n    source. Pick the yaw sign that puts your team at the bottom of the screen (check with a screenshot). V or R3 toggles\n    it, and Settings has it too; the attract mode cuts between both. Tune Broadcast pitch 28–36 and scale 1.3–1.5 by\n    screenshot, keeping characters at least 44 px tall at zoom 1.\n  - **Resort places and the Villa:** `threequarter`. **Island map:** `iso`. **Pool Hop:** the Broadcast angle following\n    the hopper.\n  - **Shops, wardrobe, casino tables and album:** full-screen canvas UI over a live world view.\n- **Resolution:** `res: 'ps1'` with `expand: true` (at least 320×240; about 427×240 on 16:9). Every HUD is anchored to\n  `r.W` and `r.H`.\n- **Length:** a whole vacation takes about 45–75 minutes. A Beach Match to 7 takes about 4 minutes.\n- **Hooks for the full game:** days, slots, cast, items, locations, events, text, music and tuning are all data tables.\n  Adding a day, a fighter or a shop is a data edit plus art.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Tech and architecture\n\n### 3.1 Stack\n\n- **Engine:** my-3D2dge **v0.85.2**, the handoff package at\n  `https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/tree/main/dist/handoff`.\n  - Use the full engine `my-3d2dge.js`, which carries every module (story, songs, rhythm, arcade…).\n  - Copy it to `DEV/engine/my-3d2dge.js` and patch it as §3.2 says.\n  - Read `API.md` and `docs/ASSETS.md` whole. Grep `API-INDEX.md` and `AI_GUIDE.md` for: the sports recipe, Shell,\n    Players, Audio, Testing without a browser, Recorded sessions, and \"New animation on the rigs\".\n- **Kit to learn from:** `kits/sports.js` (2v2, `game.allowJoin`, the ball as a Body, `E.arc`, the crowd, radio\n  commentary, the `proof()`/`bot()` pattern). Read it all. The volleyball simulation is new, but reuse its patterns.\n- **Motion clips:** `src/mocap/readable.js`, `src/mocap/mocap.js`, and a small set cut with `tools/anim-set.mjs` from\n  `src/mocap/sets/{quaternius,mesh2motion,cmu}.js`. Raw files are at\n  `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/main/<path>`. The clip list is in §4.26.\n- **AI Hub client:** `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/session.js` (v1.4.0 when this\n  was planned), pasted in **unmodified**. For tests also fetch `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` from the same\n  folder. Read `lib/hub/README.md` whole.\n- **Tooling:** Node ≥ 20 (24 is installed); Playwright **1.63.0** (the handoff pins it) and Chromium for browser checks;","numLines":140,"startLine":1,"totalLines":2180}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01WZNzrY1K822xSjPt9nuYhz","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
