{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh2hEJvV5XcsSN4zciQc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GuJWvM6HGdJ1fbf9rF34fW","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174749__x8de669/work/PLAN.md","offset":140,"limit":200},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4856,"cache_read_input_tokens":484119,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4856},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"99d4115e-ac85-4844-bf9c-39009e8f9714","uuid":"f698d97f-a682-41e2-9689-96ae0c6c6c0f","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:35:54.404Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh2hE4YH11votUt7XmuM","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01GuJWvM6HGdJ1fbf9rF34fW":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174749__x8de669/work/PLAN.md","offset":140,"limit":200}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GuJWvM6HGdJ1fbf9rF34fW","type":"tool_result","content":"140\t- **Tooling:** Node ≥ 20 (24 is installed); Playwright **1.63.0** (the handoff pins it) and Chromium for browser checks;\n141\t  the handoff's `tools/check.mjs`, `filmstrip.mjs` and `replay.mjs`; Python 3 for the hub harness's local server.\n142\t- **Rules:** no other runtime libraries and no network at runtime. The hub client only talks to its parent frame.\n143\t- **Machine note:** `/tmp` was almost full when this was planned. If npm or Playwright fail with ENOSPC, set\n144\t  `TMPDIR=DEV/.tmp`.\n145\t\n146\t**Fetching the sources** (M0):\n147\t\n148\t```sh\n149\tgit clone --depth 1 --filter=blob:none --sparse https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge.git DEV/.src/my-3d2dge\n150\tcd DEV/.src/my-3d2dge && git sparse-checkout set --no-cone /dist/handoff/ /src/mocap/mocap.js /src/mocap/readable.js \\\n151\t  /src/mocap/sets/ /src/mocap/catalogs/ /tools/anim-set.mjs /docs/MOCAP.md\n152\t# (add any file anim-set.mjs imports if it complains)\n153\tcurl -fsSL -o DEV/vendor/aihub-session.js https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/session.js\n154\tfor f in harness.html bridge.js round.js README.md; do curl -fsSL -o DEV/hub/$f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/$f; done\n155\t```\n156\t\n157\t### 3.2 Engine patches\n158\t\n159\tAll patches go in `DEV/engine/my-3d2dge.js`. Mark each with `// AOA:`, list it in `DEV/ENGINE-CHANGES.md` with what\n160\tchanged and why, give it a headless test, and mention it in the About screen's Engine Feedback.\n161\t\n162\t1. **PlayStation symbols in the pixel font.** The 5×7 font table `G57` (around line 1322) lacks ✕ ○ □ △, which\n163\t   `input.label()` returns for PlayStation pads. Add them, plus ◀ ▶ for steppers.\n164\t2. **Button symbols setting.** Change the standard `glyphs` setting (around line 2999) to `{ group: 'Game', label:\n165\t   'Button symbols', type: 'select', value: 'playstation', options: [['playstation', 'PlayStation ✕ ○ □ △'], ['xbox',\n166\t   'Xbox A B X Y']] }`. That way it appears on the Settings screen and defaults to PlayStation, as TASK.md requires.\n167\t3. **Per-letter dialog voice.** In `Dialog`'s typing (around line 8956, `if (this.voice && …) this.game.audio.sfx(this.voice)`),\n168\t   when `typeof this.voice === 'function'`, call `this.voice(ch, index, pageText, this)` for **every** newly shown\n169\t   letter. Do not skip every other letter, and do not call sfx. This drives the Animalese voices (§4.24.3).\n170\t4. **Audio.**\n171\t   - (a) Add a third bus `_voxBus` under `_master`, with `audio.voiceVolume` and a standard setting `voices` (Sound\n172\t     group, slider, default .8). Add `audio.bus('sfx' | 'music' | 'voice')`, which returns the GainNode, or null\n173\t     headless.\n174\t   - (b) New options for a music track:\n175\t     - `decay` (seconds): an exponential pluck envelope instead of a held note;\n176\t     - `filter: 'lowpass'` with `cutoff` (Hz);\n177\t     - `detune` (cents): a second detuned oscillator;\n178\t     - `wave`: may name an entry in `audio.instruments`, a registry of PeriodicWave partial tables `{ real: [], imag: [] }`,\n179\t       so songs can use `steel`, `marimba`, `pluck`, `bell`, `organ` and `pad` (§4.24.1).\n180\t5. **Humanoid** (the art patch, §4.25.2):\n181\t   - (a) an `athletic` entry in `BUILDS`;\n182\t   - (b) `outfit: 'swim'` with `swim: { cut, pattern, colors: { main, accent, trim }, brief }`. Also allow\n183\t     `o.pattern` on the `shirt` outfit, for Sonny's loud shirt.\n184\t   - (c) hair styles `twinbuns`, `bun`, `braid`, `bob`, `puff` and `curly`;\n185\t   - (d) hat styles `sunhat` and `visor`;\n186\t   - (e) an `extras` hook: `rig.extras = [{ at: 'head' | 'face' | 'neck' | 'hair' | 'wristL' | 'wristR', draw(g, P,\n187\t     rig, view) }]`. It is called inside `draw` with the projected anchor point and depth-sorted with the head and torso.\n188\t     Sunglasses, flowers, necklaces, masks, glasses and wristbands use it.\n189\t   - (f) bare feet: when `colors.boot === colors.skin`, draw simple feet with no boot cuff; also an optional sandal strap\n190\t     color.\n191\t   - (g) new held poses: `vready`, `bump`, `set`, `block`, `toss`, `highfive`, `clap`, `facepalm`, `peace`, `lookback`,\n192\t     `stretch`, `sit`, `sunbathe`. Build them as `cheer`, `cast` and `kneel` are built in `solvePose`: joint targets,\n193\t     arms solved with `E.ik3`, blended by `poseW`.\n194\t6. **Session combo.** Add `game.input.reserveCombo = [8, 9]`: while pad button 8 (Create/View) is held, button 9\n195\t   (Options/Menu) presses reach no action. This is an AI Hub rule.\n196\t7. **Touch-off mode.** `new E.Game({ touch: 'never' })` hides touch buttons and the touch stick for good and hides the\n197\t   Touch settings group, but keeps the corner's menu button. Touch-only devices use it (§4.1.5).\n198\t8. Register the `court` and `servecam` views. Adding them to `E.VIEWS`, or making them in game code with `new E.View`,\n199\t   are both fine.\n200\t\n201\t### 3.3 Folder layout\n202\t\n203\t```\n204\t./PLAN.md                    this plan\n205\t./<GAME>.html                the deliverable (built; never edited by hand)\n206\t./exit-interview.json\n207\tDEV/\n208\t  package.json               { \"type\": \"module\", \"scripts\": { \"build\": \"node tools/build.mjs\", \"test\": \"node test/run.mjs\" },\n209\t                               \"devDependencies\": { \"playwright\": \"1.63.0\" } }\n210\t  README-DEV.md              how to build, run and test; conventions\n211\t  ENGINE-CHANGES.md          every engine patch: what and why\n212\t  .src/                      sparse clone of the engine repository (reference only; never bundled)\n213\t  engine/my-3d2dge.js        the patched engine\n214\t  vendor/aihub-session.js    unmodified hub client\n215\t  vendor/mocap/readable.js, mocap.js, aoa-clips.js     (the cut clip set, name AOA)\n216\t  hub/harness.html, bridge.js, round.js, README.md      (tests only; never bundled)\n217\t  src/*.js                   game modules (§3.6), concatenated in name order\n218\t  build/game.js              generated: every src file inside one IIFE\n219\t  build/dev.html             generated: engine, vendor and build/game.js as separate <script src>, for quick looks\n220\t  tools/build.mjs            builds build/ and the deliverable\n221\t  tools/rigsheet.mjs         every fighter × suit × facing × view to test-output/rigsheet/*.png (Playwright)\n222\t  tools/check.mjs, filmstrip.mjs, replay.mjs, asset-sheet.mjs, asset-find.mjs, asset-set.mjs   (copied from the handoff)\n223\t  test/run.mjs               THE test command (§9)\n224\t  test/lib/load.mjs, fakehub.mjs, bots.mjs, assert.mjs\n225\t  test/suites/*.test.mjs\n226\t  test-output/               screenshots, filmstrips, rig sheets (never bundled)\n227\t```\n228\t\n229\t### 3.4 Build (`node tools/build.mjs`, also `npm run build`)\n230\t\n231\t1. Concatenate `src/*.js` in lexical order into `build/game.js`, wrapped as\n232\t   `(() => { 'use strict'; const E = My3D2dge, G = {}; window.AOA = G; /* files */ })();`. Each src file is plain code\n233\t   that adds to `G`: no import or export.\n234\t2. Write `build/dev.html`.\n235\t3. Write the deliverable html. Order matters:\n236\t   ```html\n237\t   <!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n238\t   <script>/* vendor/aihub-session.js, verbatim */</script>        <!-- first script, right after meta charset (hub rule) -->\n239\t   <meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\"> … (the tags of §4.23)\n240\t   <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\">\n241\t   <title>Ahead or Alive: Xtreme Beach Volleyball</title>\n242\t   <style>html,body{margin:0;height:100%;background:#000;overflow:hidden}#screen{width:100%;height:100%;display:block;image-rendering:pixelated;touch-action:none}</style>\n243\t   </head><body>\n244\t   <!-- the handoff template's #e3-boot splash div, retitled AHEAD OR ALIVE -->\n245\t   <canvas id=\"screen\"></canvas>\n246\t   <script>/* engine/my-3d2dge.js */</script>\n247\t   <script>/* vendor/mocap/readable.js + mocap.js + aoa-clips.js */</script>\n248\t   <script>/* build/game.js */</script>\n249\t   </body></html>\n250\t   ```\n251\t4. Escape every `</script` inside inlined code as `<\\/script`. Add no external URL. Print the file size.\n252\t5. The build never edits the vendor client.\n253\t\n254\t### 3.5 Runtime architecture\n255\t\n256\t- **One game.**\n257\t  ```js\n258\t  G.game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'ps1', expand: true, view: 'court', id: 'ahead-or-alive', bg: '#0a2d3d',\n259\t    menu: hub ? false : { items, settings, quit: 'title' },\n260\t    autoPause: !hub, corner: !hub, fullscreen: hub ? false : true, touch: touchOnly ? 'never' : 'auto' })\n261\t  ```\n262\t  Here `hub = window.AIHub && AIHub.active` is known on the first line, and `items` are the pause actions of §4.2.\n263\t  Add `G.ui = new E.Shell(game, { theme })` for themed standard screens, toasts and tutorial cards. If the Shell's pause\n264\t  screen doesn't list the `menu.items`, pass them again as `screens: { pause: { actions } }`. A headless test checks the\n265\t  pause screen lists them.\n266\t- **Scenes** (`game.start({ scenes, scene, boot })`): `title`, `menu`, `attract`, `charselect`, `cutscene` (runs story\n267\t  scripts), `map`, `location` (every walkable place, entered with `{ loc }`), `match`, `poolhop`, `shop`, `wardrobe`,\n268\t  `journal`, `album`, `casino` (cashier, slots, blackjack and roulette as sub-states), `dayend`, `results`, `credits`,\n269\t  `about`, `howto`, `exhibition` (setup and join), `hub` (AI Hub card and match). Gameplay scenes are `pausable: true`;\n270\t  title, menu, attract, about, credits and the hub scene are not.\n271\t- **Overlays.** `G.overlay` is a stack for the dev panel, photo mode, toasts, the touch-only notice and the attract\n272\t  watcher. Wrap every scene with `G.wrapScene(scene)`: its `update` first calls `G.overlay.update(dt)`, which returns\n273\t  true when an overlay took the input, and its `draw` ends with `G.overlay.draw(r)`.\n274\t- **State.** `G.state` is the vacation save object (§4.19), or null outside a vacation. `G.session` is the\n275\t  exhibition/hub match config. `G.unlocks` lives in `E.store('aoa-unlocks')`.\n276\t- **Tuning.** `G.T` is the live object every system reads every step. It is built from `G.TUNING` defaults (§4.22.2),\n277\t  with dev overrides from `E.store('aoa-dev-tuning')`.\n278\t- **Randomness.** Gameplay never calls `Math.random`; use `G.rng(stream)`:\n279\t  - `world`: schedules, moods, weather and stock (seeded per save);\n280\t  - `match`: AI rolls, net cords (seeded per match);\n281\t  - `casino`;\n282\t  - `cosmetic`: crowd, particles, voices (never affects state).\n283\t  In a hub shared world the host seeds `match` from `AIHub.rng('match')`. A test greps `src/` for `Math.random(`.\n284\t- **Event bus.** `G.bus.on/off/emit` carries `point`, `touch`, `fault`, `matchEnd`, `gift`, `affinity`, `purchase`,\n285\t  `slotEnd`, `dayEnd`, `photo` and `story`. Commentary, stats, tests and the attract director listen to it.\n286\t- **Debug handle.** `game.debug = { snapshot(), tools }` (§9.2). The dev panel's buttons call the same `tools`.\n287\t\n288\t### 3.6 Source modules (`DEV/src/`)\n289\t\n290\t| File | Holds |\n291\t| --- | --- |\n292\t| `00-core.js` | G namespace, constants, rng streams, event bus, scene wrapper, overlay stack, helpers (`G.fmtMoney` → `S$12,500`) |\n293\t| `01-tuning.js` | `G.TUNING` (every slider: default, min, max, step, group, label, unit) and difficulty presets |\n294\t| `02-data-cast.js` | fighters, hosts and staff: looks, stats, tastes, likes, voice profiles, schedules, celebration clips |\n295\t| `03-data-items.js` | swimsuits, accessories, gifts, shops and stock rotation |\n296\t| `04-data-world.js` | location maps (rows, legends, props, spots, interactables), island map, calendar, weather, events |\n297\t| `05-data-text.js` | all dialogue as `E.Story` nodes, commentary lines, UI strings, How to Play and About texts |\n298\t| `06-data-music.js` | songs (step notation), jingles, instrument tables |\n299\t| `10-input.js` | action maps per context, devices, glyph icons, prompt drawing, the touch-only gate, mouse helpers |\n300\t| `11-ui.js` | the 10-foot canvas UI kit (§4.2) |\n301\t| `12-audio.js` | SFX defines, music control and layers, ambience loops, the Animalese voice synth |\n302\t| `13-rigs.js` | the rig factory (cast + suit + accessories), extras drawers, portraits |\n303\t| `14-world-art.js` | resort `E.SHAPES` and `E.MATERIALS`, backdrops and lighting by time of day, water, effects helpers |\n304\t| `15-anim.js` | move timelines, the arm-IK overlay, celebrations and emotes, mocap glue |\n305\t| `20-ball.js` | closed-form ball flight, launches, aiming, prediction, net and ground events |\n306\t| `21-rules.js` | the referee: touches, faults, scoring, serve rotation, match end, stats |\n307\t| `22-players.js` | player entity: movement, actions, the timing judge, the human controller |\n308\t| `23-ai.js` | volleyball AI: assignment, positioning, decisions, error model, chemistry, spectacle mode |\n309\t| `24-match.js` | the Match: phases, cameras, HUD, crowd, commentary, celebrations, replay, results |\n310\t| `25-netplay.js` | AI Hub shared-world host and client sync, the card, reporting |\n311\t| `30-vacation.js` | calendar, slots, weather, schedules, moods, affinity, partners, money, events, saves |\n312\t| `31-map.js` | the island map scene |\n313\t| `32-location.js` | the walkable location scene, NPC spots, talk menu, interactables |\n314\t| `33-shop.js` | shops, wardrobe, gift bag, journal |\n315\t| `34-story.js` | `E.Story` wiring, cutscene scripts, portraits and voices, prologue, party, endings |\n316\t| `40-poolhop.js` | Pool Hop |\n317\t| `41-casino.js` | casino floor, cashier, slots, blackjack, roulette |\n318\t| `42-photo.js` | photo mode and album |\n319\t| `50-title.js` | boot steps, title, main menu, How to Play, About & Credits |\n320\t| `51-attract.js` | the attract director |\n321\t| `52-exhibition.js` | Beach Match setup and local join |\n322\t| `53-dev.js` | the dev panel |\n323\t| `54-results.js` | match results, day end, vacation results, credits roll |\n324\t| `99-main.js` | building the game, scene registry, hub detection, boot, `game.start` |\n325\t\n326\t---\n327\t\n328\t## 4. Systems\n329\t\n330\t### 4.1 Input, devices, glyphs, prompts (`10-input.js`)\n331\t\n332\t**4.1.1 Action maps.** Each scene sets an `input` preset. Every preset includes the engine defaults for `up`, `down`,\n333\t`left` and `right` (WASD, arrows, d-pad, left stick) and for `start` and `pause`.\n334\t\n335\t| Preset | Action | Keyboard | Mouse | Pad (standard mapping) |\n336\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n337\t| MATCH | `play`: bump, set, spike, serve (timed) | Space, J | Left | 0 ✕/A |\n338\t| | `shot`: tip/cut shot, block, jump serve, free ball | E, K | Right | 2 □/X |\n339\t| | `dive` | Left Shift, L | — | 1 ○/B |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"99d4115e-ac85-4844-bf9c-39009e8f9714","uuid":"9cc3137d-7847-4aad-b588-f41af7d6d38f","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:35:54.410Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174749__x8de669/work/PLAN.md","content":"- **Tooling:** Node ≥ 20 (24 is installed); Playwright **1.63.0** (the handoff pins it) and Chromium for browser checks;\n  the handoff's `tools/check.mjs`, `filmstrip.mjs` and `replay.mjs`; Python 3 for the hub harness's local server.\n- **Rules:** no other runtime libraries and no network at runtime. The hub client only talks to its parent frame.\n- **Machine note:** `/tmp` was almost full when this was planned. If npm or Playwright fail with ENOSPC, set\n  `TMPDIR=DEV/.tmp`.\n\n**Fetching the sources** (M0):\n\n```sh\ngit clone --depth 1 --filter=blob:none --sparse https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge.git DEV/.src/my-3d2dge\ncd DEV/.src/my-3d2dge && git sparse-checkout set --no-cone /dist/handoff/ /src/mocap/mocap.js /src/mocap/readable.js \\\n  /src/mocap/sets/ /src/mocap/catalogs/ /tools/anim-set.mjs /docs/MOCAP.md\n# (add any file anim-set.mjs imports if it complains)\ncurl -fsSL -o DEV/vendor/aihub-session.js https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/session.js\nfor f in harness.html bridge.js round.js README.md; do curl -fsSL -o DEV/hub/$f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/$f; done\n```\n\n### 3.2 Engine patches\n\nAll patches go in `DEV/engine/my-3d2dge.js`. Mark each with `// AOA:`, list it in `DEV/ENGINE-CHANGES.md` with what\nchanged and why, give it a headless test, and mention it in the About screen's Engine Feedback.\n\n1. **PlayStation symbols in the pixel font.** The 5×7 font table `G57` (around line 1322) lacks ✕ ○ □ △, which\n   `input.label()` returns for PlayStation pads. Add them, plus ◀ ▶ for steppers.\n2. **Button symbols setting.** Change the standard `glyphs` setting (around line 2999) to `{ group: 'Game', label:\n   'Button symbols', type: 'select', value: 'playstation', options: [['playstation', 'PlayStation ✕ ○ □ △'], ['xbox',\n   'Xbox A B X Y']] }`. That way it appears on the Settings screen and defaults to PlayStation, as TASK.md requires.\n3. **Per-letter dialog voice.** In `Dialog`'s typing (around line 8956, `if (this.voice && …) this.game.audio.sfx(this.voice)`),\n   when `typeof this.voice === 'function'`, call `this.voice(ch, index, pageText, this)` for **every** newly shown\n   letter. Do not skip every other letter, and do not call sfx. This drives the Animalese voices (§4.24.3).\n4. **Audio.**\n   - (a) Add a third bus `_voxBus` under `_master`, with `audio.voiceVolume` and a standard setting `voices` (Sound\n     group, slider, default .8). Add `audio.bus('sfx' | 'music' | 'voice')`, which returns the GainNode, or null\n     headless.\n   - (b) New options for a music track:\n     - `decay` (seconds): an exponential pluck envelope instead of a held note;\n     - `filter: 'lowpass'` with `cutoff` (Hz);\n     - `detune` (cents): a second detuned oscillator;\n     - `wave`: may name an entry in `audio.instruments`, a registry of PeriodicWave partial tables `{ real: [], imag: [] }`,\n       so songs can use `steel`, `marimba`, `pluck`, `bell`, `organ` and `pad` (§4.24.1).\n5. **Humanoid** (the art patch, §4.25.2):\n   - (a) an `athletic` entry in `BUILDS`;\n   - (b) `outfit: 'swim'` with `swim: { cut, pattern, colors: { main, accent, trim }, brief }`. Also allow\n     `o.pattern` on the `shirt` outfit, for Sonny's loud shirt.\n   - (c) hair styles `twinbuns`, `bun`, `braid`, `bob`, `puff` and `curly`;\n   - (d) hat styles `sunhat` and `visor`;\n   - (e) an `extras` hook: `rig.extras = [{ at: 'head' | 'face' | 'neck' | 'hair' | 'wristL' | 'wristR', draw(g, P,\n     rig, view) }]`. It is called inside `draw` with the projected anchor point and depth-sorted with the head and torso.\n     Sunglasses, flowers, necklaces, masks, glasses and wristbands use it.\n   - (f) bare feet: when `colors.boot === colors.skin`, draw simple feet with no boot cuff; also an optional sandal strap\n     color.\n   - (g) new held poses: `vready`, `bump`, `set`, `block`, `toss`, `highfive`, `clap`, `facepalm`, `peace`, `lookback`,\n     `stretch`, `sit`, `sunbathe`. Build them as `cheer`, `cast` and `kneel` are built in `solvePose`: joint targets,\n     arms solved with `E.ik3`, blended by `poseW`.\n6. **Session combo.** Add `game.input.reserveCombo = [8, 9]`: while pad button 8 (Create/View) is held, button 9\n   (Options/Menu) presses reach no action. This is an AI Hub rule.\n7. **Touch-off mode.** `new E.Game({ touch: 'never' })` hides touch buttons and the touch stick for good and hides the\n   Touch settings group, but keeps the corner's menu button. Touch-only devices use it (§4.1.5).\n8. Register the `court` and `servecam` views. Adding them to `E.VIEWS`, or making them in game code with `new E.View`,\n   are both fine.\n\n### 3.3 Folder layout\n\n```\n./PLAN.md                    this plan\n./<GAME>.html                the deliverable (built; never edited by hand)\n./exit-interview.json\nDEV/\n  package.json               { \"type\": \"module\", \"scripts\": { \"build\": \"node tools/build.mjs\", \"test\": \"node test/run.mjs\" },\n                               \"devDependencies\": { \"playwright\": \"1.63.0\" } }\n  README-DEV.md              how to build, run and test; conventions\n  ENGINE-CHANGES.md          every engine patch: what and why\n  .src/                      sparse clone of the engine repository (reference only; never bundled)\n  engine/my-3d2dge.js        the patched engine\n  vendor/aihub-session.js    unmodified hub client\n  vendor/mocap/readable.js, mocap.js, aoa-clips.js     (the cut clip set, name AOA)\n  hub/harness.html, bridge.js, round.js, README.md      (tests only; never bundled)\n  src/*.js                   game modules (§3.6), concatenated in name order\n  build/game.js              generated: every src file inside one IIFE\n  build/dev.html             generated: engine, vendor and build/game.js as separate <script src>, for quick looks\n  tools/build.mjs            builds build/ and the deliverable\n  tools/rigsheet.mjs         every fighter × suit × facing × view to test-output/rigsheet/*.png (Playwright)\n  tools/check.mjs, filmstrip.mjs, replay.mjs, asset-sheet.mjs, asset-find.mjs, asset-set.mjs   (copied from the handoff)\n  test/run.mjs               THE test command (§9)\n  test/lib/load.mjs, fakehub.mjs, bots.mjs, assert.mjs\n  test/suites/*.test.mjs\n  test-output/               screenshots, filmstrips, rig sheets (never bundled)\n```\n\n### 3.4 Build (`node tools/build.mjs`, also `npm run build`)\n\n1. Concatenate `src/*.js` in lexical order into `build/game.js`, wrapped as\n   `(() => { 'use strict'; const E = My3D2dge, G = {}; window.AOA = G; /* files */ })();`. Each src file is plain code\n   that adds to `G`: no import or export.\n2. Write `build/dev.html`.\n3. Write the deliverable html. Order matters:\n   ```html\n   <!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n   <script>/* vendor/aihub-session.js, verbatim */</script>        <!-- first script, right after meta charset (hub rule) -->\n   <meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\"> … (the tags of §4.23)\n   <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\">\n   <title>Ahead or Alive: Xtreme Beach Volleyball</title>\n   <style>html,body{margin:0;height:100%;background:#000;overflow:hidden}#screen{width:100%;height:100%;display:block;image-rendering:pixelated;touch-action:none}</style>\n   </head><body>\n   <!-- the handoff template's #e3-boot splash div, retitled AHEAD OR ALIVE -->\n   <canvas id=\"screen\"></canvas>\n   <script>/* engine/my-3d2dge.js */</script>\n   <script>/* vendor/mocap/readable.js + mocap.js + aoa-clips.js */</script>\n   <script>/* build/game.js */</script>\n   </body></html>\n   ```\n4. Escape every `</script` inside inlined code as `<\\/script`. Add no external URL. Print the file size.\n5. The build never edits the vendor client.\n\n### 3.5 Runtime architecture\n\n- **One game.**\n  ```js\n  G.game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'ps1', expand: true, view: 'court', id: 'ahead-or-alive', bg: '#0a2d3d',\n    menu: hub ? false : { items, settings, quit: 'title' },\n    autoPause: !hub, corner: !hub, fullscreen: hub ? false : true, touch: touchOnly ? 'never' : 'auto' })\n  ```\n  Here `hub = window.AIHub && AIHub.active` is known on the first line, and `items` are the pause actions of §4.2.\n  Add `G.ui = new E.Shell(game, { theme })` for themed standard screens, toasts and tutorial cards. If the Shell's pause\n  screen doesn't list the `menu.items`, pass them again as `screens: { pause: { actions } }`. A headless test checks the\n  pause screen lists them.\n- **Scenes** (`game.start({ scenes, scene, boot })`): `title`, `menu`, `attract`, `charselect`, `cutscene` (runs story\n  scripts), `map`, `location` (every walkable place, entered with `{ loc }`), `match`, `poolhop`, `shop`, `wardrobe`,\n  `journal`, `album`, `casino` (cashier, slots, blackjack and roulette as sub-states), `dayend`, `results`, `credits`,\n  `about`, `howto`, `exhibition` (setup and join), `hub` (AI Hub card and match). Gameplay scenes are `pausable: true`;\n  title, menu, attract, about, credits and the hub scene are not.\n- **Overlays.** `G.overlay` is a stack for the dev panel, photo mode, toasts, the touch-only notice and the attract\n  watcher. Wrap every scene with `G.wrapScene(scene)`: its `update` first calls `G.overlay.update(dt)`, which returns\n  true when an overlay took the input, and its `draw` ends with `G.overlay.draw(r)`.\n- **State.** `G.state` is the vacation save object (§4.19), or null outside a vacation. `G.session` is the\n  exhibition/hub match config. `G.unlocks` lives in `E.store('aoa-unlocks')`.\n- **Tuning.** `G.T` is the live object every system reads every step. It is built from `G.TUNING` defaults (§4.22.2),\n  with dev overrides from `E.store('aoa-dev-tuning')`.\n- **Randomness.** Gameplay never calls `Math.random`; use `G.rng(stream)`:\n  - `world`: schedules, moods, weather and stock (seeded per save);\n  - `match`: AI rolls, net cords (seeded per match);\n  - `casino`;\n  - `cosmetic`: crowd, particles, voices (never affects state).\n  In a hub shared world the host seeds `match` from `AIHub.rng('match')`. A test greps `src/` for `Math.random(`.\n- **Event bus.** `G.bus.on/off/emit` carries `point`, `touch`, `fault`, `matchEnd`, `gift`, `affinity`, `purchase`,\n  `slotEnd`, `dayEnd`, `photo` and `story`. Commentary, stats, tests and the attract director listen to it.\n- **Debug handle.** `game.debug = { snapshot(), tools }` (§9.2). The dev panel's buttons call the same `tools`.\n\n### 3.6 Source modules (`DEV/src/`)\n\n| File | Holds |\n| --- | --- |\n| `00-core.js` | G namespace, constants, rng streams, event bus, scene wrapper, overlay stack, helpers (`G.fmtMoney` → `S$12,500`) |\n| `01-tuning.js` | `G.TUNING` (every slider: default, min, max, step, group, label, unit) and difficulty presets |\n| `02-data-cast.js` | fighters, hosts and staff: looks, stats, tastes, likes, voice profiles, schedules, celebration clips |\n| `03-data-items.js` | swimsuits, accessories, gifts, shops and stock rotation |\n| `04-data-world.js` | location maps (rows, legends, props, spots, interactables), island map, calendar, weather, events |\n| `05-data-text.js` | all dialogue as `E.Story` nodes, commentary lines, UI strings, How to Play and About texts |\n| `06-data-music.js` | songs (step notation), jingles, instrument tables |\n| `10-input.js` | action maps per context, devices, glyph icons, prompt drawing, the touch-only gate, mouse helpers |\n| `11-ui.js` | the 10-foot canvas UI kit (§4.2) |\n| `12-audio.js` | SFX defines, music control and layers, ambience loops, the Animalese voice synth |\n| `13-rigs.js` | the rig factory (cast + suit + accessories), extras drawers, portraits |\n| `14-world-art.js` | resort `E.SHAPES` and `E.MATERIALS`, backdrops and lighting by time of day, water, effects helpers |\n| `15-anim.js` | move timelines, the arm-IK overlay, celebrations and emotes, mocap glue |\n| `20-ball.js` | closed-form ball flight, launches, aiming, prediction, net and ground events |\n| `21-rules.js` | the referee: touches, faults, scoring, serve rotation, match end, stats |\n| `22-players.js` | player entity: movement, actions, the timing judge, the human controller |\n| `23-ai.js` | volleyball AI: assignment, positioning, decisions, error model, chemistry, spectacle mode |\n| `24-match.js` | the Match: phases, cameras, HUD, crowd, commentary, celebrations, replay, results |\n| `25-netplay.js` | AI Hub shared-world host and client sync, the card, reporting |\n| `30-vacation.js` | calendar, slots, weather, schedules, moods, affinity, partners, money, events, saves |\n| `31-map.js` | the island map scene |\n| `32-location.js` | the walkable location scene, NPC spots, talk menu, interactables |\n| `33-shop.js` | shops, wardrobe, gift bag, journal |\n| `34-story.js` | `E.Story` wiring, cutscene scripts, portraits and voices, prologue, party, endings |\n| `40-poolhop.js` | Pool Hop |\n| `41-casino.js` | casino floor, cashier, slots, blackjack, roulette |\n| `42-photo.js` | photo mode and album |\n| `50-title.js` | boot steps, title, main menu, How to Play, About & Credits |\n| `51-attract.js` | the attract director |\n| `52-exhibition.js` | Beach Match setup and local join |\n| `53-dev.js` | the dev panel |\n| `54-results.js` | match results, day end, vacation results, credits roll |\n| `99-main.js` | building the game, scene registry, hub detection, boot, `game.start` |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Systems\n\n### 4.1 Input, devices, glyphs, prompts (`10-input.js`)\n\n**4.1.1 Action maps.** Each scene sets an `input` preset. Every preset includes the engine defaults for `up`, `down`,\n`left` and `right` (WASD, arrows, d-pad, left stick) and for `start` and `pause`.\n\n| Preset | Action | Keyboard | Mouse | Pad (standard mapping) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| MATCH | `play`: bump, set, spike, serve (timed) | Space, J | Left | 0 ✕/A |\n| | `shot`: tip/cut shot, block, jump serve, free ball | E, K | Right | 2 □/X |\n| | `dive` | Left Shift, L | — | 1 ○/B |","numLines":200,"startLine":140,"totalLines":2180}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01GuJWvM6HGdJ1fbf9rF34fW","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
