{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QaynHKQCv9hNnGJBKVhQBA","type":"tool_result","content":"339\t| | `dive` | Left Shift, L | — | 1 ○/B |\n340\t| | `call`: Mine / Yours / Auto | Q, I | Middle | 3 △/Y |\n341\t| | `view`: Broadcast ↔ Serve Cam | V | — | 11 R3 |\n342\t| EXPLORE | `interact` | E, Space, Enter | Left (on a person or thing) | 0 ✕/A |\n343\t| | `run` (hold) | Left Shift | — | 1 ○/B, 7 R2 |\n344\t| | `bag`: gift bag | G | — | 2 □/X |\n345\t| | `leave`: island map | M, Tab | — | 3 △/Y |\n346\t| | `snap`: postcard (not in sessions) | C | — | 8 Create/View |\n347\t| MENU | `confirm` | Enter, Space | Left | 0 ✕/A |\n348\t| | `cancel` | Backspace (Esc on non-pausable screens) | Right | 1 ○/B |\n349\t| | `alt` | F | — | 2 □/X |\n350\t| | `extra` | R | — | 3 △/Y |\n351\t| | `tabL` / `tabR` | Q / E | wheel | 4 L1 / 5 R1 |\n352\t| POOLHOP | `hopA` / `hopB` / `hopX` / `hopY` | J, Space / L, Shift / K, E / I, Q | Left = hopA, Right = hopX | 0 / 1 / 2 / 3 |\n353\t| CASINO | MENU, plus blackjack H hit, S stand, D double, P split; slots J K L stop reels 1-2-3 | | | |\n354\t\n355\t- **Split keyboard (Beach Match).** The engine's half-keys give P1 WASD plus F G H R and P2 the arrows plus `.` `/` `,`\n356\t  `L`. Order the MATCH actions `play, dive, shot, call` so the halves come out as F/`.` = play, G/`/` = dive, H/`,` =\n357\t  shot, R/L = call. Show this on the join screen as keycaps.\n358\t- **Escape.** In pausable scenes Escape opens the pause menu, and Backspace or right click goes back inside our canvas\n359\t  screens. On title and menu screens Escape goes back.\n360\t\n361\t**4.1.2 Device and glyph logic.**\n362\t\n363\t- `G.dev(input)` returns `'ps' | 'xbox' | 'kbm'`. `lastDevice === 'gamepad'` gives `padStyle()`, which follows the\n364\t  Button symbols setting; keyboard or mouse gives `kbm`.\n365\t- `G.prompt(g, x, y, action, text, { input })` draws a glyph icon and the text and returns its width. Prompts redraw from\n366\t  the current device every frame; never cache them.\n367\t- **Glyph icons** are pixel art drawn with `px`:\n368\t\n369\t| Device | How it is drawn |\n370\t| --- | --- |\n371\t| PlayStation | a 9×9 dark disc with the symbol in its color: ✕ `#8fb8ff`, ○ `#ff7a7a`, □ `#f59ad8`, △ `#5fe0b4` |\n372\t| Xbox | a disc in the letter's color, with a dark letter: A `#6ad66a`, B `#ff5a5a`, X `#4aa8ff`, Y `#ffd23a` |\n373\t| Pad shoulders and system buttons | rounded pills: L1/R1/L2/R2 or LB/RB/LT/RT; Options/Create or Menu/View; d-pad and stick icons |\n374\t| Keyboard | a keycap (light rounded rectangle, darker bottom edge) with `input.label(action, 'keyboard')` |\n375\t| Mouse | a 7×9 mouse with the bound button lit |\n376\t\n377\t- `G.ui.promptBar([[action, text], …])` sits at the bottom centre of every screen. Text never says \"press A\": the glyph\n378\t  always comes from the action map.\n379\t\n380\t**4.1.3 Mouse.**\n381\t\n382\t- **Canvas UI:** hover moves focus (`input.pointer()` hit-tested against the widgets laid out last frame); left click\n383\t  activates; right click goes back; the wheel scrolls or pages lists.\n384\t- **World:** hovering an NPC or an interactable highlights it and shows its name (`r.actor(…, { pick: npc })` with\n385\t  `r.pick`). Clicking walks there and interacts.\n386\t- **Matches:** while the last device is keyboard or mouse, a reticle follows `game.mouseGround()` on the opponents' half.\n387\t  Spike, shot and serve aim at it.\n388\t- **Photo mode:** right-drag orbits and the wheel zooms.\n389\t\n390\t**4.1.4 Rumble.** Use `input.rumble`: spikes and serves (.35, .1 s), blocks (.5, .12 s), dives (.3, .15 s), the jackpot\n391\t(.6, .5 s).\n392\t\n393\t**4.1.5 Touch-only gate.**\n394\t\n395\t- `G.touchOnly()` is `matchMedia('(any-pointer: coarse)').matches && !matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches &&\n396\t  !G.sawKeyOrPad`. Check it at boot and on each pointer event.\n397\t- While it is true:\n398\t  - there are no touch controls (patch 7);\n399\t  - the title and menu show a centred panel, **\"Controller or keyboard required\"**, with the line \"Connect a controller\n400\t    or keyboard to play. The demo keeps running.\" and a big **Settings** button (a tap opens `game.menu('settings')`);\n401\t  - the engine corner's menu button stays;\n402\t  - taps do nothing else, and the attract mode runs as usual (a tap ends it, as any input does).\n403\t- The first key or gamepad button sets `G.sawKeyOrPad` and normal play resumes.\n404\t- In an AI Hub session a touch-only player's fighter is played by the AI, with the banner \"Connect a controller or\n405\t  keyboard to take over\".\n406\t\n407\t### 4.2 The 10-foot canvas UI kit (`11-ui.js`)\n408\t\n409\t**Readability rules.** Each one is a review item.\n410\t\n411\t- **Text sizes:** the smallest text anywhere is `E.font` 5×7 at scale 1 with a shadow. Headings are scale 2; screen\n412\t  titles are `E.font.title` at scale 3; numbers that matter (money, score) are scale 2.\n413\t- **Density:** at most 8 focusable items per screen. Item grids are 3×2 (shops, gifts, wardrobe) or 4×2 (album), paged\n414\t  with L1/R1, Q/E or the wheel. There is one detail panel. Never show stat tables: use icons, bars, hearts and short\n415\t  phrases.\n416\t- **Safe area:** keep content inside a 5% margin of `r.W`/`r.H` (TV overscan) and clear of `game.cornerArea()` and\n417\t  `input.touchArea()`.\n418\t- **Focus:** a 2-px gold outline with a 1-px white inner line, a soft additive glow pulse and a 1-px lift. Sounds:\n419\t  `ui_tick` on move, `ui_select` on confirm, `ui_back` on back, `ui_error` on refusal.\n420\t- **Navigation:** d-pad, stick, WASD and arrows move focus spatially to the nearest widget in that direction, repeating\n421\t  via `input.repeat` (0.35 s delay, 0.09 s rate). Confirm and back come from MENU; tabs are L1/R1 and Q/E; the mouse\n422\t  works as in §4.1.3.\n423\t- **Themes:**\n424\t\n425\t| Theme | Panel bg | Border | Ink | Muted | Accent |\n426\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n427\t| Day | `['#0f4c5c', '#0a2d3d']` | `#f6d38a` | `#fff8e8` | `#9fd3d6` | `#ff9e5e` |\n428\t| Night (casino, night villa) | `['#2a1240', '#12081e']` | `#ff5fa2` | as day | as day | `#5ff0ff` |\n429\t\n430\t**Widgets:**\n431\t\n432\t| Widget | Purpose |\n433\t| --- | --- |\n434\t| `Panel` | gradient window (`E.ui.box`) |\n435\t| `Button` | label, optional glyph, disabled state |\n436\t| `List` | vertical menu, scrolls past 8 |\n437\t| `Grid` | cards in rows and columns, paged |\n438\t| `Tabs` | categories; L1/R1 |\n439\t| `Slider` | number; left/right steps, held accelerates, mouse drag; shows the default as a tick |\n440\t| `Toggle`, `Stepper` | ◀ value ▶ |\n441\t| `Card` | item: icon or live rig preview, name, price, NEW/OWNED/WEARING badges |\n442\t| `CharCard` | portrait (`rig.drawPortrait`), name, hearts, mood icon and word |\n443\t| `MoneyBadge` | coin icon and amount, animated count |\n444\t| `ClockBadge` | \"Day 2 · Afternoon\" with sun/moon and weather icons |\n445\t| `Confirm` | yes/no; default No when destructive |\n446\t| `Toast` | slides in at the top for 3 s |\n447\t| `PromptBar` | glyph prompts at the bottom |\n448\t| `Tip` | one line under the focused card |\n449\t\n450\t- **Layout:** `ui.frame(r)` lays out widgets from `r.W`/`r.H` each draw and records hit rects; `update` uses last\n451\t  frame's rects.\n452\t- **E.Shell theme**, for the engine's standard pause, settings and controls screens and for toasts: the day palette,\n453\t  `font: '600 20px/1.35 \"Trebuchet MS\", system-ui, sans-serif'`.\n454\t- **Pause actions:** Resume (engine), **How to Play**, **Take a Postcard** (walkable places and match results only),\n455\t  **Dev Mode**, then the engine's Settings, Controls, Full screen and Quit to title (which asks first).\n456\t- **Game settings** (via `menu.settings`, group Game):\n457\t\n458\t| Setting | Values |\n459\t| --- | --- |\n460\t| Difficulty | Easy, Normal, Hard, Pro |\n461\t| Timing assist | Tight, Normal, Generous |\n462\t| Auto-run to the ball | on, off |\n463\t| Auto-receive | off by default |\n464\t| Timing ring | on, off |\n465\t| Match camera | Broadcast, Serve Cam |\n466\t| Text speed | Slow, Normal, Fast, Instant |\n467\t| Commentary | on, off |\n468\t| Button symbols | PlayStation, Xbox (patch 2) |\n469\t\n470\t  The Voices volume is in the Sound group (patch 4).\n471\t\n472\t### 4.3 The court and its coordinates\n473\t\n474\tOne `E.TileMap` is used both as the beach to walk around and as the match court.\n475\t\n476\t| Name | Value | Notes |\n477\t| --- | --- | --- |\n478\t| tile | 16 units | engine standard |\n479\t| map | 44 × 28 tiles (704 × 448) | rows 0–5 sea (floor tag `sea`, `block: true`), row 6 wet sand `wet`, rows 7–27 sand `sand`; `outside: false` so the backdrop shows past the far edge |\n480\t| court X0, X1 | 224, 480 | length 256 (128 a side) |\n481\t| net | x = NET_X = 352; top tape z = NET_H = 44; mesh z 28–44 | posts at y = Y0−10 and Y1+10 (h 52); antennae at y = Y0 and Y1, up to z 62 |\n482\t| court Y0, Y1 | 176, 304 | width 128; CY = 240 |\n483\t| serve zones | x < X0 (left) or x > X1 (right), y within the court | the server stands 20 behind the line |\n484\t| lines | 2-unit blue rope lines in `floorTex` on x = X0, X1 and y = Y0, Y1 | beach courts have no centre line |\n485\t| far-side strip | y 112–175 | bleachers, umbrellas, Sonny's DJ booth, Pepper's scorer table and flip scoreboard |\n486\t| left and right sand | x < 224, x > 480 | tiki bar (left), lifeguard tower and loungers (right) |\n487\t| near side | y > 304 | **low props only** (towels, sandcastle, cooler): tall ones would hide the court in Broadcast |\n488\t\n489\t- Draw order: the backdrop (sky, sun, clouds, distant islands, sea) is drawn first, then `map.drawFloor`. Match the\n490\t  `sea` floor color to the backdrop's sea layer by screenshot.\n491\t- Time of day sets the backdrop, `lights.ambient`, the tint, and torches and floodlights (lamppost shapes with lights)\n492\t  at night.\n493\t\n494\t### 4.4 Ball flight (`20-ball.js`)\n495\t\n496\tThe ball is **not** an `E.Body`. It is the current **launch**:\n497\t`{ t0, p: [x, y, z], v: [vx, vy, vz], k, g, ay, wob: { a, w, ph } | null, by, kind }`. `t0` is on the match clock,\n498\t`M.now()` in seconds: `game.time` locally, or `AIHub.time() / 1000` in a hub session.\n499\t\n500\t**Closed form.** With τ = t − t0, e = exp(−kτ), k ≥ 1e-4:\n501\t\n502\t```\n503\tx = x0 + vx(1−e)/k\n504\ty = y0 + vy(1−e)/k + ay(τ/k − (1−e)/k²) + wobble(τ)            wobble = a·sin(wτ + ph)·min(1, τ/0.3)  (float serves)\n505\tz = z0 + (vz + g/k)(1−e)/k − gτ/k\n506\tvelocity: (vx·e,  vy·e + ay(1−e)/k,  (vz + g/k)e − g/k)\n507\t```\n508\t\n509\t- `ball.at(t)` and `ball.vel(t)` are sampled every step for drawing. There is no integration drift, and every machine\n510\t  agrees, which the online play relies on.\n511\t- **Aiming** (`aim(from, to, T)`): given a flight time T,\n512\t  - vx = (xT − x0)·k / (1 − e^(−kT)), and vy the same way (subtract the wind term when `ay` ≠ 0);\n513\t  - vz = ((zT − z0) + gT/k)·k / (1 − e^(−kT)) − g/k.\n514\t- **Flight times by kind:**\n515\t\n516\t| Kind | T |\n517\t| --- | --- |\n518\t| pass | `T.passT` (1.05 s) |\n519\t| set | `T.setT` (1.1 s); quick set .75 |\n520\t| float serve | `T.serveT` (1.3 s) |\n521\t| jump serve | `T.jumpServeT` (.85 s) |\n522\t| spike | from speed: horizontal distance / (spikeSpeed · cos 15°) |\n523\t| shot | `T.shotT` (.95 s) |\n524\t| free ball | 1.2 s |\n525\t| setter dump | .6 s |\n526\t\n527\t- **Precomputed events.** Each new launch computes these once:\n528\t  - `tNet`, when x crosses NET_X (x is monotonic). At that moment:\n529\t    - **clear** if z − r > NET_H;\n530\t    - **tape** (net cord) if z + r ≥ NET_H − 3. A new launch starts from the crossing point: with probability\n531\t      `T.netCordOver` it keeps going (vx·.35, vz 60 ± 20, from the `match` rng), otherwise it drops back (vx·−.3);\n532\t    - **net** if lower: it bounces back (vx·−.25, vy·.5, vz·.3), and the team still has its touches;\n533\t    - **antenna/outside** if |y − CY| > 64 + r: a fault on the team that hit it.\n534\t  - `tLand`, when z = r. Use bisection on the descending branch to 1e-4 s. The ball is **in** when\n535\t    X0 − r ≤ x ≤ X1 + r and Y0 − r ≤ y ≤ Y1 + r (touching the line is in).\n536\t  - `timeAtHeight(h)` (descending branch) and `posAt(t)`, for contact planning.\n537\t- **The ball itself:** radius r = 3.5; a 10-px sprite (white with blue and yellow panels) whose rotation follows its\n538\t  speed; a ground shadow `r.shadow(x, y, 4 − min(2, z·.03), .4)`. The shadow is essential for reading depth.\n539\t- **Landing:** dust (`particles.dust`), `sfx('sand')`, and a ball-mark decal for 2.5 s. The ball rolls about 6 units\n540\t  for show after the point is decided.\n541\t- Players may chase and play the ball outside the court lines, but never past the net plane.\n542\t\n543\t**Default feel** (all of these are sliders): g 330, k .12, r 3.5. With these numbers:\n544\t\n545\t| Shot | Path | Apex / timing |\n546\t| --- | --- | --- |\n547\t| pass | from z 18 to set height 40 | apex ≈ 75 |\n548\t| set | from 40 to the spike contact ≈ 62 | apex ≈ 100 |\n549\t| float serve | from 52 to the floor in 1.3 s | apex ≈ 98; clears the net by ≈ 40 |\n550\t| spike from 20 behind the net, 330 u/s | to 100 beyond the net | lands in ≈ .38 s; clears the tape by ≈ 7 |\n551\t\n552\tA spike hit from far behind the net with a short, sharp target hits the net. Errors come out of the physics.\n553\t\n554\t### 4.5 Rules and referee (`21-rules.js`)\n555\t\n556\t- **Scoring:** rally scoring; one set to `pointsToWin` (vacation 7, final 11, exhibition 7/11/15/21, hub 7); win by 2;\n557\t  hard cap at pointsToWin + 4 (to 7, the first to 11 wins even at 11–10). Exhibition can play best of 3 sets of the\n558\t  same length.\n559\t- **Touches:** at most 3 a side. A block counts as a touch (the beach rule). The same player may not touch twice in a\n560\t  row, except straight after her own block.\n561\t- **Faults** (point to the other team):\n562\t  - the ball lands out after the team's last touch;\n563\t  - a 4th touch;\n564\t  - a double touch;\n565\t  - the ball crosses outside the antennae or under the net;\n566\t  - a **net touch**: an airborne player's hands or body pass NET_X ± 2 while the ball is live within 40 units (rare;\n567\t    mostly from early, fast blocks);\n568\t  - a **serve fault**: into the net, out, or no hit within 1.2 s of the toss.\n569\t- **Serve rotation:** on a side-out the receiving team serves, and its server is the player who did not serve last time\n570\t  for that team. The first serve goes by coin toss: the player's team, unless an event says otherwise.\n571\t- **After a point:** `dead` (1.0 s: the ball settles) → `point` (1.6 s: celebrations) → optional replay → `serveSetup`.\n572\t- **Calls:** big banners with a whistle: \"IN!\", \"OUT!\", \"NET!\", \"4 TOUCHES\", \"DOUBLE TOUCH\", \"ANTENNA\", \"ACE!\", \"KILL!\",\n573\t  \"BLOCK!\", \"NET TOUCH\". Each is text plus an icon, never color alone.\n574\t- **Stats:**\n575\t\n576\t| Scope | Counted |\n577\t| --- | --- |\n578\t| per player | serves, aces, serve faults, digs, perfect passes, sets, kills, attack errors, blocks, points |\n579\t| per match | rallies, longest rally |\n580\t\n581\t### 4.6 Players, actions and the timing judge (`22-players.js`)\n582\t\n583\t**The player entity:** `{ id, side: 0 | 1, slot: 0 | 1, cast, rig, x, y, z, vx, vy, vz, facing, act, input | null, ai,\n584\tcall: 'auto' | 'mine' | 'yours', lockT, stats }`.\n585\t\n586\t**Movement.**\n587\t\n588\t- Speed is `T.runSpeed × (0.86 + 0.03 × SPD)`, default 96, with acceleration 900 u/s². Players face the ball while it\n589\t  is live.\n590\t- They can't cross NET_X (clamp at ±6). They can leave the court, but not the map.\n591\t- **Auto-run** (`T.autoMove`, Settings): while a human's stick is neutral and she is assigned the next contact, she\n592\t  steers toward the contact point at `autoMove ×` her speed.\n593\t\n594\t**Contact planning.** `planContacts(side)` runs whenever a launch heads to a side and after each touch on that side.\n595\tFor each player on that side it computes:\n596\t\n597\t- **kind**, by touch number: 0 = receive/dig, 1 = set, 2 = attack. A ball arriving from the other side is always\n598\t  touch 0."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"99d4115e-ac85-4844-bf9c-39009e8f9714","uuid":"69105862-3904-44be-a512-218d91d10b7c","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:35:59.558Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174749__x8de669/work/PLAN.md","content":"| | `dive` | Left Shift, L | — | 1 ○/B |\n| | `call`: Mine / Yours / Auto | Q, I | Middle | 3 △/Y |\n| | `view`: Broadcast ↔ Serve Cam | V | — | 11 R3 |\n| EXPLORE | `interact` | E, Space, Enter | Left (on a person or thing) | 0 ✕/A |\n| | `run` (hold) | Left Shift | — | 1 ○/B, 7 R2 |\n| | `bag`: gift bag | G | — | 2 □/X |\n| | `leave`: island map | M, Tab | — | 3 △/Y |\n| | `snap`: postcard (not in sessions) | C | — | 8 Create/View |\n| MENU | `confirm` | Enter, Space | Left | 0 ✕/A |\n| | `cancel` | Backspace (Esc on non-pausable screens) | Right | 1 ○/B |\n| | `alt` | F | — | 2 □/X |\n| | `extra` | R | — | 3 △/Y |\n| | `tabL` / `tabR` | Q / E | wheel | 4 L1 / 5 R1 |\n| POOLHOP | `hopA` / `hopB` / `hopX` / `hopY` | J, Space / L, Shift / K, E / I, Q | Left = hopA, Right = hopX | 0 / 1 / 2 / 3 |\n| CASINO | MENU, plus blackjack H hit, S stand, D double, P split; slots J K L stop reels 1-2-3 | | | |\n\n- **Split keyboard (Beach Match).** The engine's half-keys give P1 WASD plus F G H R and P2 the arrows plus `.` `/` `,`\n  `L`. Order the MATCH actions `play, dive, shot, call` so the halves come out as F/`.` = play, G/`/` = dive, H/`,` =\n  shot, R/L = call. Show this on the join screen as keycaps.\n- **Escape.** In pausable scenes Escape opens the pause menu, and Backspace or right click goes back inside our canvas\n  screens. On title and menu screens Escape goes back.\n\n**4.1.2 Device and glyph logic.**\n\n- `G.dev(input)` returns `'ps' | 'xbox' | 'kbm'`. `lastDevice === 'gamepad'` gives `padStyle()`, which follows the\n  Button symbols setting; keyboard or mouse gives `kbm`.\n- `G.prompt(g, x, y, action, text, { input })` draws a glyph icon and the text and returns its width. Prompts redraw from\n  the current device every frame; never cache them.\n- **Glyph icons** are pixel art drawn with `px`:\n\n| Device | How it is drawn |\n| --- | --- |\n| PlayStation | a 9×9 dark disc with the symbol in its color: ✕ `#8fb8ff`, ○ `#ff7a7a`, □ `#f59ad8`, △ `#5fe0b4` |\n| Xbox | a disc in the letter's color, with a dark letter: A `#6ad66a`, B `#ff5a5a`, X `#4aa8ff`, Y `#ffd23a` |\n| Pad shoulders and system buttons | rounded pills: L1/R1/L2/R2 or LB/RB/LT/RT; Options/Create or Menu/View; d-pad and stick icons |\n| Keyboard | a keycap (light rounded rectangle, darker bottom edge) with `input.label(action, 'keyboard')` |\n| Mouse | a 7×9 mouse with the bound button lit |\n\n- `G.ui.promptBar([[action, text], …])` sits at the bottom centre of every screen. Text never says \"press A\": the glyph\n  always comes from the action map.\n\n**4.1.3 Mouse.**\n\n- **Canvas UI:** hover moves focus (`input.pointer()` hit-tested against the widgets laid out last frame); left click\n  activates; right click goes back; the wheel scrolls or pages lists.\n- **World:** hovering an NPC or an interactable highlights it and shows its name (`r.actor(…, { pick: npc })` with\n  `r.pick`). Clicking walks there and interacts.\n- **Matches:** while the last device is keyboard or mouse, a reticle follows `game.mouseGround()` on the opponents' half.\n  Spike, shot and serve aim at it.\n- **Photo mode:** right-drag orbits and the wheel zooms.\n\n**4.1.4 Rumble.** Use `input.rumble`: spikes and serves (.35, .1 s), blocks (.5, .12 s), dives (.3, .15 s), the jackpot\n(.6, .5 s).\n\n**4.1.5 Touch-only gate.**\n\n- `G.touchOnly()` is `matchMedia('(any-pointer: coarse)').matches && !matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches &&\n  !G.sawKeyOrPad`. Check it at boot and on each pointer event.\n- While it is true:\n  - there are no touch controls (patch 7);\n  - the title and menu show a centred panel, **\"Controller or keyboard required\"**, with the line \"Connect a controller\n    or keyboard to play. The demo keeps running.\" and a big **Settings** button (a tap opens `game.menu('settings')`);\n  - the engine corner's menu button stays;\n  - taps do nothing else, and the attract mode runs as usual (a tap ends it, as any input does).\n- The first key or gamepad button sets `G.sawKeyOrPad` and normal play resumes.\n- In an AI Hub session a touch-only player's fighter is played by the AI, with the banner \"Connect a controller or\n  keyboard to take over\".\n\n### 4.2 The 10-foot canvas UI kit (`11-ui.js`)\n\n**Readability rules.** Each one is a review item.\n\n- **Text sizes:** the smallest text anywhere is `E.font` 5×7 at scale 1 with a shadow. Headings are scale 2; screen\n  titles are `E.font.title` at scale 3; numbers that matter (money, score) are scale 2.\n- **Density:** at most 8 focusable items per screen. Item grids are 3×2 (shops, gifts, wardrobe) or 4×2 (album), paged\n  with L1/R1, Q/E or the wheel. There is one detail panel. Never show stat tables: use icons, bars, hearts and short\n  phrases.\n- **Safe area:** keep content inside a 5% margin of `r.W`/`r.H` (TV overscan) and clear of `game.cornerArea()` and\n  `input.touchArea()`.\n- **Focus:** a 2-px gold outline with a 1-px white inner line, a soft additive glow pulse and a 1-px lift. Sounds:\n  `ui_tick` on move, `ui_select` on confirm, `ui_back` on back, `ui_error` on refusal.\n- **Navigation:** d-pad, stick, WASD and arrows move focus spatially to the nearest widget in that direction, repeating\n  via `input.repeat` (0.35 s delay, 0.09 s rate). Confirm and back come from MENU; tabs are L1/R1 and Q/E; the mouse\n  works as in §4.1.3.\n- **Themes:**\n\n| Theme | Panel bg | Border | Ink | Muted | Accent |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Day | `['#0f4c5c', '#0a2d3d']` | `#f6d38a` | `#fff8e8` | `#9fd3d6` | `#ff9e5e` |\n| Night (casino, night villa) | `['#2a1240', '#12081e']` | `#ff5fa2` | as day | as day | `#5ff0ff` |\n\n**Widgets:**\n\n| Widget | Purpose |\n| --- | --- |\n| `Panel` | gradient window (`E.ui.box`) |\n| `Button` | label, optional glyph, disabled state |\n| `List` | vertical menu, scrolls past 8 |\n| `Grid` | cards in rows and columns, paged |\n| `Tabs` | categories; L1/R1 |\n| `Slider` | number; left/right steps, held accelerates, mouse drag; shows the default as a tick |\n| `Toggle`, `Stepper` | ◀ value ▶ |\n| `Card` | item: icon or live rig preview, name, price, NEW/OWNED/WEARING badges |\n| `CharCard` | portrait (`rig.drawPortrait`), name, hearts, mood icon and word |\n| `MoneyBadge` | coin icon and amount, animated count |\n| `ClockBadge` | \"Day 2 · Afternoon\" with sun/moon and weather icons |\n| `Confirm` | yes/no; default No when destructive |\n| `Toast` | slides in at the top for 3 s |\n| `PromptBar` | glyph prompts at the bottom |\n| `Tip` | one line under the focused card |\n\n- **Layout:** `ui.frame(r)` lays out widgets from `r.W`/`r.H` each draw and records hit rects; `update` uses last\n  frame's rects.\n- **E.Shell theme**, for the engine's standard pause, settings and controls screens and for toasts: the day palette,\n  `font: '600 20px/1.35 \"Trebuchet MS\", system-ui, sans-serif'`.\n- **Pause actions:** Resume (engine), **How to Play**, **Take a Postcard** (walkable places and match results only),\n  **Dev Mode**, then the engine's Settings, Controls, Full screen and Quit to title (which asks first).\n- **Game settings** (via `menu.settings`, group Game):\n\n| Setting | Values |\n| --- | --- |\n| Difficulty | Easy, Normal, Hard, Pro |\n| Timing assist | Tight, Normal, Generous |\n| Auto-run to the ball | on, off |\n| Auto-receive | off by default |\n| Timing ring | on, off |\n| Match camera | Broadcast, Serve Cam |\n| Text speed | Slow, Normal, Fast, Instant |\n| Commentary | on, off |\n| Button symbols | PlayStation, Xbox (patch 2) |\n\n  The Voices volume is in the Sound group (patch 4).\n\n### 4.3 The court and its coordinates\n\nOne `E.TileMap` is used both as the beach to walk around and as the match court.\n\n| Name | Value | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| tile | 16 units | engine standard |\n| map | 44 × 28 tiles (704 × 448) | rows 0–5 sea (floor tag `sea`, `block: true`), row 6 wet sand `wet`, rows 7–27 sand `sand`; `outside: false` so the backdrop shows past the far edge |\n| court X0, X1 | 224, 480 | length 256 (128 a side) |\n| net | x = NET_X = 352; top tape z = NET_H = 44; mesh z 28–44 | posts at y = Y0−10 and Y1+10 (h 52); antennae at y = Y0 and Y1, up to z 62 |\n| court Y0, Y1 | 176, 304 | width 128; CY = 240 |\n| serve zones | x < X0 (left) or x > X1 (right), y within the court | the server stands 20 behind the line |\n| lines | 2-unit blue rope lines in `floorTex` on x = X0, X1 and y = Y0, Y1 | beach courts have no centre line |\n| far-side strip | y 112–175 | bleachers, umbrellas, Sonny's DJ booth, Pepper's scorer table and flip scoreboard |\n| left and right sand | x < 224, x > 480 | tiki bar (left), lifeguard tower and loungers (right) |\n| near side | y > 304 | **low props only** (towels, sandcastle, cooler): tall ones would hide the court in Broadcast |\n\n- Draw order: the backdrop (sky, sun, clouds, distant islands, sea) is drawn first, then `map.drawFloor`. Match the\n  `sea` floor color to the backdrop's sea layer by screenshot.\n- Time of day sets the backdrop, `lights.ambient`, the tint, and torches and floodlights (lamppost shapes with lights)\n  at night.\n\n### 4.4 Ball flight (`20-ball.js`)\n\nThe ball is **not** an `E.Body`. It is the current **launch**:\n`{ t0, p: [x, y, z], v: [vx, vy, vz], k, g, ay, wob: { a, w, ph } | null, by, kind }`. `t0` is on the match clock,\n`M.now()` in seconds: `game.time` locally, or `AIHub.time() / 1000` in a hub session.\n\n**Closed form.** With τ = t − t0, e = exp(−kτ), k ≥ 1e-4:\n\n```\nx = x0 + vx(1−e)/k\ny = y0 + vy(1−e)/k + ay(τ/k − (1−e)/k²) + wobble(τ)            wobble = a·sin(wτ + ph)·min(1, τ/0.3)  (float serves)\nz = z0 + (vz + g/k)(1−e)/k − gτ/k\nvelocity: (vx·e,  vy·e + ay(1−e)/k,  (vz + g/k)e − g/k)\n```\n\n- `ball.at(t)` and `ball.vel(t)` are sampled every step for drawing. There is no integration drift, and every machine\n  agrees, which the online play relies on.\n- **Aiming** (`aim(from, to, T)`): given a flight time T,\n  - vx = (xT − x0)·k / (1 − e^(−kT)), and vy the same way (subtract the wind term when `ay` ≠ 0);\n  - vz = ((zT − z0) + gT/k)·k / (1 − e^(−kT)) − g/k.\n- **Flight times by kind:**\n\n| Kind | T |\n| --- | --- |\n| pass | `T.passT` (1.05 s) |\n| set | `T.setT` (1.1 s); quick set .75 |\n| float serve | `T.serveT` (1.3 s) |\n| jump serve | `T.jumpServeT` (.85 s) |\n| spike | from speed: horizontal distance / (spikeSpeed · cos 15°) |\n| shot | `T.shotT` (.95 s) |\n| free ball | 1.2 s |\n| setter dump | .6 s |\n\n- **Precomputed events.** Each new launch computes these once:\n  - `tNet`, when x crosses NET_X (x is monotonic). At that moment:\n    - **clear** if z − r > NET_H;\n    - **tape** (net cord) if z + r ≥ NET_H − 3. A new launch starts from the crossing point: with probability\n      `T.netCordOver` it keeps going (vx·.35, vz 60 ± 20, from the `match` rng), otherwise it drops back (vx·−.3);\n    - **net** if lower: it bounces back (vx·−.25, vy·.5, vz·.3), and the team still has its touches;\n    - **antenna/outside** if |y − CY| > 64 + r: a fault on the team that hit it.\n  - `tLand`, when z = r. Use bisection on the descending branch to 1e-4 s. The ball is **in** when\n    X0 − r ≤ x ≤ X1 + r and Y0 − r ≤ y ≤ Y1 + r (touching the line is in).\n  - `timeAtHeight(h)` (descending branch) and `posAt(t)`, for contact planning.\n- **The ball itself:** radius r = 3.5; a 10-px sprite (white with blue and yellow panels) whose rotation follows its\n  speed; a ground shadow `r.shadow(x, y, 4 − min(2, z·.03), .4)`. The shadow is essential for reading depth.\n- **Landing:** dust (`particles.dust`), `sfx('sand')`, and a ball-mark decal for 2.5 s. The ball rolls about 6 units\n  for show after the point is decided.\n- Players may chase and play the ball outside the court lines, but never past the net plane.\n\n**Default feel** (all of these are sliders): g 330, k .12, r 3.5. With these numbers:\n\n| Shot | Path | Apex / timing |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| pass | from z 18 to set height 40 | apex ≈ 75 |\n| set | from 40 to the spike contact ≈ 62 | apex ≈ 100 |\n| float serve | from 52 to the floor in 1.3 s | apex ≈ 98; clears the net by ≈ 40 |\n| spike from 20 behind the net, 330 u/s | to 100 beyond the net | lands in ≈ .38 s; clears the tape by ≈ 7 |\n\nA spike hit from far behind the net with a short, sharp target hits the net. Errors come out of the physics.\n\n### 4.5 Rules and referee (`21-rules.js`)\n\n- **Scoring:** rally scoring; one set to `pointsToWin` (vacation 7, final 11, exhibition 7/11/15/21, hub 7); win by 2;\n  hard cap at pointsToWin + 4 (to 7, the first to 11 wins even at 11–10). Exhibition can play best of 3 sets of the\n  same length.\n- **Touches:** at most 3 a side. A block counts as a touch (the beach rule). The same player may not touch twice in a\n  row, except straight after her own block.\n- **Faults** (point to the other team):\n  - the ball lands out after the team's last touch;\n  - a 4th touch;\n  - a double touch;\n  - the ball crosses outside the antennae or under the net;\n  - a **net touch**: an airborne player's hands or body pass NET_X ± 2 while the ball is live within 40 units (rare;\n    mostly from early, fast blocks);\n  - a **serve fault**: into the net, out, or no hit within 1.2 s of the toss.\n- **Serve rotation:** on a side-out the receiving team serves, and its server is the player who did not serve last time\n  for that team. The first serve goes by coin toss: the player's team, unless an event says otherwise.\n- **After a point:** `dead` (1.0 s: the ball settles) → `point` (1.6 s: celebrations) → optional replay → `serveSetup`.\n- **Calls:** big banners with a whistle: \"IN!\", \"OUT!\", \"NET!\", \"4 TOUCHES\", \"DOUBLE TOUCH\", \"ANTENNA\", \"ACE!\", \"KILL!\",\n  \"BLOCK!\", \"NET TOUCH\". Each is text plus an icon, never color alone.\n- **Stats:**\n\n| Scope | Counted |\n| --- | --- |\n| per player | serves, aces, serve faults, digs, perfect passes, sets, kills, attack errors, blocks, points |\n| per match | rallies, longest rally |\n\n### 4.6 Players, actions and the timing judge (`22-players.js`)\n\n**The player entity:** `{ id, side: 0 | 1, slot: 0 | 1, cast, rig, x, y, z, vx, vy, vz, facing, act, input | null, ai,\ncall: 'auto' | 'mine' | 'yours', lockT, stats }`.\n\n**Movement.**\n\n- Speed is `T.runSpeed × (0.86 + 0.03 × SPD)`, default 96, with acceleration 900 u/s². Players face the ball while it\n  is live.\n- They can't cross NET_X (clamp at ±6). They can leave the court, but not the map.\n- **Auto-run** (`T.autoMove`, Settings): while a human's stick is neutral and she is assigned the next contact, she\n  steers toward the contact point at `autoMove ×` her speed.\n\n**Contact planning.** `planContacts(side)` runs whenever a launch heads to a side and after each touch on that side.\nFor each player on that side it computes:\n\n- **kind**, by touch number: 0 = receive/dig, 1 = set, 2 = attack. A ball arriving from the other side is always\n  touch 0.","numLines":260,"startLine":339,"totalLines":2180}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01QaynHKQCv9hNnGJBKVhQBA","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
