{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh2iczhe4nfN85V5jYMF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JZaLAvUpt4U6wcytCcvAqd","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174749__x8de669/work/PLAN.md","offset":797,"limit":230},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6817,"cache_read_input_tokens":503573,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6817},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"99d4115e-ac85-4844-bf9c-39009e8f9714","uuid":"d7306abc-d1dc-42e9-8416-96a7bd1422c5","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:36:16.584Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh2ickpkX3b5dSvfePX5","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01JZaLAvUpt4U6wcytCcvAqd":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174749__x8de669/work/PLAN.md","offset":797,"limit":230}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JZaLAvUpt4U6wcytCcvAqd","type":"tool_result","content":"797\t\"Leaving ends the Morning.\"); leaving the casino at night; Rest in the villa. Talking, gifting, shopping and changing\n798\tclothes inside a location don't.\n799\t\n800\t**At night** only the Villa, the Casino and story events are open. The map shows the rest as closed.\n801\t\n802\t**Day start** (seeded from `world`):\n803\t\n804\t- roll moods, form NPC teams, place NPCs by schedule, rotate shop stock (2 items per shop);\n805\t- set the weather from the table: D1 sunny; D2 sunny or cloudy; D3 cloudy morning, rain in the afternoon, clear night;\n806\t  D4 sunny; D5 sunny with a golden afternoon (sunset light);\n807\t- autosave.\n808\t\n809\t**Day end (sleep)** shows a summary card: money earned and spent, matches, affinity changes (arrows by each portrait),\n810\ttomorrow's weather. Then:\n811\t\n812\t- your partner leaves if you lost a match that day and her affinity is below 35;\n813\t- affinity drifts `T.affinityDecay` (2) toward its base value for every NPC you didn't talk to;\n814\t- NPC pairs \"play\" each other off-screen for that day's record: one simulated result per pair from skills on the\n815\t  `world` rng. The Match Board shows records like \"Lola & Tess 3–1\".\n816\t\n817\t**Schedules** (weights in §5.4).\n818\t\n819\t- Each NPC has weights over locations for each slot, changed by weather and mood; the `world` rng picks.\n820\t- NPC team-mates go together, to the place chosen for the first one.\n821\t- Story events override the schedule.\n822\t- Guarantee at least one NPC pair at the Beach in every daytime slot.\n823\t- Your partner isn't scheduled: she \"jogs over\" whenever you open the Match Board.\n824\t\n825\t**Moods.**\n826\t\n827\t| Mood | Icon and word |\n828\t| --- | --- |\n829\t| Happy | ☀ |\n830\t| Normal | ◐ |\n831\t| Gloomy | ☁ |\n832\t\n833\tDaily roll 35/45/20. One step up if the weather is one she likes; one step down if you beat her yesterday or the\n834\tweather is one she dislikes. Mood shifts gift thresholds and invite chances.\n835\t\n836\t### 4.11 Affinity, gifts and team-ups (`30-vacation.js`, `32-location.js`)\n837\t\n838\t**Affinity** is 0–100 between you and each NPC: one symmetric number per pair, shown as 5 hearts in half steps. Start\n839\tvalues come from the table in §5.3.\n840\t\n841\t| Stage | Affinity |\n842\t| --- | --- |\n843\t| Stranger | 0–19 |\n844\t| Acquaintance | 20–39 |\n845\t| Friend | 40–59 |\n846\t| Good Friend | 60–79 |\n847\t| Best Friend | 80–100 |\n848\t\n849\t**Changes.** Positive changes are multiplied by `T.affinityGainMul`.\n850\t\n851\t| Cause | Change |\n852\t| --- | --- |\n853\t| chat, first of the day | +2 |\n854\t| chat, later (once per slot) | +1 |\n855\t| gift loved / liked / neutral | +12 / +6 / +2 |\n856\t| gift disliked | −6 (and the gift comes back to your bag) |\n857\t| your team wins / loses | +6 / −2 (−5 if she is Gloomy) |\n858\t| you beat her team | −3 (+1 for good sports: Tess and Rin) |\n859\t| event choices | ±4 |\n860\t| winning the final, for your partner | +10 |\n861\t\n862\t**Gift acceptance.** score = taste + stage bonus + mood.\n863\t\n864\t- taste: love 3, like 2, neutral 0, dislike −3;\n865\t- stage bonus: Friend 1, Good Friend 1, Best Friend 2;\n866\t- mood: Happy +1, Normal 0, Gloomy −1.\n867\t\n868\tShe accepts if score ≥ `T.giftThreshold` (0). So neutral gifts are accepted unless she is a Gloomy stranger, and\n869\tdislikes are refused unless she is a Happy Best Friend. One gift per NPC per slot.\n870\t\n871\t**Reactions:**\n872\t\n873\t| Reaction | Animation and sound |\n874\t| --- | --- |\n875\t| love | jumps, a burst of hearts, \"I love it!\"-style line, jingle `gift_love` |\n876\t| like | smile and nod |\n877\t| neutral | polite nod |\n878\t| refuse | folded arms and a head shake (`Reject` or `Idle_FoldArms`), jingle `gift_refuse` |\n879\t\n880\t**Known likes.** The first time you see her reaction to an item, record it in `known[npc][item]`. The Villa journal's\n881\tFriends page shows what you've learned as icons.\n882\t\n883\t**Team-up.**\n884\t\n885\t- She accepts if affinity ≥ `T.inviteThreshold` (40), with the threshold −10 if she's Happy and +10 if Gloomy.\n886\t- If she's already on an NPC team she needs 20 more. Her old team-mate then goes solo and is sour with you (−4).\n887\t- You have one partner at a time. Switching asks first (\"Tess will be disappointed…\").\n888\t- Partner chemistry is her affinity, shown as hearts on the match HUD.\n889\t\n890\t**Swimsuit gifts.** A suit you give must match one of her tastes or she refuses it (\"Not really my style\"). An accepted\n891\tsuit becomes her outfit (in matches and around the island), and she keeps it.\n892\t\n893\t### 4.12 Money, shops, wardrobe, inventory (`33-shop.js`)\n894\t\n895\t**Currency:** Sonny Dollars, written S$12,500. You start with S$30,000 (`T.startMoney`).\n896\t\n897\t**Income** (match prizes × `T.prizeMul`):\n898\t\n899\t| Source | Amount |\n900\t| --- | --- |\n901\t| match win | S$ (12,000 + 3,000·day + 1,000·winning margin) |\n902\t| match loss | S$3,000 |\n903\t| tutorial | S$10,000 |\n904\t| semifinal win | S$30,000 |\n905\t| final win | S$100,000 and the \"Fortuna Gold\" suit |\n906\t| Pool Hop | S$ (2,000 + 400·perfects + 150·seconds left) |\n907\t| casino | chips cashed out at S$100 each |\n908\t\n909\t**Shops**, all on the Promenade. Each has fixed core stock plus 2 items that rotate daily (seeded) and carry a NEW\n910\tbadge. Prices × `T.priceMul`.\n911\t\n912\t| Shop | Keeper | Sells |\n913\t| --- | --- | --- |\n914\t| **Riptide Sports** | Coach Bo | sporty suits, sports accessories, sports gifts |\n915\t| **Coral Couture** | Odette | fashion suits and accessories, fashion gifts |\n916\t| **Sundries & Smiles** | Kai | food, goods and books gifts, the luchador mask |\n917\t\n918\t**The shop screen.**\n919\t\n920\t- Category tabs; a 3×2 card grid; a detail panel.\n921\t- For suits and accessories, a **live rig of your fighter wearing the focused item** turns on a pedestal (right stick,\n922\t  L1/R1 or a mouse drag). □ \"Try on\" switches between the item and your current outfit.\n923\t- ✕ buys. A confirm appears when the price is over 30% of your money.\n924\t- Badges show OWNED and WEARING. Items you can't afford are dimmed with the shortfall shown.\n925\t- The keeper's portrait says a short quip, with voice.\n926\t\n927\t**Wardrobe** (the Villa closet, and the changing hut at the Beach and Pool): the suits and accessories you own; ✕\n928\tequip, □ remove an accessory, the same rotating preview. A second page shows your partner and the suits she has\n929\taccepted.\n930\t\n931\t**Gift Bag:** counts per gift, sorted by category, at most 9 of each. Opened from talk menus, or with □ on the map or in\n932\ta location to browse.\n933\t\n934\t### 4.13 Island map (`31-map.js`)\n935\t\n936\t**The map:** an iso view of Isla Fortuna, a TileMap of about 48×36 tiles.\n937\t\n938\t- Sea all round (`outside` set to the sea color, animated water floor at the edges); beaches, grass, palm groves.\n939\t- A dormant volcano: stepped rock walls, 3 levels, with steam wisps.\n940\t- The lagoon pool, the courts, the Promenade, a row of villas, the casino (neon at night), the Dock with Sonny's\n941\t  seaplane, a lighthouse.\n942\t\n943\t**Pins:** Sunset Courts, Lagoon Pool, Fortuna Promenade, Your Villa, Casino Fortuna (night only), and the Dock (shown\n944\tgreyed: \"Departures only\").\n945\t\n946\t**Controls.**\n947\t\n948\t- The stick or d-pad jumps the cursor to the nearest pin in that direction; L1/R1 cycle pins; mouse hover highlights\n949\t  (`r.pick`).\n950\t- ✕ or a click opens the **location card**: name, a small picture, who's there (portraits with mood icons, NPC pairs\n951\t  marked), activities, open or closed. ✕ again travels, with an `iris` transition at the pin.\n952\t- □ opens Friends (affinity overview), △ the Journal (save, stats), Options pauses.\n953\t\n954\t**The header** shows the ClockBadge, the MoneyBadge and the partner card.\n955\t\n956\t**Sky and weather:** a morning pastel sky, a bright afternoon, a night of stars, lit windows and neon; weather\n957\tparticles.\n958\t\n959\t### 4.14 Walkable locations (`32-location.js`)\n960\t\n961\t**One scene, driven by data per location** (§5.4): a TileMap in `threequarter`, the outside color or a backdrop,\n962\tshapes (`map.solid` for collision), NPC spots, interactables, music and ambience, exits.\n963\t\n964\t- **You:** an `E.Body` (r 5) moving at 70 units/s walking and 110 running, with the camera on you\n965\t  (`game.follow(hero, { z: 16 })`, `cam.bounds`). Lights and GPU lighting come on at night.\n966\t- **NPCs present** (from the schedule) sit at spots doing idle activities and turn their heads toward you within 40\n967\t  units.\n968\t- **Talk.** Interact within 22 units opens the talk panel: her portrait, mood, hearts, and a vertical list.\n969\t\n970\t| Choice | Notes |\n971\t| --- | --- |\n972\t| **Chat** | |\n973\t| **Give a Gift** | |\n974\t| **Team Up** | if she isn't your partner; for your partner: \"Our next match?\", which opens the Match Board |\n975\t| **Challenge** | beach only, when she's in a pair |\n976\t| **Bye** | |\n977\t\n978\t- **Interactables:**\n979\t\n980\t| Place | Interactables |\n981\t| --- | --- |\n982\t| Beach | Match Board (challengeable pairs with difficulty stars and records, your partner, Play) |\n983\t| Pool | Pool Hop start deck |\n984\t| Promenade | three shop doors, the changing hut |\n985\t| Villa | bed (Rest / Sleep), closet (Wardrobe), desk (Journal), album frame, mailbox (letters) |\n986\t| Night | the casino entrance |\n987\t\n988\t- **Leaving:** walk to the exit, or press `leave` (△ / M / Tab), then confirm \"Leave? This ends the Afternoon.\" Back on\n989\t  the map, it is the next slot.\n990\t\n991\t### 4.15 Pool Hop (`40-poolhop.js`)\n992\t\n993\t**Goal:** cross the lagoon on 32 floating pads in `T.poolTime` (40 s). Each pad shows the glyph of one of the four face\n994\tbuttons for the current device (✕○□△, A B X Y, or J L K I keycaps). Press it as the hopper lands, on the beat.\n995\t\n996\t**Rhythm.**\n997\t\n998\t- The song `lagoon` runs at `T.poolBpm` (112) with `sync: true`. One hop per beat, judged against the music clock\n999\t  (`audio.pos`).\n1000\t- PERFECT is within 60 ms and GOOD within 130 ms (× `T.poolWindowMul`).\n1001\t- Too early, too late or the wrong button: she slips, splashes, swims back (1.8 s), and continues from the same pad on\n1002\t  the next bar.\n1003\t- Each run of 8 PERFECT hops in a row adds +1 s.\n1004\t\n1005\t**Twists:**\n1006\t\n1007\t- from pad 12, **wobble pads**: the glyph flips between two buttons and settles one beat before you need it;\n1008\t- from pad 22, **double pads**: two glyphs; press both together.\n1009\t\n1010\t**Score and reward.** Time, perfects and falls give the prize (§4.12). Your best time is saved. Characters at the pool\n1011\tcheer, and a present partner gains +2 affinity when you clear it.\n1012\t\n1013\t**Camera and effects:** the Broadcast angle follows the hopper; pads bob to the beat; splashes; water shimmer.\n1014\t\n1015\tThe attract mode runs Pool Hop with a perfect bot.\n1016\t\n1017\t### 4.16 Casino Fortuna (`41-casino.js`, nights only)\n1018\t\n1019\t**The floor** is a `threequarter` map with neon, chandeliers and lights, and a crowd. Stations:\n1020\t\n1021\t- **Cashier:** chips at S$100 each; buy in steps of 10, 50 or 100; cash out any time. The chip count shows on every\n1022\t  casino screen.\n1023\t- **6 slot machines.**\n1024\t- **Blackjack table**, dealer Pepper.\n1025\t- **Roulette table**, croupier Kai.\n1026\t- **Sonny's VIP lounge**, for story events."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"99d4115e-ac85-4844-bf9c-39009e8f9714","uuid":"a2090acc-b735-48db-8581-34b9acf8cae2","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:36:16.590Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174749__x8de669/work/PLAN.md","content":"\"Leaving ends the Morning.\"); leaving the casino at night; Rest in the villa. Talking, gifting, shopping and changing\nclothes inside a location don't.\n\n**At night** only the Villa, the Casino and story events are open. The map shows the rest as closed.\n\n**Day start** (seeded from `world`):\n\n- roll moods, form NPC teams, place NPCs by schedule, rotate shop stock (2 items per shop);\n- set the weather from the table: D1 sunny; D2 sunny or cloudy; D3 cloudy morning, rain in the afternoon, clear night;\n  D4 sunny; D5 sunny with a golden afternoon (sunset light);\n- autosave.\n\n**Day end (sleep)** shows a summary card: money earned and spent, matches, affinity changes (arrows by each portrait),\ntomorrow's weather. Then:\n\n- your partner leaves if you lost a match that day and her affinity is below 35;\n- affinity drifts `T.affinityDecay` (2) toward its base value for every NPC you didn't talk to;\n- NPC pairs \"play\" each other off-screen for that day's record: one simulated result per pair from skills on the\n  `world` rng. The Match Board shows records like \"Lola & Tess 3–1\".\n\n**Schedules** (weights in §5.4).\n\n- Each NPC has weights over locations for each slot, changed by weather and mood; the `world` rng picks.\n- NPC team-mates go together, to the place chosen for the first one.\n- Story events override the schedule.\n- Guarantee at least one NPC pair at the Beach in every daytime slot.\n- Your partner isn't scheduled: she \"jogs over\" whenever you open the Match Board.\n\n**Moods.**\n\n| Mood | Icon and word |\n| --- | --- |\n| Happy | ☀ |\n| Normal | ◐ |\n| Gloomy | ☁ |\n\nDaily roll 35/45/20. One step up if the weather is one she likes; one step down if you beat her yesterday or the\nweather is one she dislikes. Mood shifts gift thresholds and invite chances.\n\n### 4.11 Affinity, gifts and team-ups (`30-vacation.js`, `32-location.js`)\n\n**Affinity** is 0–100 between you and each NPC: one symmetric number per pair, shown as 5 hearts in half steps. Start\nvalues come from the table in §5.3.\n\n| Stage | Affinity |\n| --- | --- |\n| Stranger | 0–19 |\n| Acquaintance | 20–39 |\n| Friend | 40–59 |\n| Good Friend | 60–79 |\n| Best Friend | 80–100 |\n\n**Changes.** Positive changes are multiplied by `T.affinityGainMul`.\n\n| Cause | Change |\n| --- | --- |\n| chat, first of the day | +2 |\n| chat, later (once per slot) | +1 |\n| gift loved / liked / neutral | +12 / +6 / +2 |\n| gift disliked | −6 (and the gift comes back to your bag) |\n| your team wins / loses | +6 / −2 (−5 if she is Gloomy) |\n| you beat her team | −3 (+1 for good sports: Tess and Rin) |\n| event choices | ±4 |\n| winning the final, for your partner | +10 |\n\n**Gift acceptance.** score = taste + stage bonus + mood.\n\n- taste: love 3, like 2, neutral 0, dislike −3;\n- stage bonus: Friend 1, Good Friend 1, Best Friend 2;\n- mood: Happy +1, Normal 0, Gloomy −1.\n\nShe accepts if score ≥ `T.giftThreshold` (0). So neutral gifts are accepted unless she is a Gloomy stranger, and\ndislikes are refused unless she is a Happy Best Friend. One gift per NPC per slot.\n\n**Reactions:**\n\n| Reaction | Animation and sound |\n| --- | --- |\n| love | jumps, a burst of hearts, \"I love it!\"-style line, jingle `gift_love` |\n| like | smile and nod |\n| neutral | polite nod |\n| refuse | folded arms and a head shake (`Reject` or `Idle_FoldArms`), jingle `gift_refuse` |\n\n**Known likes.** The first time you see her reaction to an item, record it in `known[npc][item]`. The Villa journal's\nFriends page shows what you've learned as icons.\n\n**Team-up.**\n\n- She accepts if affinity ≥ `T.inviteThreshold` (40), with the threshold −10 if she's Happy and +10 if Gloomy.\n- If she's already on an NPC team she needs 20 more. Her old team-mate then goes solo and is sour with you (−4).\n- You have one partner at a time. Switching asks first (\"Tess will be disappointed…\").\n- Partner chemistry is her affinity, shown as hearts on the match HUD.\n\n**Swimsuit gifts.** A suit you give must match one of her tastes or she refuses it (\"Not really my style\"). An accepted\nsuit becomes her outfit (in matches and around the island), and she keeps it.\n\n### 4.12 Money, shops, wardrobe, inventory (`33-shop.js`)\n\n**Currency:** Sonny Dollars, written S$12,500. You start with S$30,000 (`T.startMoney`).\n\n**Income** (match prizes × `T.prizeMul`):\n\n| Source | Amount |\n| --- | --- |\n| match win | S$ (12,000 + 3,000·day + 1,000·winning margin) |\n| match loss | S$3,000 |\n| tutorial | S$10,000 |\n| semifinal win | S$30,000 |\n| final win | S$100,000 and the \"Fortuna Gold\" suit |\n| Pool Hop | S$ (2,000 + 400·perfects + 150·seconds left) |\n| casino | chips cashed out at S$100 each |\n\n**Shops**, all on the Promenade. Each has fixed core stock plus 2 items that rotate daily (seeded) and carry a NEW\nbadge. Prices × `T.priceMul`.\n\n| Shop | Keeper | Sells |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **Riptide Sports** | Coach Bo | sporty suits, sports accessories, sports gifts |\n| **Coral Couture** | Odette | fashion suits and accessories, fashion gifts |\n| **Sundries & Smiles** | Kai | food, goods and books gifts, the luchador mask |\n\n**The shop screen.**\n\n- Category tabs; a 3×2 card grid; a detail panel.\n- For suits and accessories, a **live rig of your fighter wearing the focused item** turns on a pedestal (right stick,\n  L1/R1 or a mouse drag). □ \"Try on\" switches between the item and your current outfit.\n- ✕ buys. A confirm appears when the price is over 30% of your money.\n- Badges show OWNED and WEARING. Items you can't afford are dimmed with the shortfall shown.\n- The keeper's portrait says a short quip, with voice.\n\n**Wardrobe** (the Villa closet, and the changing hut at the Beach and Pool): the suits and accessories you own; ✕\nequip, □ remove an accessory, the same rotating preview. A second page shows your partner and the suits she has\naccepted.\n\n**Gift Bag:** counts per gift, sorted by category, at most 9 of each. Opened from talk menus, or with □ on the map or in\na location to browse.\n\n### 4.13 Island map (`31-map.js`)\n\n**The map:** an iso view of Isla Fortuna, a TileMap of about 48×36 tiles.\n\n- Sea all round (`outside` set to the sea color, animated water floor at the edges); beaches, grass, palm groves.\n- A dormant volcano: stepped rock walls, 3 levels, with steam wisps.\n- The lagoon pool, the courts, the Promenade, a row of villas, the casino (neon at night), the Dock with Sonny's\n  seaplane, a lighthouse.\n\n**Pins:** Sunset Courts, Lagoon Pool, Fortuna Promenade, Your Villa, Casino Fortuna (night only), and the Dock (shown\ngreyed: \"Departures only\").\n\n**Controls.**\n\n- The stick or d-pad jumps the cursor to the nearest pin in that direction; L1/R1 cycle pins; mouse hover highlights\n  (`r.pick`).\n- ✕ or a click opens the **location card**: name, a small picture, who's there (portraits with mood icons, NPC pairs\n  marked), activities, open or closed. ✕ again travels, with an `iris` transition at the pin.\n- □ opens Friends (affinity overview), △ the Journal (save, stats), Options pauses.\n\n**The header** shows the ClockBadge, the MoneyBadge and the partner card.\n\n**Sky and weather:** a morning pastel sky, a bright afternoon, a night of stars, lit windows and neon; weather\nparticles.\n\n### 4.14 Walkable locations (`32-location.js`)\n\n**One scene, driven by data per location** (§5.4): a TileMap in `threequarter`, the outside color or a backdrop,\nshapes (`map.solid` for collision), NPC spots, interactables, music and ambience, exits.\n\n- **You:** an `E.Body` (r 5) moving at 70 units/s walking and 110 running, with the camera on you\n  (`game.follow(hero, { z: 16 })`, `cam.bounds`). Lights and GPU lighting come on at night.\n- **NPCs present** (from the schedule) sit at spots doing idle activities and turn their heads toward you within 40\n  units.\n- **Talk.** Interact within 22 units opens the talk panel: her portrait, mood, hearts, and a vertical list.\n\n| Choice | Notes |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Chat** | |\n| **Give a Gift** | |\n| **Team Up** | if she isn't your partner; for your partner: \"Our next match?\", which opens the Match Board |\n| **Challenge** | beach only, when she's in a pair |\n| **Bye** | |\n\n- **Interactables:**\n\n| Place | Interactables |\n| --- | --- |\n| Beach | Match Board (challengeable pairs with difficulty stars and records, your partner, Play) |\n| Pool | Pool Hop start deck |\n| Promenade | three shop doors, the changing hut |\n| Villa | bed (Rest / Sleep), closet (Wardrobe), desk (Journal), album frame, mailbox (letters) |\n| Night | the casino entrance |\n\n- **Leaving:** walk to the exit, or press `leave` (△ / M / Tab), then confirm \"Leave? This ends the Afternoon.\" Back on\n  the map, it is the next slot.\n\n### 4.15 Pool Hop (`40-poolhop.js`)\n\n**Goal:** cross the lagoon on 32 floating pads in `T.poolTime` (40 s). Each pad shows the glyph of one of the four face\nbuttons for the current device (✕○□△, A B X Y, or J L K I keycaps). Press it as the hopper lands, on the beat.\n\n**Rhythm.**\n\n- The song `lagoon` runs at `T.poolBpm` (112) with `sync: true`. One hop per beat, judged against the music clock\n  (`audio.pos`).\n- PERFECT is within 60 ms and GOOD within 130 ms (× `T.poolWindowMul`).\n- Too early, too late or the wrong button: she slips, splashes, swims back (1.8 s), and continues from the same pad on\n  the next bar.\n- Each run of 8 PERFECT hops in a row adds +1 s.\n\n**Twists:**\n\n- from pad 12, **wobble pads**: the glyph flips between two buttons and settles one beat before you need it;\n- from pad 22, **double pads**: two glyphs; press both together.\n\n**Score and reward.** Time, perfects and falls give the prize (§4.12). Your best time is saved. Characters at the pool\ncheer, and a present partner gains +2 affinity when you clear it.\n\n**Camera and effects:** the Broadcast angle follows the hopper; pads bob to the beat; splashes; water shimmer.\n\nThe attract mode runs Pool Hop with a perfect bot.\n\n### 4.16 Casino Fortuna (`41-casino.js`, nights only)\n\n**The floor** is a `threequarter` map with neon, chandeliers and lights, and a crowd. Stations:\n\n- **Cashier:** chips at S$100 each; buy in steps of 10, 50 or 100; cash out any time. The chip count shows on every\n  casino screen.\n- **6 slot machines.**\n- **Blackjack table**, dealer Pepper.\n- **Roulette table**, croupier Kai.\n- **Sonny's VIP lounge**, for story events.","numLines":230,"startLine":797,"totalLines":2180}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01JZaLAvUpt4U6wcytCcvAqd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
