{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh2j5tDpS2Q6TMsUryqn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Kako114wVqhXXi2TKobWZA","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174749__x8de669/work/PLAN.md","offset":1026,"limit":200},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5533,"cache_read_input_tokens":510390,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5533},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"99d4115e-ac85-4844-bf9c-39009e8f9714","uuid":"918973aa-1a75-4605-ac8c-18a61ae3586f","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:36:24.140Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh2j5daoJB7Pd1dtXeVV","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Kako114wVqhXXi2TKobWZA":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174749__x8de669/work/PLAN.md","offset":1026,"limit":200}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Kako114wVqhXXi2TKobWZA","type":"tool_result","content":"1026\t- **Sonny's VIP lounge**, for story events.\n1027\t\n1028\tOn the first night Sonny hands you 20 free chips and explains the games. A prize counter swaps 300 chips for the\n1029\t\"Jackpot\" suit.\n1030\t\n1031\t**Fortuna Sevens (pachislot).**\n1032\t\n1033\t- 3 reels with 3 visible rows. Bet 1, 2 or 3 chips: 1 = the centre line, 2 = plus the top and bottom lines, 3 = plus\n1034\t  both diagonals.\n1035\t- ✕ / Space spins. Then ✕ ○ □ (J K L) stop reels 1, 2 and 3. A stop \"slips\" 0–4 symbols on the `casino` rng, so\n1036\t  timing matters a little.\n1037\t- Strips of 21 stops per reel. Payouts per line bet:\n1038\t\n1039\t| Line | Pays |\n1040\t| --- | --- |\n1041\t| 7-7-7 | ×100, with a jackpot fanfare and coin shower |\n1042\t| BAR-BAR-BAR | ×30 |\n1043\t| Sonny-Sonny-Sonny | ×20 (Sonny is wild) |\n1044\t| Volleyball ×3 | ×12 |\n1045\t| Palm ×3 | ×8 |\n1046\t| Coconut ×3 | ×5 |\n1047\t| Cherry, by count on the line | 1 ×2, 2 ×5, 3 ×10 |\n1048\t\n1049\t- Tune the strips so the RTP is **92% ± 3** at `T.slotsPayMul` 1 (a simulation test checks it).\n1050\t- Spinning reels show blur rows, then a stop clunk and a line highlight.\n1051\t\n1052\t**Blackjack.**\n1053\t\n1054\t- 6-deck shoe, reshuffled at 75%. The dealer stands on soft 17 (`T.dealerHitsSoft17` toggles it). Blackjack pays 3:2.\n1055\t  Double on any first two cards. Split once; split aces get one card each. No insurance, no surrender.\n1056\t- Bets of 1, 5, 10 or 25 chips (a stepper).\n1057\t- Controls: ✕/H hit, □/S stand, △/D double, R1/P split (only when legal), ○ leave between hands. Every button is also\n1058\t  clickable on screen.\n1059\t- Cards are pixel sprites (rank glyphs and suit sprites ♠ ♥ ♦ ♣ made with `E.sprite`), dealt with tweens and flipped.\n1060\t  Pepper has deadpan lines for a blackjack and a bust.\n1061\t\n1062\t**Roulette.**\n1063\t\n1064\t- A single-zero wheel in real order: 0, 32, 15, 19, 4, 21, 2, 25, 17, 34, 6, 27, 13, 36, 11, 30, 8, 23, 10, 5, 24, 16,\n1065\t  33, 1, 20, 14, 31, 9, 22, 18, 29, 7, 28, 12, 35, 3, 26.\n1066\t- **Betting layout:** a cursor moved with the stick, WASD or the mouse.\n1067\t\n1068\t| Bet | Pays |\n1069\t| --- | --- |\n1070\t| straight number | 35:1 |\n1071\t| red/black, odd/even, 1–18/19–36 | 1:1 |\n1072\t| dozens, columns | 2:1 |\n1073\t\n1074\t- Controls: ✕ place a chip (L1/R1 sizes 1/5/10/25), □ remove, △ spin, ○ leave.\n1075\t- An inset wheel shows the pocket ring turning while the ball spirals in, slows, bounces two pockets and settles. Then\n1076\t  the result is highlighted, payouts made, and a strip shows the last 10 results.\n1077\t- The dev-only toggle `T.rouletteDoubleZero` gives an American wheel.\n1078\t\n1079\tLeaving the casino ends the night and goes to the day-end card.\n1080\t\n1081\t### 4.17 Postcards (photo mode) and album (`42-photo.js`)\n1082\t\n1083\t**Where:** the pause menu's \"Take a Postcard\", or Create / C in walkable locations and on match results. Never in hub\n1084\tsessions or the attract. Gameplay time freezes (`timeScale` 0), while cosmetic motion (water, breathing idles) keeps\n1085\tgoing.\n1086\t\n1087\t**Controls:**\n1088\t\n1089\t| Input | Does |\n1090\t| --- | --- |\n1091\t| left stick / WASD | pan the focus |\n1092\t| right stick / right-drag | orbit at any angle (`game.rotateView`) |\n1093\t| L2/R2 / wheel | zoom .75–2.5 |\n1094\t| ✕ | take the photo |\n1095\t| ○ | exit |\n1096\t| □ | choose the subject: you, or any NPC present |\n1097\t| △ | the panel |\n1098\t| R3 / H | hide the UI |\n1099\t\n1100\tThe △ panel has:\n1101\t\n1102\t- **pose:** Wave, Peace, Hips, Cheer, Stretch, Look Back, Sit, Victory, Salute, Bow;\n1103\t- **expression:** smile, shout, wince, neutral;\n1104\t- **filter:** Clean, Sunny, Sepia, Retro, Night Glow;\n1105\t- **frame:** none, or a postcard border with a \"Greetings from Isla Fortuna\" stamp and the date.\n1106\t\n1107\t**Taking a photo.** The shutter sound and a white flash, then a \"developing\" postcard slides to a corner. It is saved\n1108\tin `state.album` (at most 24; asks before replacing the oldest) as a **spec**, never pixels:\n1109\t`{ loc, day, slot, tod, weather, cam: { x, y, z, yaw, zoom, view }, people: [{ id, suit, acc, pose, expr, x, y, facing\n1110\t}], filter, frame }`.\n1111\t\n1112\t**The album** (Villa, or the menu for the latest save):\n1113\t\n1114\t- A 4×2 grid of live thumbnails: each spec is re-rendered at half size.\n1115\t- Opening one re-renders it full screen, live, so the palms still sway.\n1116\t- □ deletes (with a confirm); △ \"Set as title backdrop\"; R1 exports a PNG download (not in sessions).\n1117\t\n1118\tThe credits slideshow re-renders the album, plus a group photo taken automatically at the party.\n1119\t\n1120\t### 4.18 Story, dialogue, voices, cutscenes (`34-story.js`)\n1121\t\n1122\t- `E.Story` holds `people` for every speaker (portrait = their rig) and the nodes from `05-data-text.js`. Its `on`\n1123\t  events run game actions: `startMatch`, `giveMoney`, `giveItem`, `setPartner`, `openShop`, `photo`, `fade`.\n1124\t  `story.state()` goes in the save.\n1125\t- **The dialog box:** bottom, 2 lines, the name tag in the speaker's color, a portrait with expression\n1126\t  (`portraitOpts`), markup for emphasis (`{c=#ffd36a}…{/c}`, `{wave}`, `{shake}`). The Animalese voice runs from the\n1127\t  per-letter hook (patch 3). Text speed is a setting. Hold ○ or right click to fast-forward; Options on a cutscene asks\n1128\t  \"Skip scene?\".\n1129\t- **Cutscenes** are `game.script` generators: camera tweens, walk-ons (`game.tween` on bodies), emotes\n1130\t  (`story.emote(target, 'heart' | '!' | '?' | 'note' | 'dots')`), fades. The list is in §5.5.\n1131\t\n1132\t### 4.19 Save and load (`30-vacation.js`)\n1133\t\n1134\t**Slots:** `game.saves` (3 slots plus autosave). The title's Load and the Villa journal's Save open `saves.show('load'\n1135\t| 'save')`. The game autosaves at every slot start; Continue loads `saves.latest()`.\n1136\t\n1137\t- `saves.write = () => ({ data: G.state, place: locationName, level: 'Day ' + day })`;\n1138\t- `read = save => G.loadState(save.data)`, with `version: 1` and a `migrate`.\n1139\t\n1140\t**State shape:**\n1141\t\n1142\t```js\n1143\t{ v: 1, seed, day: 1, slot: 0, weather: ['sunny', …], me: 'rin', money: 30000, chips: 0,\n1144\t  wardrobe: { suits: ['seigaiha'], acc: ['ribbon'] }, wearing: { suit: 'seigaiha', acc: ['ribbon'] },\n1145\t  npcWear: { lola: { suit: 'estrella', acc: ['sweatband'] }, … }, bag: { mango_smoothie: 1 },\n1146\t  affinity: { lola: 20, … }, mood: { lola: 'happy', … }, known: { lola: { hot_sauce: 'love' } },\n1147\t  partner: null, teams: [['lola', 'tess'], ['amara', 'mei']], record: { 'lola+tess': [0, 0] },\n1148\t  flags: {}, story: {}, chatted: {}, gifted: {}, album: [], titlePostcard: null,\n1149\t  stats: { matches: 0, wins: 0, points: 0, kills: 0, aces: 0, blocks: 0, poolBest: null, casinoNet: 0, gifts: 0,\n1150\t           photos: 0, earned: 0, spent: 0 } }\n1151\t```\n1152\t\n1153\t**New Vacation+** (after an ending) keeps the wardrobe, album and lifetime stats. It resets the days and affinity (to\n1154\tbase +10) and starts money at S$30,000 plus 10% of your final money.\n1155\t\n1156\t**Unlocks** for Beach Match (suits ever owned; everything after the first ending) live in `E.store('aoa-unlocks')`.\n1157\t\n1158\t### 4.20 Front end: boot, title, menu, How to Play, About (`50-title.js`)\n1159\t\n1160\t**Boot.** Boot steps build the rigs, maps, music and caches behind the engine's boot screen, with messages: \"Raking the\n1161\tsand\", \"Inflating volleyballs\", \"Chilling the smoothies\", \"Counting Sonny's chips\", \"Polishing the golden sunglasses\".\n1162\t\n1163\t**Title.**\n1164\t\n1165\t- A sunset beach backdrop: sea layers, the sun, distant islands, palms, gentle waves.\n1166\t- The six fighters stand on the sand in their signature suits, each with her own idle: Rin stretching, Lola flexing,\n1167\t  Ingrid fanning herself, Amara dancing, Tess juggling a ball, Mei waving. Now and then Sonny jogs across the background\n1168\t  with a giant trophy.\n1169\t- The logo **AHEAD OR ALIVE**: `E.font.title` scale 4, colors `['#fff7d6', '#ffd36a', '#ff9e5e', '#ff5f7a']`, depth 3,\n1170\t  with a small spinning volleyball beside it. Under it **XTREME BEACH VOLLEYBALL** at scale 2, white with a teal shadow.\n1171\t- A blinking \"PRESS ✕\" in the current device's glyph.\n1172\t- A footer with the version label (`E.versionLabel()`) and \"An original parody-tribute game\".\n1173\t- If a postcard is set as the title backdrop, it renders behind the logo instead.\n1174\t\n1175\t**Main menu.** A big list on the left; a turning fighter preview on the right.\n1176\t\n1177\t- **New Vacation**\n1178\t- **Continue** (if a save exists)\n1179\t- **Load**\n1180\t- **Beach Match**\n1181\t- **Album** (if there are postcards)\n1182\t- **How to Play**\n1183\t- **Settings** (`game.menu('settings')`)\n1184\t- **About & Credits**\n1185\t\n1186\t10 s idle starts the attract mode.\n1187\t\n1188\t**How to Play.** 10 pages, one idea each, with a live mini-scene in the panel and the current device's glyphs:\n1189\t\n1190\t1. Moving and the ring\n1191\t2. The touch chain: bump, set, spike\n1192\t3. Aiming and shots\n1193\t4. Serving\n1194\t5. Blocking and diving\n1195\t6. Calls and chemistry\n1196\t7. The vacation: slots, map, money\n1197\t8. Friends and gifts\n1198\t9. Casino and Pool Hop\n1199\t10. Postcards\n1200\t\n1201\t**About & Credits.** Pages turned with L1/R1, left/right or the on-screen arrows; the stick scrolls; large text, one\n1202\tfield per line. Contents in §10:\n1203\t\n1204\t1. Credits\n1205\t2. Source Information\n1206\t3. Testing Feedback\n1207\t4. Engine Feedback\n1208\t5. Prompt Feedback\n1209\t\n1210\t### 4.21 Attract mode (`51-attract.js`)\n1211\t\n1212\t**Trigger.** 10.0 s without input on `title` or `menu`. Input means any key, a pad button, a stick past its dead zone,\n1213\tthe mouse moving more than 4 px, a click, the wheel, or a touch; each resets the timer.\n1214\t\n1215\t**Playlist.** A director kept alive across scenes (`game.script(…, { keep: true })` plus the overlay watcher) plays it,\n1216\tre-seeded each cycle for variety. Demo scenes run on a throwaway demo state, never the player's save.\n1217\t\n1218\t1. **Match, about 50 s.** AI vs AI on Sunset Courts with random fighters, outfits and time of day: `spectacle` AI, the\n1219\t   camera cutting between Broadcast and Serve Cam every 2 points, commentary and highlight replays on.\n1220\t2. **Vacation montage, about 50 s.** 7 beats of 6–8 s, each with a big caption banner:\n1221\t\n1222\t| Caption | Shows |\n1223\t| --- | --- |\n1224\t| FIVE DAYS IN PARADISE | the island map flying from morning to night |\n1225\t| MAKE FRIENDS · GIVE GIFTS | a gift scene with hearts |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"99d4115e-ac85-4844-bf9c-39009e8f9714","uuid":"a610109c-7632-4563-8ba3-f09b06fff2ef","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:36:24.146Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174749__x8de669/work/PLAN.md","content":"- **Sonny's VIP lounge**, for story events.\n\nOn the first night Sonny hands you 20 free chips and explains the games. A prize counter swaps 300 chips for the\n\"Jackpot\" suit.\n\n**Fortuna Sevens (pachislot).**\n\n- 3 reels with 3 visible rows. Bet 1, 2 or 3 chips: 1 = the centre line, 2 = plus the top and bottom lines, 3 = plus\n  both diagonals.\n- ✕ / Space spins. Then ✕ ○ □ (J K L) stop reels 1, 2 and 3. A stop \"slips\" 0–4 symbols on the `casino` rng, so\n  timing matters a little.\n- Strips of 21 stops per reel. Payouts per line bet:\n\n| Line | Pays |\n| --- | --- |\n| 7-7-7 | ×100, with a jackpot fanfare and coin shower |\n| BAR-BAR-BAR | ×30 |\n| Sonny-Sonny-Sonny | ×20 (Sonny is wild) |\n| Volleyball ×3 | ×12 |\n| Palm ×3 | ×8 |\n| Coconut ×3 | ×5 |\n| Cherry, by count on the line | 1 ×2, 2 ×5, 3 ×10 |\n\n- Tune the strips so the RTP is **92% ± 3** at `T.slotsPayMul` 1 (a simulation test checks it).\n- Spinning reels show blur rows, then a stop clunk and a line highlight.\n\n**Blackjack.**\n\n- 6-deck shoe, reshuffled at 75%. The dealer stands on soft 17 (`T.dealerHitsSoft17` toggles it). Blackjack pays 3:2.\n  Double on any first two cards. Split once; split aces get one card each. No insurance, no surrender.\n- Bets of 1, 5, 10 or 25 chips (a stepper).\n- Controls: ✕/H hit, □/S stand, △/D double, R1/P split (only when legal), ○ leave between hands. Every button is also\n  clickable on screen.\n- Cards are pixel sprites (rank glyphs and suit sprites ♠ ♥ ♦ ♣ made with `E.sprite`), dealt with tweens and flipped.\n  Pepper has deadpan lines for a blackjack and a bust.\n\n**Roulette.**\n\n- A single-zero wheel in real order: 0, 32, 15, 19, 4, 21, 2, 25, 17, 34, 6, 27, 13, 36, 11, 30, 8, 23, 10, 5, 24, 16,\n  33, 1, 20, 14, 31, 9, 22, 18, 29, 7, 28, 12, 35, 3, 26.\n- **Betting layout:** a cursor moved with the stick, WASD or the mouse.\n\n| Bet | Pays |\n| --- | --- |\n| straight number | 35:1 |\n| red/black, odd/even, 1–18/19–36 | 1:1 |\n| dozens, columns | 2:1 |\n\n- Controls: ✕ place a chip (L1/R1 sizes 1/5/10/25), □ remove, △ spin, ○ leave.\n- An inset wheel shows the pocket ring turning while the ball spirals in, slows, bounces two pockets and settles. Then\n  the result is highlighted, payouts made, and a strip shows the last 10 results.\n- The dev-only toggle `T.rouletteDoubleZero` gives an American wheel.\n\nLeaving the casino ends the night and goes to the day-end card.\n\n### 4.17 Postcards (photo mode) and album (`42-photo.js`)\n\n**Where:** the pause menu's \"Take a Postcard\", or Create / C in walkable locations and on match results. Never in hub\nsessions or the attract. Gameplay time freezes (`timeScale` 0), while cosmetic motion (water, breathing idles) keeps\ngoing.\n\n**Controls:**\n\n| Input | Does |\n| --- | --- |\n| left stick / WASD | pan the focus |\n| right stick / right-drag | orbit at any angle (`game.rotateView`) |\n| L2/R2 / wheel | zoom .75–2.5 |\n| ✕ | take the photo |\n| ○ | exit |\n| □ | choose the subject: you, or any NPC present |\n| △ | the panel |\n| R3 / H | hide the UI |\n\nThe △ panel has:\n\n- **pose:** Wave, Peace, Hips, Cheer, Stretch, Look Back, Sit, Victory, Salute, Bow;\n- **expression:** smile, shout, wince, neutral;\n- **filter:** Clean, Sunny, Sepia, Retro, Night Glow;\n- **frame:** none, or a postcard border with a \"Greetings from Isla Fortuna\" stamp and the date.\n\n**Taking a photo.** The shutter sound and a white flash, then a \"developing\" postcard slides to a corner. It is saved\nin `state.album` (at most 24; asks before replacing the oldest) as a **spec**, never pixels:\n`{ loc, day, slot, tod, weather, cam: { x, y, z, yaw, zoom, view }, people: [{ id, suit, acc, pose, expr, x, y, facing\n}], filter, frame }`.\n\n**The album** (Villa, or the menu for the latest save):\n\n- A 4×2 grid of live thumbnails: each spec is re-rendered at half size.\n- Opening one re-renders it full screen, live, so the palms still sway.\n- □ deletes (with a confirm); △ \"Set as title backdrop\"; R1 exports a PNG download (not in sessions).\n\nThe credits slideshow re-renders the album, plus a group photo taken automatically at the party.\n\n### 4.18 Story, dialogue, voices, cutscenes (`34-story.js`)\n\n- `E.Story` holds `people` for every speaker (portrait = their rig) and the nodes from `05-data-text.js`. Its `on`\n  events run game actions: `startMatch`, `giveMoney`, `giveItem`, `setPartner`, `openShop`, `photo`, `fade`.\n  `story.state()` goes in the save.\n- **The dialog box:** bottom, 2 lines, the name tag in the speaker's color, a portrait with expression\n  (`portraitOpts`), markup for emphasis (`{c=#ffd36a}…{/c}`, `{wave}`, `{shake}`). The Animalese voice runs from the\n  per-letter hook (patch 3). Text speed is a setting. Hold ○ or right click to fast-forward; Options on a cutscene asks\n  \"Skip scene?\".\n- **Cutscenes** are `game.script` generators: camera tweens, walk-ons (`game.tween` on bodies), emotes\n  (`story.emote(target, 'heart' | '!' | '?' | 'note' | 'dots')`), fades. The list is in §5.5.\n\n### 4.19 Save and load (`30-vacation.js`)\n\n**Slots:** `game.saves` (3 slots plus autosave). The title's Load and the Villa journal's Save open `saves.show('load'\n| 'save')`. The game autosaves at every slot start; Continue loads `saves.latest()`.\n\n- `saves.write = () => ({ data: G.state, place: locationName, level: 'Day ' + day })`;\n- `read = save => G.loadState(save.data)`, with `version: 1` and a `migrate`.\n\n**State shape:**\n\n```js\n{ v: 1, seed, day: 1, slot: 0, weather: ['sunny', …], me: 'rin', money: 30000, chips: 0,\n  wardrobe: { suits: ['seigaiha'], acc: ['ribbon'] }, wearing: { suit: 'seigaiha', acc: ['ribbon'] },\n  npcWear: { lola: { suit: 'estrella', acc: ['sweatband'] }, … }, bag: { mango_smoothie: 1 },\n  affinity: { lola: 20, … }, mood: { lola: 'happy', … }, known: { lola: { hot_sauce: 'love' } },\n  partner: null, teams: [['lola', 'tess'], ['amara', 'mei']], record: { 'lola+tess': [0, 0] },\n  flags: {}, story: {}, chatted: {}, gifted: {}, album: [], titlePostcard: null,\n  stats: { matches: 0, wins: 0, points: 0, kills: 0, aces: 0, blocks: 0, poolBest: null, casinoNet: 0, gifts: 0,\n           photos: 0, earned: 0, spent: 0 } }\n```\n\n**New Vacation+** (after an ending) keeps the wardrobe, album and lifetime stats. It resets the days and affinity (to\nbase +10) and starts money at S$30,000 plus 10% of your final money.\n\n**Unlocks** for Beach Match (suits ever owned; everything after the first ending) live in `E.store('aoa-unlocks')`.\n\n### 4.20 Front end: boot, title, menu, How to Play, About (`50-title.js`)\n\n**Boot.** Boot steps build the rigs, maps, music and caches behind the engine's boot screen, with messages: \"Raking the\nsand\", \"Inflating volleyballs\", \"Chilling the smoothies\", \"Counting Sonny's chips\", \"Polishing the golden sunglasses\".\n\n**Title.**\n\n- A sunset beach backdrop: sea layers, the sun, distant islands, palms, gentle waves.\n- The six fighters stand on the sand in their signature suits, each with her own idle: Rin stretching, Lola flexing,\n  Ingrid fanning herself, Amara dancing, Tess juggling a ball, Mei waving. Now and then Sonny jogs across the background\n  with a giant trophy.\n- The logo **AHEAD OR ALIVE**: `E.font.title` scale 4, colors `['#fff7d6', '#ffd36a', '#ff9e5e', '#ff5f7a']`, depth 3,\n  with a small spinning volleyball beside it. Under it **XTREME BEACH VOLLEYBALL** at scale 2, white with a teal shadow.\n- A blinking \"PRESS ✕\" in the current device's glyph.\n- A footer with the version label (`E.versionLabel()`) and \"An original parody-tribute game\".\n- If a postcard is set as the title backdrop, it renders behind the logo instead.\n\n**Main menu.** A big list on the left; a turning fighter preview on the right.\n\n- **New Vacation**\n- **Continue** (if a save exists)\n- **Load**\n- **Beach Match**\n- **Album** (if there are postcards)\n- **How to Play**\n- **Settings** (`game.menu('settings')`)\n- **About & Credits**\n\n10 s idle starts the attract mode.\n\n**How to Play.** 10 pages, one idea each, with a live mini-scene in the panel and the current device's glyphs:\n\n1. Moving and the ring\n2. The touch chain: bump, set, spike\n3. Aiming and shots\n4. Serving\n5. Blocking and diving\n6. Calls and chemistry\n7. The vacation: slots, map, money\n8. Friends and gifts\n9. Casino and Pool Hop\n10. Postcards\n\n**About & Credits.** Pages turned with L1/R1, left/right or the on-screen arrows; the stick scrolls; large text, one\nfield per line. Contents in §10:\n\n1. Credits\n2. Source Information\n3. Testing Feedback\n4. Engine Feedback\n5. Prompt Feedback\n\n### 4.21 Attract mode (`51-attract.js`)\n\n**Trigger.** 10.0 s without input on `title` or `menu`. Input means any key, a pad button, a stick past its dead zone,\nthe mouse moving more than 4 px, a click, the wheel, or a touch; each resets the timer.\n\n**Playlist.** A director kept alive across scenes (`game.script(…, { keep: true })` plus the overlay watcher) plays it,\nre-seeded each cycle for variety. Demo scenes run on a throwaway demo state, never the player's save.\n\n1. **Match, about 50 s.** AI vs AI on Sunset Courts with random fighters, outfits and time of day: `spectacle` AI, the\n   camera cutting between Broadcast and Serve Cam every 2 points, commentary and highlight replays on.\n2. **Vacation montage, about 50 s.** 7 beats of 6–8 s, each with a big caption banner:\n\n| Caption | Shows |\n| --- | --- |\n| FIVE DAYS IN PARADISE | the island map flying from morning to night |\n| MAKE FRIENDS · GIVE GIFTS | a gift scene with hearts |","numLines":200,"startLine":1026,"totalLines":2180}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Kako114wVqhXXi2TKobWZA","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
