{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P3ftumFVbbmj33LSQLSePu","type":"tool_result","content":"1225\t| MAKE FRIENDS · GIVE GIFTS | a gift scene with hearts |\n1226\t| COLLECT 21 SWIMSUITS | the shop preview cycling suits |\n1227\t| POOL HOP | a perfect-bot run |\n1228\t| CASINO NIGHTS | slots hitting 7-7-7, then a blackjack |\n1229\t| SNAP POSTCARDS | a photo-mode orbit |\n1230\t| BEAT THE HOUSE | a slice of the final against Sonny & Pepper, with the Golden Glare |\n1231\t\n1232\t3. **Title card, 5 s**, with \"PRESS ✕\". Then repeat.\n1233\t\n1234\t**Rules.**\n1235\t\n1236\t- The AI may cheat freely: perfect timing, scripted outcomes, instant travel.\n1237\t- **Any input** returns to `title` with the input consumed, so it doesn't also press a menu item, and the title music\n1238\t  resumes.\n1239\t- A \"DEMO\" tag shows top left. On touch-only devices the bottom banner reads \"Controller or keyboard required\".\n1240\t- Sound starts only after the browser's first gesture (engine rule), so before that the attract runs silent.\n1241\t\n1242\t### 4.22 Dev mode (`53-dev.js`)\n1243\t\n1244\t**Reach.** The pause menu's **Dev Mode**, in every pausable scene. Once opened, F1 (or L3+R3 on a pad) reopens it for\n1245\tthe rest of the session. Never in hub sessions.\n1246\t\n1247\t**While it is open:**\n1248\t\n1249\t- gameplay time is frozen (`game.timeScale = 0`; the overlay updates on real time);\n1250\t- the panel is a 10-foot canvas overlay built with the UI kit;\n1251\t- tabs (L1/R1, Q/E or a click): **Tools · Match · Vacation · Minigames · Presentation · Tuning**;\n1252\t- **Back to game** restores `timeScale`.\n1253\t\n1254\t**4.22.1 Tools** (every button calls `game.debug.tools.*`).\n1255\t\n1256\t| Tab | Tools |\n1257\t| --- | --- |\n1258\t| Tools | jump to any scene, location or minigame; set the day (1–5) and slot; jump to the Semifinal, the Final, the party or ending, the credits; restart the scene; reset the save (with a confirm) |\n1259\t| Match | start a match against any pair; force a point left or right; set the score; end the match (win/lose); CPU controls your player (watch); Perfect Player (all your presses PERFECT); the debug overlay (trajectory line, landing point, every player's P* ring, AI assignment and state labels, a judge-window bar); slow motion ×.25 / ×.5 / ×1; frame step (one step per press while frozen); switch camera |\n1260\t| Vacation | money +10k / +100k / set to 0; chips +100; unlock all items; fill the gift bag ×3; set affinity per fighter (a slider 0–100); set mood; make or clear partner; reveal all likes |\n1261\t| Minigames | Pool Hop autopilot; slots: force 7-7-7 next; blackjack: deal a blackjack; roulette: force a number |\n1262\t| Presentation | time-of-day override (0–24 h); weather (sunny/cloudy/rain); show FPS (engine setting); **Voice Lab** (pick a speaker and a preset phrase, play it); music jukebox; SFX board; rig sheet viewer (fighter × suit × pose × view) |\n1263\t\n1264\t**4.22.2 Live sliders** (the Tuning tab).\n1265\t\n1266\t- Changes apply at once: every system reads `G.T` every step.\n1267\t- Each slider shows its default as a tick. △ or R on a slider resets it.\n1268\t- **Reset all to defaults** asks to confirm.\n1269\t- Values persist in `E.store('aoa-dev-tuning')`, and **Copy JSON** copies them to the clipboard.\n1270\t\n1271\t| Group | Key | Default | Range | Step |\n1272\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1273\t| Ball | `ballGravity` | 330 | 180–500 | 5 |\n1274\t| Ball | `ballDrag` | .12 | 0–.6 | .01 |\n1275\t| Ball | `passT` | 1.05 | .7–1.6 | .05 |\n1276\t| Ball | `setT` | 1.1 | .7–1.6 | .05 |\n1277\t| Ball | `serveT` | 1.3 | .9–1.8 | .05 |\n1278\t| Ball | `jumpServeT` | .85 | .6–1.3 | .05 |\n1279\t| Ball | `spikeSpeed` | 330 | 220–480 | 5 |\n1280\t| Ball | `shotT` | .95 | .6–1.4 | .05 |\n1281\t| Ball | `netCordOver` | .45 | 0–1 | .05 |\n1282\t| Timing | `perfectWin` (s) | .05 | .02–.12 | .005 |\n1283\t| Timing | `greatWin` (s) | .10 | .05–.2 | .005 |\n1284\t| Timing | `okWin` (s) | .16 | .08–.3 | .01 |\n1285\t| Timing | `reach` | 14 | 8–24 | 1 |\n1286\t| Timing | `diveReach` | 16 | 6–30 | 1 |\n1287\t| Timing | `blockRise` (s) | .28 | .15–.45 | .01 |\n1288\t| Players | `runSpeed` | 96 | 60–140 | 2 |\n1289\t| Players | `autoMove` | .85 | 0–1 | .05 |\n1290\t| AI | `aiSkillMul` (× the day's base) | 1 | .3–1.6 | .02 |\n1291\t| AI | `aiReaction` (s) | .25 | 0–.6 | .01 |\n1292\t| AI | `aiSpeedMul` | 1 | .6–1.4 | .02 |\n1293\t| AI | `chemistry` | .3 | 0–.6 | .02 |\n1294\t| Match | `pointsToWin` (vacation) | 7 | 3–21 | 1 |\n1295\t| Economy | `prizeMul` | 1 | 0–3 | .05 |\n1296\t| Economy | `priceMul` | 1 | .25–3 | .05 |\n1297\t| Economy | `startMoney` | 30000 | 0–200000 | 5000 |\n1298\t| Social | `affinityGainMul` | 1 | 0–3 | .05 |\n1299\t| Social | `affinityDecay` | 2 | 0–10 | 1 |\n1300\t| Social | `inviteThreshold` | 40 | 0–100 | 1 |\n1301\t| Social | `giftThreshold` | 0 | −3–3 | 1 |\n1302\t| Pool Hop | `poolBpm` | 112 | 80–150 | 2 |\n1303\t| Pool Hop | `poolWindowMul` | 1 | .5–2 | .05 |\n1304\t| Pool Hop | `poolTime` (s) | 40 | 20–80 | 1 |\n1305\t| Casino | `slotsPayMul` | 1 | .5–1.5 | .01 |\n1306\t| Casino | `dealerHitsSoft17` | off | toggle | — |\n1307\t| Casino | `rouletteDoubleZero` | off | toggle | — |\n1308\t| Presentation | `textSpeed` (letters/s) | 45 | 10–200 | 5 |\n1309\t| Presentation | `cameraZoomMul` | 1 | .7–1.3 | .02 |\n1310\t\n1311\t### 4.23 AI Hub sessions (`25-netplay.js`)\n1312\t\n1313\t**Head tags** in the deliverable. Keep the goal ≤ 60 characters and the howto ≤ 80.\n1314\t\n1315\t```html\n1316\t<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n1317\t<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n1318\t<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n1319\t<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"5\">\n1320\t<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Win the beach volleyball match: first to 7, by 2\">\n1321\t<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Stick/WASD move · Cross/Space hit on time · Circle/Shift dive · Square/E shot\">\n1322\t<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Game\">\n1323\t<meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1-4\">\n1324\t```\n1325\t\n1326\t**Flow when `AIHub.active` is true.**\n1327\t\n1328\t1. **Build the game for a session:** `menu: false` (no pause), `autoPause: false`, `corner: false`,\n1329\t   `fullscreen: false`, no saves, touch `'never'`, no title and no attract.\n1330\t2. **Connect.** Boot straight into the `hub` scene, which calls\n1331\t   `const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true })`. If it returns `null`, go to\n1332\t   `title` and run normally.\n1333\t3. **Teams.** Left = seat indexes 0 and 2; Right = 1 and 3. Empty slots are CPUs (Normal).\n1334\t   - Fighters: shuffle the six with `AIHub.rng('cast')`; everyone wears signature suits.\n1335\t   - Court time: `AIHub.rng('court')`.\n1336\t   - Each human's fighter gets a ground ring and a name tag in her seat color (`#e8443a`, `#3b82f6`, `#22c55e`,\n1337\t     `#f5b700`). Names are drawn with `E.font` on the canvas, never inserted as HTML.\n1338\t4. **Our own card**, until `start`:\n1339\t   - Shows: the court at sunset with the four fighters lined up (CPUs tagged), the logo, the goal line, this player's\n1340\t     controls in her device's glyphs, every player's name in her color with a READY tick (from `card.ready`), and the\n1341\t     countdown from `card.left` (\"Paused: more time\" while `paused`).\n1342\t   - Two buttons: **READY** (✕ / Enter / click) → `AIHub.answer('ready')`; **MORE TIME** (△ / T / click) →\n1343\t     `AIHub.answer('more')`, which toggles.\n1344\t   - Nothing else to choose. Call `AIHub.ready()` as soon as the card is built, with no key press.\n1345\t   - The server copy (`AIHub.server`) builds the world, calls `ready()`, and draws a minimal \"Hosting\" screen.\n1346\t5. **Start.** On `start`, the intro walk-on plays. Play begins when `AIHub.time() >= 0`, with a 3-2-1 countdown from the\n1347\t   negative clock.\n1348\t6. **Messages.** All are small JSON with short keys.\n1349\t\n1350\t| Msg | Direction | Rate | Reliable | Content |\n1351\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1352\t| `m` | client → host | 12/s while playing (also as a heartbeat) | no | `{ t: 'm', at, x, y, f, a }`: own fighter's position, facing, action |\n1353\t| `c` | client → host | per judged press | yes | `{ t: 'c', at, k, q, aim: [x, y], sh }`: a touch claim; `at` = hub ms of contact, `k` kind, `q` quality, `sh` shot or play |\n1354\t| `v` | client → host | when serving | yes | `{ t: 'v', at, q, aim, jump }`: a serve claim |\n1355\t| `s` | host → all | 12/s | no | `{ t: 's', at, p: [[id, x, y, f, a, u], …], sc: [l, r], ph, sv, tc }` |\n1356\t| `b` | host → all | each launch | yes | `{ t: 'b', t0, p, v, k, g, ay, wob, by, kind }` |\n1357\t| `e` | host → all | per point, fault or phase | yes | `{ t: 'e', ev, side, why, sc, next }` |\n1358\t| final `s` | host → all | once | yes | the last snapshot with `over: 1` |\n1359\t\n1360\t   The budget: the host sends ≤ 16 messages/s and each client ≤ 14, under the hub's 20/s. Unreliable messages stay\n1361\t   under 1,200 bytes.\n1362\t7. **Authority.**\n1363\t   - The host runs the rules and the AI, and accepts claims.\n1364\t   - Each client moves its own fighter at once and sends it at 12 Hz. The host clamps reports to max speed and the court.\n1365\t   - Each client judges its own touches against the shared ball. Every copy computes the same trajectory from `b` on the\n1366\t     shared clock, so the timing is fair whatever the latency.\n1367\t   - The host validates a claim: contact time within the planned window ±.12 s; the claimant within reach + 12 of the\n1368\t     ball at that time; the touch still open; the first valid claim wins. It then broadcasts the new launch with\n1369\t     `t0 = claim.at`, so every copy continues from the same instant; clients ease the visual jump over .12 s.\n1370\t   - Before awarding a point, the host waits for remote claims until `tLand + .25 s`.\n1371\t8. **Others' fighters.** Clients interpolate other fighters from snapshots with a 100 ms buffer. A client's own fighter\n1372\t   is never overwritten.\n1373\t9. **Reporting** (only the host calls `finish()`):\n1374\t   - Match over: `AIHub.finish({ standings: [[winner ids…], [loser ids…]], scores: { id: teamScore }, stats: { id: {\n1375\t     Points, Kills } }, awards: [{ id, title: 'MVP', detail }] })`.\n1376\t   - With one human against CPUs: `standings: [[me]]` and `won: true | false`.\n1377\t   - On `time-up`: finish at once with the current score, the team ahead first. If tied, everyone goes in one array.\n1378\t10. **Leaving.** On `leave`, that seat becomes a CPU and its fighter plays on. If the host leaves, `end` arrives with\n1379\t    `host-left`: show \"Round cancelled\" and stop.\n1380\t11. **End.** On `end`: stop input and sound (music off, mute the buses), freeze the simulation, and draw the final\n1381\t    standings with names. Send nothing more.\n1382\t12. **Session rules.** No pause, quit or title; no dialogs, alerts or new windows; nothing relies on storage; no network\n1383\t    but `AIHub.send`. Options is ignored while Create is held (patch 6).\n1384\t13. **Outside a session** nothing changes: the client is inert when `!AIHub.active`."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"99d4115e-ac85-4844-bf9c-39009e8f9714","uuid":"59736c23-d67b-472c-8d9d-69eed3199e6c","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:36:31.704Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174749__x8de669/work/PLAN.md","content":"| MAKE FRIENDS · GIVE GIFTS | a gift scene with hearts |\n| COLLECT 21 SWIMSUITS | the shop preview cycling suits |\n| POOL HOP | a perfect-bot run |\n| CASINO NIGHTS | slots hitting 7-7-7, then a blackjack |\n| SNAP POSTCARDS | a photo-mode orbit |\n| BEAT THE HOUSE | a slice of the final against Sonny & Pepper, with the Golden Glare |\n\n3. **Title card, 5 s**, with \"PRESS ✕\". Then repeat.\n\n**Rules.**\n\n- The AI may cheat freely: perfect timing, scripted outcomes, instant travel.\n- **Any input** returns to `title` with the input consumed, so it doesn't also press a menu item, and the title music\n  resumes.\n- A \"DEMO\" tag shows top left. On touch-only devices the bottom banner reads \"Controller or keyboard required\".\n- Sound starts only after the browser's first gesture (engine rule), so before that the attract runs silent.\n\n### 4.22 Dev mode (`53-dev.js`)\n\n**Reach.** The pause menu's **Dev Mode**, in every pausable scene. Once opened, F1 (or L3+R3 on a pad) reopens it for\nthe rest of the session. Never in hub sessions.\n\n**While it is open:**\n\n- gameplay time is frozen (`game.timeScale = 0`; the overlay updates on real time);\n- the panel is a 10-foot canvas overlay built with the UI kit;\n- tabs (L1/R1, Q/E or a click): **Tools · Match · Vacation · Minigames · Presentation · Tuning**;\n- **Back to game** restores `timeScale`.\n\n**4.22.1 Tools** (every button calls `game.debug.tools.*`).\n\n| Tab | Tools |\n| --- | --- |\n| Tools | jump to any scene, location or minigame; set the day (1–5) and slot; jump to the Semifinal, the Final, the party or ending, the credits; restart the scene; reset the save (with a confirm) |\n| Match | start a match against any pair; force a point left or right; set the score; end the match (win/lose); CPU controls your player (watch); Perfect Player (all your presses PERFECT); the debug overlay (trajectory line, landing point, every player's P* ring, AI assignment and state labels, a judge-window bar); slow motion ×.25 / ×.5 / ×1; frame step (one step per press while frozen); switch camera |\n| Vacation | money +10k / +100k / set to 0; chips +100; unlock all items; fill the gift bag ×3; set affinity per fighter (a slider 0–100); set mood; make or clear partner; reveal all likes |\n| Minigames | Pool Hop autopilot; slots: force 7-7-7 next; blackjack: deal a blackjack; roulette: force a number |\n| Presentation | time-of-day override (0–24 h); weather (sunny/cloudy/rain); show FPS (engine setting); **Voice Lab** (pick a speaker and a preset phrase, play it); music jukebox; SFX board; rig sheet viewer (fighter × suit × pose × view) |\n\n**4.22.2 Live sliders** (the Tuning tab).\n\n- Changes apply at once: every system reads `G.T` every step.\n- Each slider shows its default as a tick. △ or R on a slider resets it.\n- **Reset all to defaults** asks to confirm.\n- Values persist in `E.store('aoa-dev-tuning')`, and **Copy JSON** copies them to the clipboard.\n\n| Group | Key | Default | Range | Step |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Ball | `ballGravity` | 330 | 180–500 | 5 |\n| Ball | `ballDrag` | .12 | 0–.6 | .01 |\n| Ball | `passT` | 1.05 | .7–1.6 | .05 |\n| Ball | `setT` | 1.1 | .7–1.6 | .05 |\n| Ball | `serveT` | 1.3 | .9–1.8 | .05 |\n| Ball | `jumpServeT` | .85 | .6–1.3 | .05 |\n| Ball | `spikeSpeed` | 330 | 220–480 | 5 |\n| Ball | `shotT` | .95 | .6–1.4 | .05 |\n| Ball | `netCordOver` | .45 | 0–1 | .05 |\n| Timing | `perfectWin` (s) | .05 | .02–.12 | .005 |\n| Timing | `greatWin` (s) | .10 | .05–.2 | .005 |\n| Timing | `okWin` (s) | .16 | .08–.3 | .01 |\n| Timing | `reach` | 14 | 8–24 | 1 |\n| Timing | `diveReach` | 16 | 6–30 | 1 |\n| Timing | `blockRise` (s) | .28 | .15–.45 | .01 |\n| Players | `runSpeed` | 96 | 60–140 | 2 |\n| Players | `autoMove` | .85 | 0–1 | .05 |\n| AI | `aiSkillMul` (× the day's base) | 1 | .3–1.6 | .02 |\n| AI | `aiReaction` (s) | .25 | 0–.6 | .01 |\n| AI | `aiSpeedMul` | 1 | .6–1.4 | .02 |\n| AI | `chemistry` | .3 | 0–.6 | .02 |\n| Match | `pointsToWin` (vacation) | 7 | 3–21 | 1 |\n| Economy | `prizeMul` | 1 | 0–3 | .05 |\n| Economy | `priceMul` | 1 | .25–3 | .05 |\n| Economy | `startMoney` | 30000 | 0–200000 | 5000 |\n| Social | `affinityGainMul` | 1 | 0–3 | .05 |\n| Social | `affinityDecay` | 2 | 0–10 | 1 |\n| Social | `inviteThreshold` | 40 | 0–100 | 1 |\n| Social | `giftThreshold` | 0 | −3–3 | 1 |\n| Pool Hop | `poolBpm` | 112 | 80–150 | 2 |\n| Pool Hop | `poolWindowMul` | 1 | .5–2 | .05 |\n| Pool Hop | `poolTime` (s) | 40 | 20–80 | 1 |\n| Casino | `slotsPayMul` | 1 | .5–1.5 | .01 |\n| Casino | `dealerHitsSoft17` | off | toggle | — |\n| Casino | `rouletteDoubleZero` | off | toggle | — |\n| Presentation | `textSpeed` (letters/s) | 45 | 10–200 | 5 |\n| Presentation | `cameraZoomMul` | 1 | .7–1.3 | .02 |\n\n### 4.23 AI Hub sessions (`25-netplay.js`)\n\n**Head tags** in the deliverable. Keep the goal ≤ 60 characters and the howto ≤ 80.\n\n```html\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"5\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Win the beach volleyball match: first to 7, by 2\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Stick/WASD move · Cross/Space hit on time · Circle/Shift dive · Square/E shot\">\n<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Game\">\n<meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1-4\">\n```\n\n**Flow when `AIHub.active` is true.**\n\n1. **Build the game for a session:** `menu: false` (no pause), `autoPause: false`, `corner: false`,\n   `fullscreen: false`, no saves, touch `'never'`, no title and no attract.\n2. **Connect.** Boot straight into the `hub` scene, which calls\n   `const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true })`. If it returns `null`, go to\n   `title` and run normally.\n3. **Teams.** Left = seat indexes 0 and 2; Right = 1 and 3. Empty slots are CPUs (Normal).\n   - Fighters: shuffle the six with `AIHub.rng('cast')`; everyone wears signature suits.\n   - Court time: `AIHub.rng('court')`.\n   - Each human's fighter gets a ground ring and a name tag in her seat color (`#e8443a`, `#3b82f6`, `#22c55e`,\n     `#f5b700`). Names are drawn with `E.font` on the canvas, never inserted as HTML.\n4. **Our own card**, until `start`:\n   - Shows: the court at sunset with the four fighters lined up (CPUs tagged), the logo, the goal line, this player's\n     controls in her device's glyphs, every player's name in her color with a READY tick (from `card.ready`), and the\n     countdown from `card.left` (\"Paused: more time\" while `paused`).\n   - Two buttons: **READY** (✕ / Enter / click) → `AIHub.answer('ready')`; **MORE TIME** (△ / T / click) →\n     `AIHub.answer('more')`, which toggles.\n   - Nothing else to choose. Call `AIHub.ready()` as soon as the card is built, with no key press.\n   - The server copy (`AIHub.server`) builds the world, calls `ready()`, and draws a minimal \"Hosting\" screen.\n5. **Start.** On `start`, the intro walk-on plays. Play begins when `AIHub.time() >= 0`, with a 3-2-1 countdown from the\n   negative clock.\n6. **Messages.** All are small JSON with short keys.\n\n| Msg | Direction | Rate | Reliable | Content |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `m` | client → host | 12/s while playing (also as a heartbeat) | no | `{ t: 'm', at, x, y, f, a }`: own fighter's position, facing, action |\n| `c` | client → host | per judged press | yes | `{ t: 'c', at, k, q, aim: [x, y], sh }`: a touch claim; `at` = hub ms of contact, `k` kind, `q` quality, `sh` shot or play |\n| `v` | client → host | when serving | yes | `{ t: 'v', at, q, aim, jump }`: a serve claim |\n| `s` | host → all | 12/s | no | `{ t: 's', at, p: [[id, x, y, f, a, u], …], sc: [l, r], ph, sv, tc }` |\n| `b` | host → all | each launch | yes | `{ t: 'b', t0, p, v, k, g, ay, wob, by, kind }` |\n| `e` | host → all | per point, fault or phase | yes | `{ t: 'e', ev, side, why, sc, next }` |\n| final `s` | host → all | once | yes | the last snapshot with `over: 1` |\n\n   The budget: the host sends ≤ 16 messages/s and each client ≤ 14, under the hub's 20/s. Unreliable messages stay\n   under 1,200 bytes.\n7. **Authority.**\n   - The host runs the rules and the AI, and accepts claims.\n   - Each client moves its own fighter at once and sends it at 12 Hz. The host clamps reports to max speed and the court.\n   - Each client judges its own touches against the shared ball. Every copy computes the same trajectory from `b` on the\n     shared clock, so the timing is fair whatever the latency.\n   - The host validates a claim: contact time within the planned window ±.12 s; the claimant within reach + 12 of the\n     ball at that time; the touch still open; the first valid claim wins. It then broadcasts the new launch with\n     `t0 = claim.at`, so every copy continues from the same instant; clients ease the visual jump over .12 s.\n   - Before awarding a point, the host waits for remote claims until `tLand + .25 s`.\n8. **Others' fighters.** Clients interpolate other fighters from snapshots with a 100 ms buffer. A client's own fighter\n   is never overwritten.\n9. **Reporting** (only the host calls `finish()`):\n   - Match over: `AIHub.finish({ standings: [[winner ids…], [loser ids…]], scores: { id: teamScore }, stats: { id: {\n     Points, Kills } }, awards: [{ id, title: 'MVP', detail }] })`.\n   - With one human against CPUs: `standings: [[me]]` and `won: true | false`.\n   - On `time-up`: finish at once with the current score, the team ahead first. If tied, everyone goes in one array.\n10. **Leaving.** On `leave`, that seat becomes a CPU and its fighter plays on. If the host leaves, `end` arrives with\n    `host-left`: show \"Round cancelled\" and stop.\n11. **End.** On `end`: stop input and sound (music off, mute the buses), freeze the simulation, and draw the final\n    standings with names. Send nothing more.\n12. **Session rules.** No pause, quit or title; no dialogs, alerts or new windows; nothing relies on storage; no network\n    but `AIHub.send`. Options is ignored while Create is held (patch 6).\n13. **Outside a session** nothing changes: the client is inert when `!AIHub.active`.","numLines":160,"startLine":1225,"totalLines":2180}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01P3ftumFVbbmj33LSQLSePu","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
